[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Fix $t,q\in (0,\infty)$. There exist constants $N_0(t, q) \in \bbN$ and $C(t, q) \in (0, \infty)$ depending on $(t,q)$ such that for all $N\geq N_0(t, q)$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \bbE\Big[\bbW_1^2(P_t^1(\bfJ),\gamma_q)\Big]\geq \frac{C(t,q)}{N}.
    \end{align*}

