[Theorem 64 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $0\le T\le I_m$, and let $F$ be a $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function analytic in $\mathbb C_r$. The kernel
\[
  K_{T,1}(z,w)=\frac{F(z)+F(w)^*-F(z)TF(w)^*}{z+\overline{w}}
\]
is positive definite in $\mathbb C_r$ if and only if $\det(F(z)+I_m)\not=0$, $z\in\mathbb C_r$ and
\begin{equation}

(F(z)+I_m)^{-1}\begin{pmatrix} F(z)\sqrt{I_m+T}&I_m\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation}
is a $\mathbb C^{m\times 2m}$-valued bounded function.

