[Thm thm-P1 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let $d=3$ and $\lambda\in \Sigma_\theta$.
Let $(u, \phi )$ be a weak solution of (equation eq-0 of the paper), where
$F\in C_{0, \sigma}^\infty(\Omega)$ and $\Omega$ is a bounded Lipschitz domain.
Let  $B(x, 2r)\subset \Omega$.
Then
\begin{equation}
\left(
\fint_{B(x, r)} |\phi -\fint_{B(x, r)}  \phi  |^q \right)^{1/q}
\le C  M_2(|\nabla u|)(\delta(x) )
\end{equation}
for any $2< q< \infty$, 
where $C$ depends only on  $\Omega$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

