[Proposition H2sn of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] The term \(H_s^2(n)\) is equal to 
\[
\frac{2 \sqrt{n}}{4 \Gamma(\frac{s+1}{2})} \sum_{f=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{f^{2s+1}} \sum_{l=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{l^{s+1}} \sum_{\xi \in \mathbb{Z}} \text{Kl}_{l,f}(\xi,n) J_{l,f}(\xi,n)
\]
where 
\begin{equation}
    J_{l,f}(\xi,n) = \int_{-1}^{1} F_s(y) \Phi_2 \left( \frac{\sqrt{\pi} lf^2}{2\sqrt{n(1-y^2)}}\right) e\left(\frac{-\xi \sqrt{n}y}{2lf^2} \right) dy 
\end{equation}
with 
\begin{equation}
    \Phi_2(x) = \Gamma\left( \frac{s+1}{2}, x^2 \right) 
\end{equation}
and \(\text{Kl}_{l,f}(\xi,n)\) defined as in (H1sn of the paper) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

