[Theorem t4.2 of arXiv:2603.14447, '\Large \bf Backward doubly stochastic differential equations with and without reflection u'] \sl
	Assume that the conditions \(\textbf{(A2)}\), \(\textbf{(F2')}\), \(\textbf{(G1)}\), and \(\textbf{(G2)}\) hold with \(\lambda(t) = 0\) for all \(t \in [0, T]\).
	Then  BDSDE (equation 1 of the paper) has a maximal bounded solution $(Y,Z)\in S_\mathbb{F}^{\infty}([0,T];\mathbb{R})\times L_\mathbb{F}^2([0,T];\mathbb{R}^d)$, and for  any $t\in[0,T]$, $U_0\leqslant U_t\leqslant Y_t\leqslant V_t\leqslant V_0$, $ \mathbb{P} $-a.s., where
