body:
[Lemma Expected length of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:finite_exp_leng}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 1$, and let $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ be a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

    Then for any $x \in G$ we have $\mathbf{E}_{\beta}\left[\mathrm{length}(x)\right] < \infty$ if and only if $\alpha > 1 + 1/d$, in which case there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that $\mathbf{E}_{\beta}\left[\mathrm{length}(x)\right] \leq c \beta$.

