[Lemma cup_expectation of arXiv:2412.07258, 'Permuton limit of a generalization of the Mallows and $k$-card-minimum models'] Let $\sigma_n \in S_n$ be a $g$-random permutation. Then for any $j \in [n]$ the sequence of random variables $V_{\sigma_n}\big(\frac{1}{n},\frac{j}{n}\big), V_{\sigma_n}\big(\frac{2}{n},\frac{j}{n}\big), \dots, V_{\sigma_n}\big(\frac{n}{n},\frac{j}{n}\big) $ (cf.\ Definition (def_permutation_permuton of the paper)) forms a Markov chain. Specifically, for any $i,j \in [n]$ we have
   \begin{align}
  \mathbb{E}\Big(V_{\sigma_n}\Big(\frac{i}{n}, \frac{j}{n}\Big) - V_{\sigma_n}\Big(\frac{i-1}{n},\frac{j}{n}\Big)\: \big| \: \mathcal{F}_{i-1}^{n}\Big) = \frac{1}{n} \cdot \frac{g\Big(V_{\sigma_n}(\frac{i-1}{n}, \frac{j}{n})\Big)}{g(\frac{i-1}{n})}.
   \end{align}

