[Prop of arXiv:2607.08187, 'Asymptotic behaviours of critical branching random walk in $\mathbb{R}^d$'] $(1)$ $V_{(\gamma,\theta)}(\mathbf{y})$ is continuous in $\mathbf{y} \in \overline{D}_1 \cap \mathbb{Q}^d$. Moreover, the following limit exists:
	\begin{align}
		V_{(\gamma,\theta)}(\mathbf{y}):=\lim_{\mathbf{z}\to \mathbf{y}, \mathbf{z} \in \overline{D}_1 \cap \mathbb{Q}^d} V_{(\gamma,\theta)}(\mathbf{z}), \quad \mathbf{y} \in \overline{D}_1.
	\end{align}
	$(2)$ The limit (equation limi-of-U of the paper) holds for any $\mathbf{y} \in \overline{D}_1$.

