[Lemma 169 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under the conditions of Proposition~\ref{Proposition_hex_hole_offcrit}, $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}$ has exactly two bands and $q^-(z)$ factorizes as:
 \begin{equation}

 q^-(z)=p(z) \sqrt{(z-\alpha_1)(z-\beta_1)(z-\alpha_2)(z-\beta_2)} ,
 \end{equation}
 where $(\alpha_1,\beta_1)$ and $(\alpha_2,\beta_2)$ are two bands, and $p(z)$ is a polynomial of degree $1$ with a zero inside $[\hat b'_1,\hat a'_2]$.

