[Prop Prop local asymp expect CR 1 8 of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] There is an explicit constant $\mathbf{C}_{\rm{SLE}4}^{\rm loop}$ such that as 
$\max(\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2)\to 0$, we have that
\begin{multline*}
\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^v)
=
\varepsilon_{1}^{1/8}
\varepsilon_{2}^{1/8}
(\mathbf{C}_{\rm{SLE}4}^{\rm loop})^2
\,
\mathbb{E}
\big[
\CR(z_1,\widehat{D}_{r_0}(z_1))^{-1/8}
\CR(z_2,\widehat{D}_{r_0}(z_2))^{-1/8}
\1_{E_{r_0}}
\big]
(1+o(1))
.
\end{multline*}
Above, $\widehat{D}_{r_0}(z_1)$ and
$\widehat{D}_{r_0}(z_2)$
are random simply connected domains around
$z_1$, respectively $z_2$,
corresponding to the connected component of
$z_1$, respectively $z_2$, in
$
D\setminus
\overline{
\bigcup_{\mathcal{C}\in \mathfrak{C}_{r_0}}\mathcal{C}
}
.
$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma LEM: mu-mgf of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] There exist constants $c_1, c_2>0$ such that for any $0<\lambda\le c_2$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0} }\Big[e^{\lambda\int_{-L^2}^{L^2}Q^{\eta_L}_{x_0}|h^\perp|^2\,\mathrm{d}x} \Big] &\le\frac{1}{1-c_1 \lambda}, 

\end{align}

\noindent
uniformly in $x_0\in \mathbb{T}_{L^2}$, $\theta\in [0,2\pi]$, and $L \ge 1$, where $c_2$ ensures that the condition $0<c_1 \lambda<1$ holds.

