[Proposition thm:jdt-forest-evolution-weak of arXiv:2607.24018, 'Jeu de taquin forests \\ and the inverse infinite RSK correspondence'] Let $T$ be an IYT.
	There exists a canonical injection
	\begin{equation}  
	    \iota\colon \big\{\text{peripheral trees in }\Phi(T)\big\} 
	\to \big\{\text{all trees in }\Phi(J(T))\big\}
	\end{equation}
	uniquely characterized by the following property: for each 
	peripheral tree $\tau$ in $\Phi(T)$, $\tau$ is 
	a subtree of its image $\iota(\tau)$ under the natural 
	inclusion of graphs.

[Corollary q-bound of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $Q_L(n) = \frac{\br{1-\frac{1}{(n^\alpha-2)^2}}^n \br{1-n^{-\alpha}} \sqrt{1-2n^{-\alpha}-n^{-1}}}{e^{\frac{1}{12\lfloor n - 2n^{1-\alpha}\rfloor}} \br{2+n^{\alpha-1}}}$, we have for $\alpha \geq 1/2$ that
    \begin{align}
        Q_L(n) n^\alpha \leq Q_K(x,x+1)
    \end{align}
    for all $x \in K' = \{\lfloor 2\lambda_n - n,...,n-2\}$ where $\lambda_n = n-n^{1-\alpha}$.

