[Proposition RSRI-main of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\} $ and $t \in {\mathrm{supp}_\mathrm{t}} \ {\mathring{R}_{q + 1}}$, there exists a constant $\alpha \in \left( {\frac{\beta }{{b}},\beta } \right)$ such that the Reynolds stress ${\mathring{R}_{q + 1}}\left( {t,x} \right)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
{\left\| { \mathring{R}_{q + 1} } \right\|_N} \lesssim {\delta _{q + 2}}\lambda _{q + 1}^{N - \alpha } ,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
{\left\| { {{ D_{t,{q + 1} }}} \mathring{R}_{q + 1} } \right\|_N}  \lesssim \delta _{q + 1}^{\frac{1}{2}}{\delta _{q + 2}}\lambda _{q + 1}^{N + 1 - \alpha }  .  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

