[Theorem 47 ($2$ shift operator main result) of arXiv:2604.04267, 'On Sharpest Tail Bounds for Functions \\ of Tail Bounded Random Variables'] Let $V \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be closed. Then there exists $G \ni 0$ and $c = (c_1,...,c_n) \in [0,1]^n$ such that\footnote{$\mathscr{S}_2$ is at definition~\ref{S2def}.}
