[Defn 2 of arXiv:2608.30415, 'On generalized complex projective product spaces'] A closed smooth $2n$-dimensional $T^n$-manifold $M^{2n}$ is called a quasitoric manifold over a simple polytope $Q$ if the following conditions are satisfied:
\begin{enumerate}
\item the $T^n$ action is locally standard, denoted by $\rho$.
\item the orbit map $\mathfrak{q} \colon M^{2n} \to Q$ sends  an $\ell$-dimensional orbit to a point in the interior of an $\ell$-dimensional face of $Q$.
\end{enumerate}

