{"artifact_digest":"sha256:ad2f8fb7eb41f17740e08e2a425c8d7cacbdb6caa9dbf0b412a9824525c2eb38","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/ad/ad2f8fb7eb41f17740e08e2a425c8d7cacbdb6caa9dbf0b412a9824525c2eb38.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:8176106a961dee0c88f34e3e1fd966ba0bbc005648b314dd2e841b33b2f3d1e6","bundle_entry_key":"2607-18194-lemma-44-removing-completion","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_034","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_034.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-18194-lemm-44-removing-completion","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Applying a Borel isomorphism reduces to the case $S\in\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})$. 
    We first assume that $Z$ is integrable.
