body:
[Defn 18 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\mathbf{D}$ be an ordered finite subset of $\R$ with cardinality $|\mathbf{D}|\geq 3$, and $X : \Omega \rightarrow \mathbf{D}$ be a random variable with probability mass function 
\begin{align}
\P\left(X = d_j\right) = P_{X}(d_j), \notag 
\end{align}
for every $d_j \in \mathbf{D}$. The random variable $X$ is called \emph{near}-log-concave of degree $r\in \Z_+$ for finite $0 \leq r \leq |\mathbf{D}|-3$, if 
\begin{align} 
P_{X}(d_{j-1})P_{X}(d_{j+1}) \leq P_{X}(d_j)^2 \hspace{0.15in} \text{$\forall j\in\mathcal{I}_{|\mathbf{D}|}^{(r)}$}, \notag
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{I}_{|\mathbf{D}|}^{(r)} \subseteq \mathcal{I}_{|\mathbf{D}|} = \{2,\ldots,|\mathbf{D}|\}$ such that 
\begin{align}
|\mathcal{I}_{|\mathbf{D}|}^{(r)}| = |\mathbf{D}| - r - 2. \notag
\end{align}

[Lem lem_ballVolumeBoundsGeneralRiemann of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a Riemannian manifold and let $A\subseteq\mathcal{M}$ be relatively compact. Then there is $0<r\leq\inj(A)$ and constants $c,C>0$ depending on $A$, such that 
    \begin{align*}
        c~\varepsilon^d \leq \sigma(\mathcal{B}_\varepsilon^{\mathcal{M}}(\eta)) \leq C ~ \varepsilon^{d}.
    \end{align*}
    holds uniformly for all $\eta\in A$ and all $0<\varepsilon<r$. If $\mathcal{M} = \mathcal{M}_\kappa$ with $\kappa\leq 0$ then any finite $r>0$ is admissible. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

