metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5dc98b38a287143907610b6852504a644847cbb25f891a17f504161787670786","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/5d/5dc98b38a287143907610b6852504a644847cbb25f891a17f504161787670786.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:dde5771ffd13a4937becabce8cc7c871144a385884e0e6106514c37d766dfdae","bundle_entry_key":"2605-30017-theorem-13-agreement","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_028","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_028.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-30017-theorem-13-agreement","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Assume $\omega \in C^\infty$, and let $H = m(\omega)$.  By Lemma (lem:contain of the paper), we have $H \subseteq C^\infty$.  From $H \in \mathcal G_A \wedge \mathcal G_B$, we have $H \in \mathcal G_A$, in particular, and therefore, by Part (i) of Lemma (lem:ordered of the paper):
\begin{equation}
