body:
[Theorem th 5.6 of arXiv:2511.07173, '\bf Mean-field backward stochastic Volterra integral equations: well-posedness and related'] \rm
              Let (ass4.1-1 of the paper) and  $\max\limits_{1\leqslant i\leqslant N}\|\psi^i(\cdot)\|_{L^\infty_{\mathscr{F}_T}[0,T]}\leqslant K_1$ hold. If the generator $g$ is independent of the law of $Z(\cdot,\cdot)$,

                then for any $p\geqslant2$, there exist  constants $\lambda>1 $ and
               $C>0$, depending only on $(T,\beta,\beta_0, K_1,K_2,\phi(\cdot),\gamma,p,\lambda)$,   such that for $i=1,\cdots,N,$

               \begin{equation*}
                   \begin{aligned}
                       \mathop{\rm esssup}\limits_{t\in[0,T]}\mathbb{E}\Big[| Y^{N,i}(t)- \overline{Y}^i(t)|^p
                       +\(\int_t^T \sum\limits_{j=1}^N|Z^{N,i,j}(t,s)- \delta_{ij}\overline{Z}^i(t,s)|^2ds\)^\frac{p}{2} \Big]
                           \leqslant CN^{-\frac{1}{2\lambda}}.
                 \end{aligned}
                \end{equation*}

