body:
[Theorem 14 (Cubic discriminant criterion) of arXiv:2607.04467, 'Bernstein Functions at Work:\\ Coalescents, Copulas, and Subordination'] Let $a,b\ge0$ and let $\varphi$ be the positive inverse of
\begin{equation}
\lambda=\varphi^3+a\varphi^2+b\varphi.
\end{equation}
Then $\varphi\in\BF$ on $(0,\infty)$ if and only if $a^2\ge3b$.

[Lemme corr:plusdefonctions of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] We work under the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:convergence of the paper) and consider a subsequence of the sequence $\left(\left(\mu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t}\right)_{t \in [0,T]}\right)_{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}}$ that converges in law towards $(\mu^{*}_{t},R^{*}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]}$ in $\mathbb{D}([0,T], (\mathcal{M}_{\omega}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}),v) \times [0,R_{\max}])$. Let $\varphi : (t,x) \in \mathbb{R}^{+} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} \mapsto \varphi_{t}(x)$ be continuous and such that
\begin{align*}
\exists C>0, \forall x>0, \quad \sup_{t \in [0,T]} |\varphi_{t}(x)| \leq C(1+x+ \omega(x)).
\end{align*}
Then, we have
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left( \sup_{t \in [0,T]} \left| \langle \mu^{*}_{t}, \varphi_{t} \rangle \right|\right) <+ \infty.
\end{align*}

