[Lemm l:a-priori-change-full of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] There exists $C>0$ such that for all sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$, all $k\in\llbracket 1, M-1\rrbracket$, and  all $n\geqslant 1$,
    it holds $\mathbb{P}_\mathrm{re}$-a.s. that
    \begin{align*}
        \left|
                \mathcal{H}^{\xi,(n)}_{{\,\mathrm{TF}_k}} - \mathcal{H}^{\eta_k,(n)}_{{\,\mathrm{TF}_k}}
        \right|
        \1_{\xi,\eta_k \in \mathsf{Good}_{\varepsilon,n}}
        \leqslant 
        C \varepsilon^{1/2} n^{1/3} \log^{4}(1/\varepsilon)
        + C\log\log(1/\varepsilon),
    \end{align*}
    where $\mathsf{Good}_{\varepsilon,n}$ was defined in (equation e:def-Good-event of the paper).

