[Theorem thm:muckenhoupt_majorant of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] If $J_0\in L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ is a radially decreasing majorant of $J\in L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$,
then for all $u\in L^1_{\operatorname{loc}}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, we have the following pointwise estimate
\begin{align*}
(u\ast J)(x)\leq\|J_0\|_{L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)}\mathfrak{M}(u)(x),\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^d,
\end{align*}
where $u\ast J:=\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}J(\cdot-y) u(y)\,dy$ denotes \emph{convolution}, and ${\mathfrak M}$ is as in (equation eq:Max of the paper).

[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] The process $({\bar X}^\varepsilon_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with state space $\{0,1\}$ and c\`adl\`ag  trajectories defined by 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\forall t \ge 0, \quad {\bar X}^\varepsilon_t = \sum_{k\ge 0} {\mathbf 1}_{ t \in [e_{2k+1}^{\varepsilon}, e_{2k+2}^\varepsilon )} 
\end{split}
\end{equation}
converges in law to the jump Markov process $({\bar X}_t)_{t \ge 0}$ defined in Section \ref{sec:imr}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

