{"artifact_digest":"sha256:c51e64a2904c9d2bac07c21a34041588a76168dcdf3cb16571b965ce2065375f","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/c5/c51e64a2904c9d2bac07c21a34041588a76168dcdf3cb16571b965ce2065375f.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:9a55bd87a3dbcd12b685a1cbdd2b8e74003347ea9cea944883f6b992f6dd6ed7","bundle_entry_key":"2411-18155-theorem-23-powers","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_112","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_112.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2411-18155-satz-23-powers","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \emph{Step 1: $p\neq \infty$.}
From (thm:norm-lemma of the paper) and the monotonicity of the expectation, we conclude $\mathds{E}[\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}^r]\lesssim\mathds{E}[\Xi^{\frac{r}{p}}]$ with $\Xi$ as in 
  \hyperref[{eq:master-quantity}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:master-quantity}}}}
