[Lemma lem:eva of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Take any $X, H, G, L \in \mathbb Z_{\ge 0}$ with $X+H+G$ even, and sample $\mathfrak{f}:\llbracket 0, X\rrbracket \to \mathbb Z_{\ge 0}$ uniformly from $\mathscr F(X;H,G)$, conditional on $\max \mathfrak{f}\le L$.
Take $k\in\mathbb N$ and discrete intervals $\llbracket X_1, Y_1\rrbracket, \ldots, \llbracket X_k, Y_k\rrbracket$ contained in $\llbracket 0, X\rrbracket$.
Assume that they are disjoint from each other, except for at endpoints  and also assume that $Y_i-X_i\ge 1$ for all $i$. Take $a_1,\ldots, a_k \in \mathbb N$, and denote $a=\sum_{i=1}^k a_i$.  For each $i\in\llbracket 1, k\rrbracket$, denote $V_i = \max_{\llbracket X_i, Y_i\rrbracket}\mathfrak{f} - \min_{\llbracket X_i, Y_i\rrbracket}\mathfrak{f}+1$.
We have
\begin{equation}  
\mathbb E\left[\prod_{i=1}^k \frac{V_i^{a_i}}{a_i!} \right] < C^a \log(a+1)^a (a^{-a/2}X^{a/2} + a^{-a} |H-G|^a )
\end{equation}
and for any $K\in \mathbb N$,
\begin{multline}  
\mathbb E\left[\prod_{i=1}^k \frac{V_i^{a_i}}{a_i!} (\mathds 1[\max \mathfrak{f} \ge \max\{H,G\}+K] + \mathds 1[\min \mathfrak{f} \le \min\{H,G\}-K]) \right] \\ < C^a \log(a)^a (a^{-a/2}X^{a/2} + a^{-a} (|H-G|+K)^a ) \exp(-cK^2/X).
\end{multline}
We emphasize that the constant $C$ does not depend on $k$, i.e., the number of intervals.

