[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2608.22112, '2608.22112'] \textbf{(Optimality under extended horizon)}
Let $\tilde \f_H$ and $\tilde \f_{H+1}$ be minimizers of $\mathrm{Loss}_H$ and $\mathrm{Loss}_{H+1}$, respectively. Then
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Loss}_{H+1}(\tilde \f_{H+1})
\le
\mathrm{Loss}_{H+1}(\tilde \f_H).
\end{equation}

