[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $0< a \leq b$ and $r\geq0$. Define an ellipse
    \begin{equation}
        E_r = \left \{(x,y)\in \R^2 :\frac{x^2}{b^2}+\frac{y^2}{a^2}\leq \frac{r}{\pi} \right \}.
    \end{equation}
There exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that for every $0 \leq r_1 \leq r_2$ we have
\begin{equation}
     \#\left(( E_{r_2} \setminus E_{r_1})\cap \Z^2 \right) \leq ab(r_2-r_1) + C(a\sqrt{r_2} + b \sqrt{r_2-r_1} + 1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:Z-moments of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Fix a target exponent $q^* \geq 1$. Under Assumptions~(ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper), (ass:SC of the paper), and~(ass:SC-raised of the paper) at target $q^*$, there exists a finite constant $C_{q^*} > 0$, depending only on $q^*$, $T$, $\varepsilon_{q^*}$, the BDG constants, and the structural constants of Assumptions~(ass:SC of the paper) and~(ass:SC-raised of the paper), such that for every $v \in H$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}\Bigl[\sup_{\max(s,r) \leq \tau \leq t} \norm{\mathcal{Z}(\tau, s; r)v}_{L_2(U,H)}^{2q^*}\Bigr] \;\leq\; C_{q^*}\,\lVert v \rVert_H^{2q^*}.
\end{equation}
As in Proposition~(prop:Y-moments of the paper), the corresponding operator-norm bound $\mathbb{E}[\sup_\tau\norm{\mathcal{Z}(\tau,s;r)}_{L(H)}^{2q^*}]$ is in general strictly stronger and not provided by the abstract framework. At the base target $q^* = 1$ the displayed exponents of Assumption~(ass:SC-raised of the paper) reduce to those of Assumption~(ass:SC of the paper), and Proposition~(prop:Z-moments of the paper) recovers Theorem~(thm:Z-wellposed of the paper) exactly.

