[Lemma lem:correlation_stopping_tilde of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There is some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, c > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[
        \exists j \in L^0_\ell \text{ such that } \mathsf{AllReversed}^j(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}},\widetilde{\mathbf{Y}}) \text{ holds}
    \mright] \geqslant 1 - C e^{-c t},
\end{equation}
and the same holds with $L^0_\ell$ replaced by $L^0_r$, $L^t_\ell$, or $L^t_r$.

[Lem 4arms_polynomial_concentration of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $\zeta>0$. Then there exists $R(\zeta)$ such that for all $R\geq R(\zeta)$, there exists $c=c(R)$ such that for all $k\geq2$, $n> R^k$ and $B\in\mathcal{B}^R_{k,n}$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\mathbf{P}(B\textrm{ is important})\geq cR^{-\!\left(\frac{5}{4}+\zeta\right)k}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}

