[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_ambient_restriction of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $K\subseteq T$ be finite and contain $t_0$. For
$j\in\cbr{1,2}$, write $d_{j,K}:=d_j|_{K\times K}$.
There exists a probability measure $\widetilde\mu_{j,K}$ on $K$ such
that, for every $t\in K$ and every $r\ge0$,
\begin{align*}
\widetilde\mu_{j,K}(\cbr{t_0})
\ge\frac12,\ 
\widetilde\mu_{j,K}(B_{d_{j,K}}(t,2r))
\ge
\frac12\mu_j(B_{d_j}(t,r)).
\end{align*}
Moreover, if $c_{\alpha_j}^{(0)}
:=
\max\cbr{1,2^{1/\alpha_j-1}}$, then
\begin{align*}
&\int_0^{4v_j(t)}
\left(
\log\frac{1}{
\widetilde\mu_{j,K}(B_{d_{j,K}}(t,r))
}
\right)^{1/\alpha_j}dr\le
2c_{\alpha_j}^{(0)}
\Phi_j(t)
+
4c_{\alpha_j}^{(0)}
(\log2)^{1/\alpha_j}v_j(t).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

