[Theorem 51 (cf.\ {\cite[Theorem 1.5) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {K24}}]
    Let $\cT^\omega_{n, \beta}$ be the RSTRE on the complete graph $K_n=(V_n, E_n)$ with $n$ vertices and i.i.d.\ disorder variables $(\omega_e)_{e\in E_n}$ uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$. Denote by $M_n$ the MST coupled to $\omega$ as in \ref{SS:CoupleRG}. If $\beta \ll n^2/\log n$, then
    \begin{equation*}
        \widehat{\P}( \cT^\omega_{n, \beta} = M_n) \rightarrow 0.
    \end{equation*}
    If on the other hand $\beta \gg n^2 \log n$, then
    \begin{equation*}
        \widehat{\P}( \cT^\omega_{n, \beta} = M_n) \rightarrow 1.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem convexbifurcation of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] After some arbitrarily $C^\infty$-small perturbation of $\xi$, there exists finitely many times $0 < t_1 < \dots < t_N < 1$ such that 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $t \neq t_i$, then $S_t$ is $\xi$-convex ,
        \item At $t=t_i$, a pair of parallel closed characteristics of $\xi|_{S_t}$ is born or dies.
    \end{itemize}
    Moreover, when a pair of characteristics is born (in forwards time), a $\flat$ annulus appears between them, and when a pair of characteristics dies, a $\sharp$ annulus disappears between them (see \zcref{fig:birthdeath}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

