[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.04853, 'Minimal-Norm Extensions of Stationary Kernels on Subgroups of Locally Compact Abelian Grou'] Let $f \in L^1(G)$ and assume that $\hat{f}\in L^1(\hat{G})$. Then 
    \begin{align*}
        f(x)= \int_{\hat{G}} \xi(x) \hat{f}(\xi) \d \xi
    \end{align*}
for almost all $x \in G$. Moreover, if $f$ is continuous, then the identity holds for every $x \in G$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

