[Proposition 6 (Constant rank theorem) of arXiv:2609.02516, 'Power convexity of the torsion function on horo-convex domains in hyperbolic space'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded, smooth domain in $\mathbb{H}^n$ for $n\geq 2$, and let $v\in C^\infty(\Omega)$ be a solution of
\begin{equation}
\Delta v=-\frac{1+|\nabla v|^2}{v}
\end{equation}
satisfying
\begin{equation}
-\frac{1}{2n}<v<0\quad\mathrm{in}\ \Omega.
\end{equation}
If $\Lambda=\nabla^2v-|\nabla v|g\geq 0$ in $\Omega$, then $\Lambda$ has constant rank in $\Omega$.

