[Lemma lem.m-mu-tail of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Let $\mathcal{X}_\mu(\omega)$ be the smallest integer $n\ge \mathcal{X}_{\beta_h}(\omega)$ satisfying
	\begin{equation}
		\|e^{-2V}-\mathbb{E}[e^{-2V(0)}]\|_{\hat{\phantom{H}}\v@true\h@true\negph@nt{H}\underline{H}^{-1/6}(\square_M)}\le 3^{M/24}\qquad\text{for every integer }M\ge n\, .
	\end{equation}
	There exist deterministic $C<\infty$ and $c>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{Q}(\mathcal{X}_\mu\ge M)\le C\exp(-cM^{\sigma})\qquad\text{for every }M\ge 0\, ,
	\end{equation}
	with $\sigma\in(0,1)$ as in (equation eq.m-beta0-tail of the paper).

