[Proposition 8 (Bartlett--Koopman correspondence) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Let $\eta$ be stationary with local second moments. For every
$f\in\mathcal S(\bR^d)$,
\begin{equation}

    d\varsigma_{(\mathbb S f)^\circ}(\xi)
    =|\hat f(\xi)|^2\,d\sigma_\eta(\xi).
\end{equation}
For the standard-lattice subaction $T^k\omega:=k.\omega$ one therefore has
\begin{equation}

    \varsigma_{(\mathbb S f)^\circ}^{\mathrm{lat}}
    =p_*\bigl(|\hat f|^2\sigma_\eta\bigr).
\end{equation}

