[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.01742, 'Large deviation principles for SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] (Large deviation principle) The solution $\{u^\varepsilon\}_{\varepsilon> 0}$ to  Eq.\,\eqref{SHE} is said to satisfy an LDP on $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K,\mathbb R)$ with the rate function $I$, if the following two conditions hold:

	(a) (Upper bound) For each closed subset $F$ of $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K, \mathbb R)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\limsup_{ \varepsilon\to0}  \varepsilon\log \mathbb{P}(u^\varepsilon\in F)\le -\inf_{z\in F} I(z).
	\end{align*}

	(b) (Lower bound) For each open subset $G$ of $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K, \mathbb R)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\liminf_{ \varepsilon\to0}  \varepsilon\log \mathbb{P}(u^\varepsilon\in G)\ge -\inf_{z\in G} I(z).
	\end{align*}

[Proposition prop:Markov of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $f_1,\ldots,f_m:\mathbb{Z}_{\ge j}$ be a coupling of initial conditions, independent of the weights at and above level $j$ : $(\omega_{k,\ell})_{k \ge \ell \ge j}$ (not necessarily independent among the $f_i$). 
Then, the process
\begin{equation} 
n \mapsto \Bigl(G_{f_i,j}(n + k,n)\Bigr)_{i \in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket, k \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}}, \quad n \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge j-1}
\end{equation}
is a Markov chain on the state space $(\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}})^m$. Furthermore,
the recentered process 
\begin{equation} 
n \mapsto \Bigl(G_{f_i,j}(n + k,n) - G_{f_i,j}(n,n) \Bigr)_{i \in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket, k \in \mathbb{N}}, \quad n \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge j}
\end{equation}
is a Markov chain on the state space $(\mathbb{R}^\mathbb{N})^m$.

