[Corollary 21 (Identification of the Debye corrector) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Assume the preparation in \cref{cor:expansion} with $M\ge1$.  Then
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
 \sup_{t_0\le t\le T}\biggl(&
 \norm{\eps^{-2}(n-\Nr)-N_1}_{H^s}
 +\norm{\eps^{-2}(u-(\Vr,0))-U_1}_{H^s}\\
 &+\norm{\eps^{-2}(\phi-\log\Nr)-\Phi_1}_{H^s}\biggr)
 \le C\eps^2. 
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
Thus the forced system \eqref{eq:first-corrector-mass}--
\eqref{eq:first-corrector-momentum}, together with
\eqref{eq:first-phi}, is the actual first variation of the
Euler--Poisson solution around the quasineutral smooth simple wave.

[Proposition 26 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] Equations \eqref{eq_defZtau_Naif_Alternative} and \eqref{eq_defZtau_T+_alternative} are respectively equivalent to
\begin{equation} 
	{ \PPi}^\mcZ\left(\Psi(\tau)\right)(x) = x^p \, \xi_\ell  \,  \prod_{j=1}^{n} \partial^{b_j}K * {\PPi}^\mcZ\left(\Psi(\tau_j)\right),  
\end{equation}
for $\tau = X^p\Xi_\ell\prod_{j=1}^n\mcI_{b_j}(\tau_j) \in T$. And 
\begin{equation} 
	{ \PPi}^\mcZ\left(\Psi(\tau)\right)(x) = x^p \prod_{j=1}^{n} { g}^\mcZ\left(D^{b_j}\Psi(\mcI(\tau_j))\right),
\end{equation}
for $\tau = X^p\prod_{j=1}^n\mcI^+_{b_j}(\tau_j) \in T^+$.

