[Thm fixed K 't Hooft master loop equation for surface sum of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a non-null loop $\ell$ and a plaquette assignment  $K:\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to\mathbb{N}$. Let $\mathbf{e}$ be a specific edge of the loop $\ell$. Suppose that the  edge $\mathbf{e}$ is a copy of the lattice edge $e\in E_{\mathbb{Z}^d}$. Then
\begin{align*}
	\phi^K(\ell) =&\sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
	\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}
	\phi^{K_1}(\ell_1)\phi^{K_2}(\ell_2) - \sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
	\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}\phi^{K_1}(\ell_1)\phi^{K_2}(\ell_2) \\
	&+ \upbeta
	\sum_{p\in \mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}(e^{-1},K)}
	\phi^{K\setminus p}(\ell \ominus_{\mathbf{e}}p)
	-\upbeta\sum_{q\in \mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}(e,K)}
	\phi^{K\setminus q}(\ell \oplus_{\mathbf{e}}q),
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}(e,K)$ denotes the collection of plaquettes in $\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}$ containing $e$ as one of the four boundary edges (with the correct orientation) and such that $K(p)\geq 1$.

We also used the (more compact) notation $\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}$ to indicate the sum $\sum_{\substack{K_1,K_2:\\K_1+K_2=K}}$, where $K_1+K_2=K$ means that $K_1(p) + K_2(p)=K(p)$ for all $p\in \mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma G-positive of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] If 
\begin{equation}
M\geq \frac{2}{3},\qquad p\in (M,1],  
\end{equation}
then 
\begin{equation}
G(p,M)=2p^{3}+(1-4M)p^{2}-p+2M^{2}>0.  
\end{equation}

