[Theorem thm:weak, density of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be a  capacity preserving system, where $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$ is standard and $V$ is an upper probability. Then $V$ is weakly mixing if and only if there exists $Q\in\mathcal{ M}^{wm}(T)\cap\operatorname{core}(V)$   such that for any $f\in L^\infty(\Omega,\mathcal{F},Q)$, there exists a subset $J=J_f$ of $\mathbb{N}$ with  $D(J)=0$ such that for any $g\in L^\infty(\Omega,\mathcal{F},Q)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{n\notin J,n\to\infty}\int (f\circ T^n)\cdot gdP=\int fdQ\int gdP\text{ for any }P\in\operatorname{core}(V).
	\end{equation}

