[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.02785, 'Characterization of Stanley-Reisner varieties by their automorphism group'] Let $i\in[n]$, let $\beta\in\ZZ^n_{\geq0}$ with $\beta_i=0$, and set $S:=\supp(\beta)$. The formula
$$
\partial:=\overline{\mathbf{x}}^{\beta}\,\frac{\partial}{\partial \overline{x}_i}
$$
defines a nonzero locally nilpotent derivation of $\KK[\Delta]$ if and only if
\begin{equation}
\emptyset\neq\mathcal{F}_{S}(\Delta)\subseteq\mathcal{F}_i(\Delta).
\end{equation}
Condition \eqref{eq:root-condition} is the description of the negative roots in
\cite[Proposition~3]{Mul95}; see \cref{rem:muller-dictionary}.

