[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] Let \(x^{\varepsilon}_t\) be the solution to the random ODE \eqref{eq: random odes} and \(y_t^{\varepsilon}\) be the fractional Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process defined in \eqref{eq: fOU SDE}. Then for any \(G\in L^2(\mu)\) we have that 
\begin{equation}
\left\|\alpha(\varepsilon, H^*(m))\int_0^\delta G(Y^{\varepsilon}_s)ds\right\|_{L^2}\sim K\delta^{1/2\vee H^*(m)}
\end{equation}

