{"artifact_digest":"sha256:7ad5670ef265ae00bd01cf60e1cfeab00f1b0ac2e8e0439580007f3027b1485b","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/7a/7ad5670ef265ae00bd01cf60e1cfeab00f1b0ac2e8e0439580007f3027b1485b.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:650492c0ab3ce3848585d529f899b77e57a9176ff03b13a8af64d24bef41db0f","bundle_entry_key":"2511-02725-lemma-32-fast-mixing-within-ell-loc","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_004","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s1_004.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2511-02725-lemma-32-fast-mixing-within-ell-loc","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We prove this by reducing to a block dynamics restricted to the set $\ell_0\loc$ which we will now denote by $\bar \Omega$. 
    Let $M = e^{\Te(1/\ep)}(\log n)^3$ with appropriate constants to be specified implicitly later in the proof.
    The main reduction will be to the restricted block dynamics with the following two blocks: 
    \begin{enumerate}
