[Lemma 11 (Density--Stiefel representation) of arXiv:2606.21137, 'A Sudakov--Fernique proof of Lehner-type edge bounds for matrix-valued GUE sums'] Assume \(M\ge N\).  Then, in distribution,
	\begin{equation}

		\lambda_{\max}(H_M)
		=
		\sup_{C\in\DN,\,W\in\St_{N,M}}
		\left\{
		\Tr(A_0C)+\frac1{\sqrt M}\sum_{i=1}^n
		\ip{G_i}{W^*B_i(C)W}_F
		\right\}.
	\end{equation}

[Definition 1 of arXiv:2607.17087, 'Transportation-cost inequalities for invariant measures of stochastic reaction-diffusion e'] We say that a measure $\mu$ on $(X,d)$ satisfies the $L^p$-transportation-cost inequality $T_p(C)$ if there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for all probability measures $\nu$ on $(X,d)$,
\begin{equation}
 W_p(\nu, \mu)\leq \sqrt{2C H(\nu| \mu)}.
 \end{equation}
The case $p=2$ is referred to as the quadratic transportation-cost inequality, also called the Talagrand inequality.

