body:
[Thm brownian1 of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] [CC]
    As $L\to \infty$, $N\rightarrow\infty$, the following weak convergence holds in $\Omega$:
    \begin{equation}
    P_{t,L,N}^{*,0,0} \circ (\psi_{t,L})^{-1} \implies B_{e}(\cdot)
    \end{equation}
    where $B_{e}:\ [0,t]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ is the law of a Brownian excursion of length $t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop: limit of hazard rate term of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Given any Lipschitz function $\varphi \in C_b(\mathbbm{R}_+^3)$, we have:
	\begin{equation*}
		\bar\boldsymbol{D}_t(\varphi) = \int_0^t \angled{\varphi_s\left[\bar r\left(\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s\right) h_g^x + h_g^y\right]}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}ds
	\end{equation*}
	for all $t \geq 0$ with probability one.

