[Lemma lem:contraction of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] If the conditions of (t:hp of the paper) hold, then

    \begin{equation}
        \beta(\phi P_u^n, \psi P_u^n) \leq 2(1-\epsilon)^n
        \quad \text{for all  $\phi, \psi \in \mathscr{P}(S)$ and $n \in \mathbb{Z}_+$.}
    \end{equation}

[Definition 2 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] For an integer $\ell\geq 0$, we say a permutation $\sigma\in S_n$ is $\ell$-\emph{localized} if the following holds:
\begin{align*}
    \si\in \ell\loc := \bigcap_{1\le k\le n} \{|\sigma^{-1}(k) - k| \le \ell\}\,.
\end{align*}

[Lm 9 of arXiv:2609.02576, 'Sharp estimates for the Jacobi and trigonometric Dunkl heat kernels'] The following bound holds uniformly in $t\geq 1$ and $0<y\le x<\infty$,
	\begin{equation*}
		H^-_t(x,y)\simeq H^0_t(x,y).
	\end{equation*}

