[Lemma lem:radial-L2-local-mass-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Let \(\nu\) be a finite Borel measure on \(\mathbb S^1\). There exist constants \(c,C>0\) such that for every \(x_0\in\mathbb S^1\) and all sufficiently small \(r>0\), if \(\Lambda=r^{-2}\), then
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}}\lvert\widehat\nu(Rx_0)\rvert^2e^{-\pi(R/\Lambda)^2}\,dR
