[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2607.25645, 'Estimates of the total variation distance between laws of Sobolev mappings on Gaussian spa'] Let $g_1,\ldots,g_k,h_1,\ldots,h_k\in L^p(\gamma)$, where $p>2k-1$. Then
\[
\Bigl\|
\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^k |g_j|^2\Bigr)^{k-1}
\Bigl(\sum_{j=1}^k |h_j|^2\Bigr)^{1/2}
\Bigr\|_{L^{\frac{p}{2k-1}}(\gamma)}
\le
k^{k-\frac12}
\Bigl(
\max_{1\le j\le k}\max\{\|g_j\|_{L^p(\gamma)},\|h_j\|_{L^p(\gamma)}\}
\Bigr)^{2k-1}.
\]

