[Corollary of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $\widetilde{p}$ be the reference kernel defined in Theorem (prop:alpha_llt of the paper) with $\alpha=2$. In the diffusive regime ($n\lambda \to \infty$), we have
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{x,y} |p_n(x,y) - \widetilde{p}_n(x,y)| = o\Big( \frac{1}{M (n\lambda)^{d/2}} \Big),
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{x} \sum_{y \in [N]} |p_n(x,y) - \widetilde{p}_n(x,y)| = o(1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm 42 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Adopt the notation of \Cref{thm:therecursion}. For every $i\le i_{max}-1$ and for every initial condition, the following holds off of an event of probability at most  $N^{-2L}+2\epsilon_{i+1}$ (with $L$ the same constant as in  \Cref{rem:whoisL}):
  for all times $t$ in the interval
  \begin{eqnarray}

I^N_i=    [\mC N_i^{2+\delta}+t_{\rm mix}^{N_{i+1}}(\epsilon_{i+1}),N^5],
  \end{eqnarray}
 we have that { $\mathcal{H}_{-q_0} (z) \le H^{N_i}_t (z) \le \mathcal{H}_{q_0} (z)$} for all $z \in \mathfrak{X}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

