[Proposition thm|ABGeneral of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] Assume that $a/(b-a)\not\in\mathbb N$.
Then, there exists an integer $n_0$ and an edge $j$ such that for all $n\geq n_0$, the following holds
\begin{align}
A_j\setminus \hat E_j&\neq \emptyset; 
\\
E_j\setminus \hat A_j&\neq \emptyset. 
