[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be a rational elliptic curve such that there exists $P\in E(K)[5]\setminus E(\mathbb{Q})$, where $K|\mathbb{Q}$ is a quadratic field. Suppose that $E$ has additive reduction at $5$. Then the following are equivalent
\begin{itemize}
    \item $5| d_K$, where $d_K$ is the discriminant of $K$,
    \item the Kodaira symbol of $E$ at $5$ is neither $II$ nor $III$.
\end{itemize}
Moreover, if $5|d_K$ then the Kodaira symbol of $E$ is $IV^*$ or $III^*$.

