[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] We have
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty} P^\varrho\biggl(\,\bigcup_{x\in\BbbL_n}\Bigl\{\sqrt{L_t(x)}\le\frac12 m_n\Bigr\}\cap \BB_{n,k}(x)\biggr)=0
\end{equation}
and, recalling that $ \overline P^\varrho$ denotes the coupling measure from Lemma~\ref{lemma-4.1}, 
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty} \overline P^\varrho\biggl(\,\bigcup_{x\in\BbbL_n}\bigl\{\tilde h(x)- \tilde h(z)+\sqrt{L_t(z)}<0\bigr\}\cap\BB_{n,k}(x)\biggr)=0,
\end{equation}
where we again invoked the shorthand $z:=\frakm^k(x)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] For any $a>0,b\ge0$ and any continuous function $\gamma:[T_1,T_2]\rightarrow[0,+\infty)$, the following inequality holds
\begin{equation*}
    \min_{s\in [T_1,T_2]}\left( b\sqrt{\gamma\left(s\right)}-a\int_{s}^{T_2}\gamma\left(t\right)dt\right)\leq \frac{b^2}{a\left(T_2-T_1\right)}.
\end{equation*}

