[Theorem thm:7 of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Suppose $\gamma_2(x_{max}, Y^\pm(x_{max})) = 0$ (so $\alpha^* = 0$). Then,
\begin{equation}
g^{z_0}(r\cos(\alpha), r\sin(\alpha))
\underset{r\to\infty \atop \alpha\to 0}{\sim} 
e^{-r(\cos(\alpha)x(\alpha) + \sin(\alpha)y(\alpha)} \frac{h_{0}(z_0)}{\sqrt{r}}.
  \end{equation}
where $h_{0}(z_0)$ is given by ((harm3 of the paper)). Furthermore, $h_{0}(z_0) \neq 0$.

