[Lemma lem:roughness_of_pinning of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $k \in \mathbb{N}$, $r\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}$, $x\in (0,1)$, and $m(k,r,x) \in \mathbb{N}$ with $m(k,r,x) \geq k+\left(r+k\right) \left(\min\{x,1-x\}\right)^{-1}$. Then it holds for all $y \in B_r(0)$ that
    \begin{equation*}
        \{z \in C_0 \mid z+(y-z_x) \, l^x \in \mathrm{HC}_{m(k,r,x)}^c\} \subseteq \mathrm{HC}_k^c.
    \end{equation*}
	Note that the complements above can be seen in $C_0$ as well as in $L$. Qualitatively speaking, this means that if the modified map $z+(y-z_x) \, l^x$ is very rough, then $z$ has to be of a certain roughness, too.

