[Lemma 16 (Spatial Markov property for infinite graphs) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] \sloppy 
    Suppose $(G, \weight)$ is an infinite connected weighted graph and let $A, B\subset E$ be two finite disjoint sets of edges such that $\bP^\weight_G(A\subset \cT, B\cap \cT=\emptyset)>0$. Then for any set of finite edges $F\subset E$,
	\begin{equation*}
	    \bP^\weight_G(F \subset \cT \mid A\subset \cT, B\cap \cT =\emptyset) = \bP^{\weight}_{(G-B)/A}(F \subset \cT).
	\end{equation*}
