[Lem 7 ({\cite[Lemma 3.1) of arXiv:2608.28234, 'A note on the positivity of $Q$-curvature via the continuity method'] {GurHangLin2016}}]

Assume that $(M, g)$ is a smooth compact Riemannian manifold with dimension $n \geq 5$. If $Y(M, [g]) > 0$, $Y^{\ast}_{4}(M, [g]) > 0$, and $0\leq \lambda \leq \lambda_{0} < 4$, then any smooth positive solution $u$ to \eqref{eq:GurHangLin-continuity-path-in-terms-of-lambda} with $\tilde{J} > 0$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
\Vert u \Vert_{L^{\frac{2n}{n-4}}} \leq c, ~~\text{and}~~ u \geq c > 0.
\end{equation}
Here the constant $c$ is independent of $u$ and $\lambda$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

