body:
[Definition def:gen-supermartingale of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a generalized sequential gamble space.
  A sequence $\{X_t:\mathcal{S}_t\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}\}_{t\leq T}$ is a \emph{game-theoretic supermartingale} if for all $t< T$ and situations $s\in\mathcal{S}_t$, we have 
  \begin{align}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] \leq X_t(s)~,
  \end{align}
  and a \emph{game-theoretic martingale} if $\textsf{\textbf{E}}[ X_{t+1} \mid s] = X_t(s)$.

[Lem uniqueness of arXiv:2605.14910, 'Sharp Phase Transition for the Formation of Infinite Tubes'] Let $w>0$, and let $G_w=(V_w,E_w)$ be the associated directed graph.
  Then for every $p\in[0,1]$, the following holds $\mathbb{P}_p$-almost surely$:$
  If
  \[
  \pi^-=(\ldots,\Delta_{-2}^-,\Delta_{-1}^-,\Delta_0^-)\in V_w^{\mathbb{Z}_{\le0}}
  \quad\text{and}\quad
  \pi^+=(\Delta_0^+,\Delta_1^+,\Delta_2^+,\ldots)\in V_w^{\mathbb{Z}_{\ge0}}
  \]
  are in-ray and out-ray, respectively, then there exists a double ray
  \[
  \pi=(\ldots,\Delta_{-1},\Delta_0,\Delta_1,\ldots)\in V_w^\mathbb{Z}
  \]
  such that
  \begin{equation}
  \pi|_{\mathbb{Z}\cap(-\infty,-I]}=\pi^-|_{\mathbb{Z}\cap(-\infty,-I]}
  \quad\text{and}\quad
  \pi|_{\mathbb{Z}\cap[I,\infty)}=\pi^+|_{\mathbb{Z}\cap[I,\infty)}
  \end{equation}
  for some $I\in\mathbb{N}_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

