[Lemma lemma_1-d_6-2d of arXiv:2412.05706, 'Quasi-multiplicativity and regularity for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 7$, there exists $C>0$ such that for all $n\ge 1$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\sum\nolimits_{z_1\in \mathcal{B}(n),z_2\in \partial \mathcal{B}(n)}  |z_1|^{1-d}|z_1-z_2|^{6-2d}\le C.
	\end{equation}

