body:
[Prop 29 of arXiv:2609.03653, 'The derived set of multiple star polylogarithms'] For every infinite index ${\bf k}$,
\[
P_{\bf k}(z)=\frac{zF_{\bf k}'(z)}{F_{\bf k}(z)}
\]
belongs to $\mathfrak{T}$ and is not constant.  Hence, for $0<\theta<\pi$,
\begin{equation}
\frac{d}{d\theta}\arg F_{\bf k}(e^{i\theta})>0,
\qquad
\frac{d}{d\theta}|F_{\bf k}(e^{i\theta})|<0.
\end{equation}

[Lemma eq:BinomialApproximation1 of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $n,k \in \mathbb{N}$ with $k \leq n$. For $x = k/n$ holds
        \begin{equation}

            \binom{n}{k} \approx \frac{\exp{nh(x)}}{\sqrt{2\pi nx(1-x)}}.
        \end{equation}

