[Lem rep1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists a constant $c > 0$ such that, if $k$ is large enough, for any $i,j \in \mathbb N$ with $i<j$, $n \geq k$ and $x,\widetilde{x} \in {\rm D}_n$ such that $x \in {\rm B}^-[\widetilde{x};j-1]$ and $\overline{{\rm B}^+[\widetilde{x};j]}\subseteq {\rm D}_n$, we have that	
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\Big( Z_t[x;i] = (u,\overline{y}) \,\Big|\, Z_t[\widetilde{x};j] = (v,\overline{z})\,;\mathcal F[\widetilde{x};j]\Big) = \mathbb{P} \Big( \sqrt{\widehat{T}^{[i-1,j]}_{(v)}(i)} = u\Big)h_{k,i}(\overline{y}) (1+O({\rm e}^{-ck^\gamma})), 
\end{equation}
uniformly over all $t> 0$ and $(u,\overline{y}) \in \mathcal Z_k[i]$, $(v,\overline{z}) \in \mathcal Z_k[j]$ with $0 \leq \widetilde{u}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$ and $1 \leq \widetilde{v}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$. Above, the function $h_{k,i}$ is given by 
	\begin{equation}
		h_{k,i}(\overline{y}):=\begin{cases}1 & \text{ if $\overline{y}=\emptyset$}\\ \\\displaystyle{\prod_{r=1}^m \amalg_{{\rm B}^-[0;i]}(y_r) \Pi_{{\rm B}^+[0;i]}(0,y_r')} &\text{ if $\overline{y}=((y_1,y_1'),\dots,(y_{m},y'_{m})) \in \textrm{E}_{m}[i]$ for $m \in \mathbb N$}.
		\end{cases}	
	\end{equation}

