[Lemma lemma-N1 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let  $2\le p< \infty$ and $q=\frac{pd}{d-1}$.
Let $\phi$ be the same as in Lemma (lemma-P1 of the paper).
Then, for $0< r< r_0$,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{x_0 \in \partial\Omega} 
\left(\fint_{B(x_0, r) \cap \Omega} |\phi -\fint_{I(x_0, r)} \phi |^q\right)^{1/q}
\le C M_p(g) (r).
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $x\in \Omega$,
\begin{equation}
 \delta(x) |\nabla \phi (x) | 
\le C M_2 (g) (\delta (x) ), 
\end{equation}
 where $\delta (x)=  \text{\rm dist}(x, \partial\Omega)$.
 The constants  $C$ in (equation N1-0 of the paper)-(equation N1-1 of the paper)  depend at most on $d$, $p$ and the Lipschitz character of $\Omega$.

