body:
[Prop prior-kac-rice of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $P$ be a polynomial of degree $m$ with only simple roots. Let $U \subset \mathbb{C}$ be an open set and let $\mathscr{N}(P,U)$ denote the number of roots of $P$ in $U$. Then 
     \begin{align}
        \mathscr{N}(P,U)  = \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \frac{1}{\pi \varepsilon^2} \int_{U} |P'(z)|^2 \mathbbm{1}_{\{|P(z)|<\varepsilon\}} A(dz).
    \end{align}
    Moreover, 
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{\varepsilon \in (0,\infty)} \frac{1}{\pi \varepsilon^2} \int_{U} |P'(z)|^2 \mathbbm{1}_{\{|P(z)|<\varepsilon\}} A(dz) \leq m .
    \end{equation}

