[Lemma ManyToOne:ExponentialMartingale2 of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Let $(M^\zeta_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the martingale introduced above, and $\mathbb{P}_x$ the underlying probability measure for $(Z_t)_{t\geq 0}$ in (equation eq:Intro:Diffusion of the paper). Then, $\mathbb{P}_x$-almost surely,
    \begin{equation}
        M^\zeta_t-\frac{1}{2} \langle M^\zeta \rangle_t= \log\frac{\psi(Z_t;\zeta)}{\psi(Z_0;\zeta)} + \zeta\cdot(Z_t-Z_0) - t \gamma(\zeta) + \int_0^t R(Z_s) \ ds.
    \end{equation}

