body:
[Definition def:phi4 of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Given $\nu \in \R$ and $g>0$,
the $|\varphi|^4$ model on $\Lambda_N$ (with periodic boundary condition) is the probability measure
\begin{align}
	\P_{g, \nu, N} (d \varphi) = \frac{1}{Z_{g,\nu, N}} e^{-H_N (\varphi)} d \varphi
	,  \qquad \varphi \in (\R^n)^{\Lambda_N}
\end{align}
where $Z_{g,\nu, N}$ is a normalisation constant and $H_{g,\nu,N}$ is the Hamiltonian given by
\begin{align}
	H_{g,\nu,N} (\varphi) &= \frac{1}{2} \big( \varphi,   (-\Delta)^{1-\eta/2}  \varphi \big) + V_{g,\nu,N} (\varphi)  ,    \\
	V_{g,\nu,N} (\varphi) &= \sum_{x \in \Lambda_N}  \frac{1}{2} \nu |\varphi(x)|^2  + \frac{1}{4} g |\varphi (x)|^4 .

\end{align}
Expectation is denoted either $\E_{g,\nu,N}$ or $\langle \cdot \rangle_{g,\nu,N}$.

[Prop single_tree_size of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] Let $\tau$ be a Bienaymé tree with offspring distribution $\mu$. Let $\mathrm{h}$ be the largest common divisor of the support of $\mu$, and let $\mathrm{M}$ be the set of integers $m$ such that $\mathbf{P}(\#\tau=m)>0$. Then, there exists a constant $c> 0$ that only depends on $\sigma^2$ such that
   \begin{align*}
   \lim_{\substack{m\to\infty \\ m\in \mathrm{M}}} m^{3/2}\mathbf{P}(\#\tau=m)&=\mathrm{h}c,\\
   \quad \lim_{m\to\infty}m^{1/2}\mathbf{P}(\#\tau\geq m)&= 2c.
   \end{align*}

