body:
[Proposition 36 (cf.\ {\cite[Proposition 6.1) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {MSS23}}] 
Let $K_n$ be the complete graph with $n$ vertices and let $\mu$ be the law of the random variable $- \exp(U^{-1})$, where $U$ is uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$. Fix $\beta =1$, and let $M^{(n)}$ be the MST coupled to the environment as in Section \ref{SS:CoupleRG}, then
\begin{equation} 
	\widehat \P( \cT = M^{(n)}) \xrightarrow{n \rightarrow \infty} 1.
\end{equation}
As a consequence, with high probability, the diameter of the uniform spanning tree $\cT$ is of order $n^{1/3}$ as $n \rightarrow \infty$.

