body:
[Theorem 4 (First variation in polynomial directions) of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Let \((a_*,\mu_*)\) be a joint minimizer of \(\mathcal{J}\) in \eqref{var:eq:J-def}, and let \(\rho_*=\mathcal{J}(a_*,\mu_*)\). Define
\begin{equation}
    \eta_*
    :=\rho_*\mu_*^2
    =\min_{0\ne a\in\Pcal_m}\Lambda_{\mu_*}(a),
\end{equation}
with $a_*$ realizing this minimum, and set
\begin{equation}
    R_*(t)=(t-\mu_*)^2-\eta_*.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
    \int_0^\infty R_*(t)a_*(t)b(t)\e^{-t}\,dt=0
    \qquad
    \text{for every }b\in\Pcal_m.
\end{equation}

