[Proposition prop:recursive of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] For each $k \ge 0$
  \begin{equation}

    p_{k+1} \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:entropy of the paper)}} p_k^2 + C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:entropy of the paper)}} \varepsilon_k,
  \end{equation}
  where the decoupling error $\varepsilon_k$ is given by
  \begin{equation}
    \varepsilon_k = C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:eps_decay of the paper)}} \ell_k^4 \Big( \rho_0 \exp\braces{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:eps_decay of the paper)}} \ell_k^{1/3}} + \exp\braces{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:eps_decay of the paper)}} \rho_0^{-1} \ell_k^{1/3 - 2s}} \Big)
  \end{equation}
  for constants $C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:eps_decay of the paper)}} = C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:eps_decay of the paper)}}(s, \Gamma_+, \Gamma_-)$ and $c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:eps_decay of the paper)}} = c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:eps_decay of the paper)}}  (s, \Gamma_+, \Gamma_-)>0$ depending only on the parameters indicated.

