body:
[Corollary cor-est-maximum-Poisson of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Suppose $m=\omega(1) \in \mathbb Z_+$, $m' \in [m]$ and we have $m$ independent random variables $X_1,\ldots,X_{m} \sim \mathsf{Pois(\lambda)}$ where $\lambda = \omega(1)$. Then, for $h > 3$ such that $\frac{\lambda}{h\log \lambda}>\log m$ and $h < \sqrt{\log \lambda}$ we have
    \begin{equation}{}
        \begin{aligned}
            &\mathbb P\left( \max_{1 \leq i \leq m} \{ X_i \} \leq \lambda + \sqrt{\lambda\log m} \right) \leq \exp(-m^{1/3}) \,; \\
            &\mathbb P\left( \max_{1 \leq i \leq m'} \{ X_i \} \geq \lambda + \sqrt{\lambda h\log m} \right) \leq \frac{1}{m^{(h-3)/2}} \,.
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}

