[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2506.12834, 'Space-time fractional stochastic partial differential equations driven by L\'evy white noi'] Let $p>0$ if $\alpha\ge d+1$ or $0<p<\frac{d}{d+1-\alpha}$ if $\alpha<d$. Then,
there exists a constant $C$ depending on $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,d,p)$ such that for all $t>0$,
  \begin{equation*}
    \int_{\R^d} \left|\frac{\partial }{\partial x_i} p(t,x)\right|^p\ud x = C\: t^{p(\beta+\gamma-1)+\frac{\beta}{\alpha}(d-pd-p)}.
  \end{equation*}

