[Proposition prop: spatial rescaling of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] If $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}_{\bar \boldsymbol{y}}[a, b]$, then for all $t \in [a, b]$ and $\varphi \in C_c^1(\mathbbm{R}_+ \times U_g)$, we have:
	\begin{equation}

		L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_t}\left(\varphi_t\right) = L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_a}\left(\varphi_a\right) + \lambda_0 \int_a^t \varphi_s(0, 0)ds + \int_a^t L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}\left(\partial_t\varphi_s + \bar \boldsymbol{r}_s \partial_x \varphi_s + \partial_y\varphi_s\right)ds,
	\end{equation}
	where $\bar \boldsymbol{r}_s(y) = \mathbbm{1}_{\left\{y \leq \bar \boldsymbol{y}_s\right\}}$ for all $s \in [a, b]$ and $y \in \mathbbm{R}_+$.

