body:
[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2606.17381, 'Large deviation principle for friendship-biases\\ in Galton--Watson trees'] {\bf[Spectral representation of $\Lambda$]}

For every $t = (t_-,t_0,t_+) \in \R^3$, $\Lambda(t)$ exists in $[-\infty,\infty]$. In particular,
\[
\Lambda(t) =
\begin{cases}
\log \vartheta(t), & \text{if } t_0 < \log(1/p),\\
\infty, & \text{if } t_0\geq \log(1/p),
\end{cases}
\]
where $\vartheta(t)$ is the Perron--Frobenius eigenvalue of $M(t)$.

