body:
[Theorem 18 (Gamma-ray formula) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] For the model \eqref{eq:gamma-ray-model},
\begin{equation}
 K_X(t)=\frac12t^\top A t+
 \sum_{j=1}^m\alpha_j\left[-\log(1-\beta_j\ip{t}{v_j})-
 \beta_j\ip{t}{v_j}\right]
\end{equation}
on the domain
\begin{equation}
 D_X=\{t:\beta_j\ip{t}{v_j}<1\text{ for }j=1,\ldots,m\}.
\end{equation}
For every \(t\in\R^d\),
\begin{equation}
 C_X(t)=\max_{1\leq j\leq m}
 \bigl(\beta_j\ip{t}{v_j}\bigr)_+
 =p_{D_X}(t).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if
\begin{equation}
 P=\conv\{0,\beta_1v_1,\ldots,\beta_mv_m\},
\end{equation}
then \(C_X=h_P\), the support function of \(P\).

