body:
[Cor 30 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Define functions $  {\mathpzc F},\mathpzc G_{ij}$ on $\ak$ by 
    \begin{align*}
          {\mathpzc F} (   \beta)&:= \int_I x e^{   \beta \bullet    x - \log M(   \beta)}\mu(\mathrm d   x),\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\mathpzc G_{ij}(   \beta):= \int_I x_ix_j e^{   \beta \bullet    x - \log M(   \beta)}\mu(\mathrm d   x).
    \end{align*}
    There exists $C>0$ such that the following bounds hold uniformly over $   \beta \in \ak$ and $\x\in I^k$ and $1\le i<j\le k$ and $A\in \mathbb N$:
    \begin{align*}
       \bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa) -   {\mathpzc F}(   \beta)\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-1}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|} +|   \beta|^{A}\bigg)
       \\\bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)(   a_i-   x_i)^T\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa)-\mathpzc G(\beta)\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-2}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|}+|   \beta|^{A-1}\bigg)\\\bigg| \int_{I^k} (   a_i-   x_i)(   a_j-   x_j)^T\qdif(\x,\dr \bfa)-   {\mathpzc F(\beta)}  {\mathpzc F(\beta)}^T\bigg| &\leq Ce^{C\cdot A} \bigg(|   \beta|^{2p-2}e^{-\frac1{\Con} \min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|}+|   \beta|^{A-1}\bigg).
    \end{align*}
    In the left side of the second and third bounds, one could interpret the expression using any norm on $d\times d$ matrices.

