{"artifact_digest":"sha256:4d491a4113f0544937312458ce81d36dbf338c87a508680fa711bc5a7b21f70b","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/4d/4d491a4113f0544937312458ce81d36dbf338c87a508680fa711bc5a7b21f70b.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:0e4d9f0960e50564094e8b9e3e2e031ff6651a315cd90320295f475b368af0ad","bundle_entry_key":"2609-03101-lemma-164-decomposition-of-various-compo","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_013","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s0_013.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-03101-lemma-164-decomposition-of-various-compo","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Identities \eqref{E:QLL}--\eqref{E:QBREVETL} were proven in \cite{abbrescia2022emergence}*{Lemma 21.13}; we omit the details, noting only that the proofs are based on Lemmas\,\ref{L:BASICPROPERTIESOFVECTORFIELDS} and\,\ref{L:USEFULIDENTITIESFORFIRSTFUNDAMENTALFORM}.

