[Lemma lemma-6.8 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For each~$\delta,\delta'\in(0,1)$ there exists~$\epsilon>0$ such that for all~$\boldsymbol\lambda_{0}\in\Sigma'$ and all~$\beta>0$ with $1<b\theta<1+\epsilon$ and  there exists~$k_2\ge0$ for which
\begin{equation}

\lambda_k(1)\ge\biggl(\frac{(b-1)^2}2\frac{(b+1)^3}{b^3-1}+\delta\biggr)^{-1/2}\sqrt{b\theta-1}
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}

\lambda_k(1)\le\biggl(\frac{(b-1)^2}2\frac{(b+1)^3}{b^3-1}-\delta\biggr)^{-1/2}\sqrt{b\theta-1}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\biggl|\frac{\lambda_k(2)}{b\theta-1}- \frac1{(b-1)(b+1)^3}\Bigr|\le\delta'
\end{equation}
hold when $\min\{k,n-k\}\ge k_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 5 (Increment mass bound) of arXiv:2607.12666, 'Sample-path Large deviations for \\Scheduled Arrival Processes with Unpunctuality'] Under Assumption \ref{ass:Per}, there exists $C > 0$ such that for all $0\le s<t\le T$,
\begin{equation}
\sum_{k\in\Z}\Pbb(A_k\in(s,t]) \le C(t-s).
\end{equation}

