[Definition 24 of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For a radial vector $u=(u_0,\ldots,u_n)$, let
\begin{equation}
 r_n(u)=\min\{r\in\{0,\ldots,n\}:u_i\geq0
 \text{ for every }i\geq r\},

\end{equation}
with value $+\infty$ if the set is empty.  For
$\varsigma\in\{-1,+1\}$, define
\begin{equation}
 A^{\mathrm K}_{\varsigma}(n)
 =\inf\{r_n(u):0\ne u\in\cE_n^\varsigma,\ u_0=0\},

\end{equation}
again with value $+\infty$ if there is no such vector with finite last-sign
radius.

[Lemma lm:recursionforAn of arXiv:2505.00198, '\ttl'] The sequence $A_n$ defined in (equation eqn-An-MMr of the paper), satisfies
\begin{equation}
(\theta + \gamma) A_0 - \theta A_1 = \gamma 
\end{equation}
and, for $n\ge 1$, 
\begin{equation} 
\theta  A_{n+1}- (n + \theta + \gamma)   A_n +  n  A_{n-1} =0.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

