[Proposition PropDataSingle of arXiv:2608.28949, 'The information geometry of product-reference discrete diffusion: Interaction growth compl'] For any choice of $u \in [a,b]$, the \textsf{IGC}\xspace increment is sandwiched as
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align}

  \frac{1}{2 c_u(a, b)} \mathsf{D}_u(a, b) & \leq \mathsf{G}(a, b) \leq 2
  c_u(a, b) \mathsf{D}_u(a, b).
\end{align}
Moreover, the one-step KL error~(equation EqnExactKL of the paper) is equal to
\begin{align}

\Gamma_{\scaleto{\operatorname{prod}}{5pt}}(a, b) & = \int_a^b \frac{\mathsf{D}_v(a, v)}{v (1 - v)} \, dv.
\end{align}
\end{subequations} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem incball.1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $k$ is large enough (depending only on $\gamma$), then, given $n\geq 0$, $i \in \mathbb{N}_{\geq 2}$ and~$x \in \mathbb{X}_k$ such that $\overline{{\rm B}^-[x;i+1] }\subseteq {\rm D}_n$, there exists $y \in \mathbb{X}_{k+(i-2)k^\gamma}$ satisfying $\overline{{\rm B}(y;k+ik^\gamma -3{\rm e}^{-k^\gamma})} \subseteq {\rm D}_n$ such that ${\rm B}^-[x;\max\{i-2,1\}] \subseteq {\rm B}^-[y;i-1]$, and, for all $t > 0$,
\begin{equation}
\widehat{N}^{\rm{in}}_t[y;i] \geq \widehat{N}_{t}[x;i]	 \geq \widehat{N}^{\rm{out}}_t[y;i],
\end{equation}  
 where 
\begin{equation}
\widehat{N}^{\rm{in}}_t[y;i]:=	k^\gamma N_{t}(y; k+(i-1)k^\gamma +{\rm e}^{-k^\gamma},k+ik^\gamma -5{\rm e}^{-k^\gamma})
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
\widehat{N}^{\rm{out}}_t[y;i]:= k^\gamma N_{t}(y; k+(i-1)k^\gamma -{\rm e}^{-k^\gamma},k+ik^\gamma -3{\rm e}^{-k^\gamma}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

