[Definition 6 (Admissible radial denominator) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] A function \(q:\R^d\to[0,\infty]\) is admissible for \(X\) if it is positively homogeneous and
\begin{equation}
 K_X(t)\leq\frac{V_X(t)}{2(1-q(t))}
 \qquad\text{whenever }q(t)<1.
\end{equation}

