body:
[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2606.22940, 'From smooth to discontinuous kernels: a variance transfer principle for hyperuniform proce'] Let $ f\in \B_{ c}^{}(\mathbb{R}^{ d})  \setminus \{0\}$ non-negative. There is $ \rho _{ f}>0$ such that the following holds:

 Let $\lambda >0, \M$ a weakly stationary measure with $\mathbf E\left[
 \M( \T) 
\right]=\lambda ^{ d} $.  Let $ R_{ 0}\geqslant 1$. Assume that for  all $ R\in [1,R_{ 0}]$, 
\begin{align}

  \textrm{Var}\left(\M(f_{ R})\right)\leqslant  | \hat f(0) |^{ 2}  R^{ d}\zeta(R).
\end{align}
Then the structure factor of $ \M$ satisfies for $ \varepsilon \in (0,1)$   
\begin{align*}
 \S(B_{ \varepsilon })\leqslant 2  | \hat f(0) | ^{ 2}\varepsilon ^{ d}\zeta (\rho _{ f}/\varepsilon ).
\end{align*}
Let $ \varphi    \in \F_{ \gamma }$     for some $\gamma >0$. Then   for all $ R\in [1,R_{ 0}]$,    { $ \mathbf E\left[
 \M(\varphi _{ \rho _{ f}R})^{ 2}
\right]<\infty $ and}
\begin{align}

  \textrm{Var}\left(\M(\varphi _{ \rho _{ f}R})\right) \leqslant  | \hat f(0) | ^{ 2}  \| \hat \varphi \|_{ \infty } ^{ 2} R^{ d}(\zeta (R) + c_{ d,\gamma }( 1 + \zeta (1))R^{ -\gamma } + \sigma _{ \zeta,\gamma }(R))
\end{align}
where $ c_{ d,\gamma }$ does not further depend on $ f,n,\M,R,\xi,\varphi  .$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

