body:
[Prop decoup of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] For every $k\ge2$ there exists a constant $C_k>0$, depending only on $k$, with the following property.  Let $\{\xi_i\}_{i}$ be a sequence of independent random variables in a measurable space $(S,\mathscr{S})$, let $\{\xi_i^{(j)}\}_{i}$, $1\le j\le k$, be independent copies of $\{\xi_i\}$, and let $f_{i_1\cdots i_k}:S^{k}\to E$ be measurable functions with values in a Banach space $(E,\|\cdot\|)$.  Then, for every $n\ge k$ and every $t>0$,
\begin{multline}
\mathbb{P}\Bigg(\Big\|\sum_{1\le i_1\ne \cdots\ne i_k\le n} f_{i_1\cdots i_k}(\xi_{i_1}^{(1)},\ldots,\xi_{i_k}^{(1)})\Big\| \ge t \Bigg) \\
\le C_k\,\mathbb{P}\Bigg(C_k\Big\|\sum_{1\le i_1\ne \cdots\ne i_k\le n} f_{i_1\cdots i_k}(\xi_{i_1}^{(1)},\ldots,\xi_{i_k}^{(k)})\Big\| \ge t \Bigg),
\end{multline}
the summations ranging over all tuples $(i_1,\ldots,i_k)\in[n]^k$ with distinct entries. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 6 (Poissonized ratio moments) of arXiv:2608.24616, '2608.24616'] For every $p>0$ and $t>0$,
\begin{equation}
  m_t(p)=\frac{t}{\Gamma(p)}\int_0^\infty
  q^{p-1}\E(Y^pe^{-qY})e^{-t\Phi(q)}\,dq.

\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
  m_t(1)=1-e^{-t\lambda}.

\end{equation}

