{"artifact_digest":"sha256:714a298932681d5ae675ab8a1708f9fec0539b6095439345c17d96b986dcdd75","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/71/714a298932681d5ae675ab8a1708f9fec0539b6095439345c17d96b986dcdd75.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:4392b5fb64c0455cb1306d5dcd7991dd009f9c5bf9ffecd1275a1650d0a6a7e5","bundle_entry_key":"2604-26819-lemma-8-m","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_022","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_022.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2604-26819-lemma-8-m","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: It is equivalent to proving that 
\begin{align}
    V(t) \coloneqq M(t)^2 &= \frac{t R'(t)^2}{u(t) R(t)}  
\end{align}
is strictly decreasing. 
Our strategy is to show that $ V' $ is strictly negative on $ (0,\infty) $. 
The proof is divided into several steps. 

\paragraph{Explicit expression of $ V' $.}
Taking the derivative of the logarithm of both sides of the defining equation \Cref{eqn:V} for $V$, we obtain 
\begin{align}
    \frac{V'(t)}{V(t)} &= \frac{1}{t} + 2\frac{R''(t)}{R'(t)} - \frac{u'(t)}{u(t)} - \frac{R'(t)}{R(t)} .  
\end{align}
Defining 
\begin{align}
    B(t) &\coloneqq 2 R''(t) + R'(t) \paren{\frac{1}{t} - \frac{u'(t)}{u(t)}} ,  
\end{align}
