[Def CC of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A probability measure $Q$ on $(\Pi, \mathcal D_\Pi)$ satisfies \textbf{Conditional Consistency} if for every $E \subseteq F \subseteq G$, with $E \in \cal F$ and $F, G \in \cal G$:
\begin{equation} 
Q([E, G]_\Pi) = Q([F, G]_\Pi) \times Q([E, F]_\Pi).
\end{equation}

