[Definition 19 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] We call a contour ${\mathcal C}$ (of the type defined above) a \emph{good contour}
if it satisfies the following properties:
\begin{itemize}
\item if $z\in  \CC^+_{\mathcal C}$   then the whole half-line
$\{z+t \; : \; t \in [0,\infty) \}\subset \CC^+_{\mathcal C}$;
\item if $z\in  \CC^-_{\mathcal C}$ then the whole half-line
$\{z+t \; : \;t\in (-\infty,0]\} \subset \CC^-_{\mathcal C}$.
\end{itemize}

