body:
[Lemma lem:optimalrs of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] \textbf{Optimal $r,s$ minimising MSE.}    Adopt the same conditions as in Lemma  (lem:asympbiasvar of the paper) and assume further that $m = n = 1$ (scalar setting).  Given a fixed $r > 0$, the optimal value of $s$ minimising $E_\infty$ is given by
\begin{align}

	s^{\text{opt}} = \frac{r(A_\infty^\ast +\sqrt{G^2 + rH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma})}{G +\sqrt{G^2 + rH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}}
\end{align}
where $A_\infty^\ast$ denotes the optimal value of $A_\infty$ as defined in (equation eq:defnAt of the paper),  which has an explicit representation in terms of the system parameters, 
\begin{align}

	A_\infty^\ast := 
	\begin{cases}
		\left(-\frac{q}{2} + \sqrt{\tau}\right)^{1/3} + \left(-\frac{q}{2} - \sqrt{\tau}\right)^{1/3}, \enskip \tau > 0\\

		2\,\sqrt{-\frac{p}{3}}\,\cos\left[\,\frac{1}{3} \cos^{-1}\left(\frac{3q}{2p}\sqrt{\frac{-3}{p}}\,\right) - \frac{4\pi}{3}\,\right] , \enskip \tau < 0
	\end{cases}
\end{align}
and $\tau := \frac{q^2}{4} + \frac{p^3}{27}$ with $ p := - (H^2 \Xi^{-1}\Sigma + G^2) $ and $q := 4b^2H^2\Xi^{-1}$.  Furthermore, the admissible values of $s$ guaranteeing $A_\infty < 0$ satisfy 
\begin{align}

	s < \min \left( r, \frac{ \sqrt{G^2 + rH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}}{G + \sqrt{G^2 + rH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}} r \right). 
\end{align}
Conversely, given a fixed $s$, there may be either one or two corresponding optimal $r$ values minimising $E_\infty$.  Specifically, given a fixed $s \geq s^u$ where $s^u:= \frac{(|G| - G)(A_\infty^\ast + G)}{H^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}$, there is a unique optimal $r$ value given by 
\begin{align}

	r^{\text{opt}} =  \frac{1}{4H^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma} \left( G - A_\infty^\ast + \sqrt{(G - A_\infty^\ast)^2 + 4(G A_\infty^\ast + sH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma)} \right)^2 - \frac{G^2}{H^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}.
\end{align}
Furthermore, if $G - 2|G| \geq A_\infty^\ast$ then given an $s$ such that $s^l < s < s^u$ where $s^l := -\frac{(G + A_\infty^\ast)^2}{4 H^2 \Xi \Sigma} $, there are two optimal $r$ values given by 
\begin{align}

	r^{\text{opt}} = \frac{1}{4H^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma} \left( G - A_\infty^\ast \pm \sqrt{(G - A_\infty^\ast)^2 + 4(G A_\infty^\ast + sH^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma)} \right)^2 - \frac{G^2}{H^2 \Xi^{-1} \Sigma}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

