[Theorem 12 (M-formula) of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] For every mean-zero and compactly supported $F\in W^{s,2}(\R^2)$ for some~$s\in(0,1)$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{\delta\rightarrow 0} \rcE_{\delta}\Ll[\mathcal A_F(\lpcfg)\Rr]=\exp\Big( \frac{1}{2\pi^2} \iint_{\R^2\times\R^2} F(z)F(z')\log|z-z'| \d z\d z' \Big).
    \end{equation}

