[Lemma Lem-MKillTn of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a constant $c > 0$ such that for any  $n \geqslant 1$ and $x \in \bb R$, 
\begin{align}
\max\{x, 0\}  \leqslant  \mathbb{E} \left(x + S_n; \tau_x > n \right) 
\leqslant V(x) = -\mathbb{E} (S_{\tau_x}). 
\end{align}

