[Lemma lem:unifbound of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Assume that $f_\ell$, with $\ell \in \mathbb{N}$ is a sequence of Gaussian fields satisfying (eq:assjet of the paper), with covariances $C_\ell$ such that
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{\ell\in \mathbb{N}}\sup_{x,y\in M,\alpha,\beta \le 3} |\nabla^\alpha_x \nabla^\beta_y C_\ell|<+\infty,
\end{equation}
then for any compact subset $K\subset M$,
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{\ell\in \mathbb{N}}\mathbb{E}\left\{ |\mathcal{L}_{f_\ell}(K)|^2 \right\}<+\infty.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:form_core_1 of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For any Bernstein function $\phi$, 
\begin{align}
    C^\infty_c(\mathbb G)\subset \mathcal{D}(\Delta^\phi_{\mathcal H})\subset \mathcal{D}(\mathcal{E}^\phi).
\end{align}
Moreover, $C^\infty_c(\mathbb G)$ is a form core for $\mathcal{E}^\phi$.

