[Definition eq-def-(M,1-delta,Z)-admissible of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    For $M \in \mathbb Z_+$, $0 \leq \delta \leq 1$ and $Z \in \mathbb R_+$, we say $(\mathbf X_1,\ldots,\mathbf X_n) \in \Omega_n$ is an \emph{$(M,\delta,Z)$-admissible} tuple, if 
    \begin{align*}
        (\mathbf X_1,\ldots,\mathbf X_n) \in \Omega_n(M,\delta) \mbox{ and } \mathbf Z_\mathbf X = \sum_{i \in [n]}\mathbf X_i^\alpha \leq Z \,.
    \end{align*}
    Denote by $\Omega_n(M,\delta,Z)$ the set of all $(M,\delta,Z)$-admissible tuples.

[Proposition prop:negative-moments of arXiv:2608.28004, 'Hausdorff Dimension of the Set of Extreme Points\\ of a Random Countable Stable Zonotope'] Let \(U=B_S(u_0,r)\subsetS^{d-1}\) be a geodesic ball, that is, the ball of
radius \(r\) centered at \(u_0\) in the metric \(d_S\), and suppose that
\(\diam U\leq\pi/4\). For every \(0<\beta<N\), there exists
\(C_\beta<\infty\), depending only on \(d\), \(\alpha\), and \(\beta\),
such that, for all distinct \(u,v\in U\),
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb E\|X(u)-X(v)\|^{-\beta}
    \leq
    C_\beta\, d_S(u,v)^{-\beta/\alpha}.
\end{equation}

