[Lemma lemma16 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A4 of the paper) hold and let $\varphi$ be a characteristic satisfying (C2 of the paper)-(C3 of the paper). Then, for every $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, the function 
\begin{align} 
t\in \mathbb{R} \mapsto e^{-\alpha t} \int_{[0, \infty)} {\rm Var}[\varphi](t-x) \nu^{(h)}({\rm d} x)
\end{align}
\noindent is directly Riemman integrable, where $\nu^{(h)}$ is defined in (equation eq62 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

