[Lemma 58 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Let $d \geq 3$ and let $(Z_\ell)_{\ell \geq 1}$ be a sequence of independent $\R^d$-valued Gaussian random variables with
    \[\E Z_\ell = 0 \quad \text{and} \quad \lambda I \leq \E Z_\ell \otimes Z_\ell \leq \Lambda I.\]
    Let $A_n := \sum_{\ell=1}^n Z_\ell$. Then there exists $C(\Lambda/\lambda,d)>0$ such that for all $x \in \R^d$, $k \geq 1, r >0$,
    \begin{align}
        \P\big(\exists {\ell \geq 1}, A_\ell \in B_r(x)\big)&\leq C \Big(\frac{r}{|x|}\Big)^{d-2}

        \\\P\big(A_k \in B_r(x)\big) &\leq C \Big(\frac{r}{\sqrt{k \Lambda}}\Big)^d.

    \end{align}

