[Lemma thm:factor_hl of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] Let $\tau_1,\ldots,\tau_{\binom{n}{k}} \in S_n$ be a set of coset representatives for $S_n/(S_k \times S_{n-k})$, let $\mu \in \Sig_k, \nu \in \Sig_{n-k}$, and define
     \begin{equation}
         \lambda(D) = (\mu_1+D,\ldots,\mu_k+D,\nu_1,\ldots,\nu_n)
     \end{equation}
     for all $D$ large enough such that this is a valid signature. Then 
     \begin{multline}
         P_{\lambda(D)}(x_1,\ldots,x_n;t) = \\ 
         \sum_{j=1}^{\binom{n}{k}} \tau_j\left( \Pi_t(x_1^{-1},\ldots,x_k^{-1};x_{k+1},\ldots,x_n) x_1^D \cdots x_k^D P_\mu(x_1,\ldots,x_k;t) P_\nu(x_{k+1},\ldots,x_n;t)\right).
     \end{multline}

