body:
[Prop Prop-Linear-Lower of arXiv:2609.01964, 'The critical exponent for the two-dimensional semilinear wave equation with strong damping'] Assume that $u_0,u_1\in\mathcal C_0^\infty$ and additionally that $M_1$ in (equation Positive-Mean of the paper) is positive. Define
	\begin{align*}
		W_{\mathrm{lin}}(t,r):=r^{\frac12}\mathcal M\bigl[S_0(t)u_0+S_1(t)u_1\bigr](r).
	\end{align*}
	For every fixed $0<\sigma_-<\sigma_+<\infty$, one has
	\begin{align}
		W_{\mathrm{lin}}\bigl(t,t-\sigma\sqrt t\,\bigr)=M_1\Phi(\sigma)\,t^{-\frac14}+o(t^{-\frac14})\ \ \text{as}\ \ t\to\infty,
	\end{align}
	uniformly for $\sigma\in[\sigma_-,\sigma_+]$. Consequently, there exist $T_{\mathrm{lin}},c_{\mathrm{lin}}>0$ such that
	\begin{align*}
		W_{\mathrm{lin}}(t,r)\geqslant c_{\mathrm{lin}}t^{-\frac14}
	\end{align*}
	whenever $t\geqslant T_{\mathrm{lin}}$ and $r=t-\sigma\sqrt t$ for $\sigma\in[\sigma_-,\sigma_+]$.

