[Lemma lem:H_Monotonicity of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] For any $z\in\mathbb{C}_+$ and $0<\varepsilon<\operatorname{Im}(z)$, there exist $R>0$ such that for all $u\in\mathbb{C}_-$ with $|u|>R$  
	\begin{align*}
		\partial_y H(u)<-\varepsilon,
	\end{align*}
	where $y=\operatorname{Im}(u)$. Moreover, if $z\in\mathbb{C}_+\cup \mathbb{R}$ and $u\in\mathbb{R}\setminus \{0\}$, then $\partial_y H (u-0\ii)=-\operatorname{Im}(z)\le0$.

