[Lemma lem:properce of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $E_{\mathcal{N}} : \mathcal{M} \to \mathcal{N}$ a conditional expectation with respect to $\sigma$. Then $E_{\mathcal{N}}$ is self-adjoint with respect to the $s$-inner product $\langle \cdot ,\cdot \rangle_{\sigma,s}$ for any $s \in [0,1]$, where the inner product $\langle \cdot ,\cdot \rangle_{\sigma,s}$ is defined as in (equation def:s-inner of the paper). It follows that $E_{\mathcal{N}}$ commutes with the modular automorphism group:
\begin{align*}
    \Delta_\sigma^{is} \circ E_{\mathcal{N}} = E_{\mathcal{N}} \circ  \Delta_\sigma^{is}\,,\quad \forall s \in \mathbb{R}\,,
\end{align*}
where $\Delta_\sigma$ is the modular operator in (equation def:modularoperator of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:GoldenThompsonInequality of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] For symmetric matrices $X,Y \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times m}$ holds
        \begin{equation*}
            \tr\cosh(X + Y) \leq \inp{\cosh(X)}{\cosh(Y)} + \inp{\sinh(X)}{\sinh(Y)}.
        \end{equation*}

