[Theorem thm-2 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For each~$b\ge2$ there exists a continuous function $\kappa\colon(0,\ffrac12)\times\mathbb R_+\to\mathbb R_+$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

\kappa(\alpha,\beta)\,\begin{cases}
=
\frac{4\beta_\text{\rm c}}\beta \alpha^2,\qquad&\text{if }\beta\le\beta_\text{\rm c},
\\*[2mm]
<

\frac{4\beta_\text{\rm c}}\beta \alpha^2,\qquad&\text{if }\beta>\beta_\text{\rm c},
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
such that the following is true for all models satisfying
Assumptions~(ass-1 of the paper)--(ass-2 of the paper) with~$\{\fraktura d_k\}_{k\ge0}$ decaying exponentially when~$\beta>\beta_\text{\rm c}$  and obeying $\sum_{j\ge1}\fraktura d_j\log(j)<\infty$ when~$\beta=\beta_\text{\rm c}$:  For all $\alpha_0\in(0,\ffrac12)$ there exists $\epsilon>0$ and, for all $\alpha\in(0,\alpha_0]$, all $\beta>0$ with~  $1/\beta > 1/\beta_\text{\rm c}-\epsilon$   and all~$n\ge1$, there exists $C_n\in(0,\infty)$ satisfying~$0<\inf_{n\ge1}C_n\le\sup_{n\ge1}C_n<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}

\bigl\langle \text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu \alpha(\phi_x-\phi_y)}\bigr\rangle_{n,\beta}
=\bigl[C_n+o(1)\bigr]\begin{cases}
d(x,y)^{-\kappa(\alpha,\beta)},&\text{if }\beta\ne\beta_\text{\rm c},
\\*[3mm]
d(x,y)^{-\kappa(\alpha,\beta)} [\log d(x,y)]^{\tau(\alpha)},&\text{if }\beta=\beta_\text{\rm c},
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
holds for all~$x,y\in\Lambda_n$ with~$x\ne y$, where
\begin{equation}

\tau(\alpha):=2\frac{b^3-1}{(b-1)(b+1)^3}\biggl[\frac{b-1}{b^{1+2\alpha}-1}+\frac{b-1}{b^{1-2\alpha}-1}- 2\biggr]
\end{equation}
and~$o(1)\to0$ in the limit as~$\min\{d(x,y),\operatorname{diam}(\Lambda_n)/d(x,y)\}\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

