[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Under \textbf{A1}--\textbf{A4}. As \(\epsilon\to 0\), \(z^\epsilon\) weakly converges to \(\bar z\), that is 
\begin{equation}
\dd \bar z_t = D\bar g(\bar x_t) \bar z_t \dd t+\bar f(\bar x_t) \dd B^H_t + \bar V^{\frac{1}{2}}(\bar x_t)\dd \hat W_t,
\end{equation}
where \(V(x,y):=(D_y \Psi \sigma)(D_y \Psi \sigma)^{*}(x,y)\) with $\bar V^{\frac{1}{2}}(x)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{m}} V^{\frac{1}{2}}(x,y)\mu^{x}(dy)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:quad_identity of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let $k \in \mathbb{R}$ and let $f \in D(\mathcal{L}_k^A)\cap D((\mathcal{L}_k^A)^\dagger)$
be real-valued. Then
\begin{align}
  \bigl\langle \mathcal{L}_k^A f, f \bigr\rangle_{L^2(\mu)}
  =
  \bigl\langle \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_k^A f, f \bigr\rangle_{L^2(\mu)},

\end{align}
with $\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}_k^A$ as in Definition~(def:sym_tilted of the paper), i.e.,
the quadratic form of $\mathcal{L}_k^A$ is determined entirely by its
self-adjoint part.

[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] For $q_N\in E_N$, with $q_1\perp\phi$ when $N=1$,
\begin{align*}
 \norm{C_\phi^{*,0}q_N}_2
 \ge \frac14\norm{q_N}_2.
\end{align*}
In particular,
\begin{align*}
 \Ker(C_\phi^{*,0}|_{E_N})
 =\begin{cases}
   \{0\},&N\ne1,\\
   \operatorname{span}\{\phi\},&N=1.
  \end{cases}
\end{align*}

