[Lemma 435 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Assume that there exists a $\sigma$-finite measure $m(dy)$ on $(0,\infty)$ such that for any $T>0$ and non-negative measurable function $f$ on $\mathbb{R}_+$, 
  \begin{eqnarray}
   \sup_{t\in[0,T]}\int_0^\infty \big| G(t,y) \big|^2 \, m(dy) < \infty 
    \quad \mbox{and} \quad 
   \sup_{n\geq 1} \int_0^\infty f(y) \,\mu_n(n\cdot dy) \leq  \int_0^\infty f(y) \, m(dy)  . 
  \end{eqnarray} 
  If $X^{(n)}  \to X^* \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+) $ weakly in $D(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)$ and $\mu_n(n\cdot dy)\to \mu^*(dy) $ vaguely as $n\to\infty$, we have $Z^{(n)} \overset{\rm f.d.d.}\longrightarrow Z^*$ with the limit process $Z^*$ given by
  \begin{eqnarray*}
  Z^*(t):= \int_0^t \int_0^{X^*(s)} \int_0^\infty G(t-s,y)\, N^*(ds,dz,dy), \quad t\geq 0,
  \end{eqnarray*}  
  where $N^*(ds,dz,dy)$ is a Poisson random measure on $(0,\infty)^3$ with intensity $ ds\,dz\,\mu^*(dy)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:MKT-L of arXiv:2412.01015, 'Classical beta ensembles and related eigenvalues processes at high temperature and the Mar'] Let $\xi$ be a random variable having distribution $\nu_0 = {\mathcal M}_{c}(\mu_0)$. Let $Y_t$ be a stochastic process satisfying 
\begin{equation}
	dY_t = \sqrt{2Y_t} db_t + (\alpha + c) dt, \quad Y_0 = \xi.
\end{equation}
Then
	${\mathcal L}(Y_t) = {\mathcal M}_{c}(\mu_t)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

