{"artifact_digest":"sha256:9ee91030e20ea8dee7731e6dae7f623e38416a967eb75819c847f48320affe62","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/9e/9ee91030e20ea8dee7731e6dae7f623e38416a967eb75819c847f48320affe62.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:851c2716eb67a70c69c90b293ee31ed585711362db170224489def809d96c48d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-27520-lemma-21-two-point-critical","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_059","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_059.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-27520-lemma-21-two-point-critical","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We use the notation from the proof of Theorem~\ref{T:two_point_order}. 
From the definition of the first renewal step, 
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{r \geq 0} Q(0 \leftrightarrow x_r) z^r &= \sum_{r \geq 0} \sum_{n \geq r+1}Q(\xi_1 =n) z^r = \sum_{n\geq 1} Q(\xi_1 =n) \sum_{r =0}^{n-1} z^r \\
    &=  \sum_{n\geq 1} Q(\xi_1 =n) \frac{1-z^n}{1-z}  = \frac{1-F(z)}{1-z} = \frac{1}{(1-z)Q(z)},
\end{align*}
or, equivalently,
\begin{equation} 
