[Theorem 25 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $D$ be regular for $A$ and $\mathpzc{l}(D)<+\infty$, and $f\in \BB_b(D)\cap C_{loc}^2(D)$. The  problem
		\begin{align}
			\begin{cases}
				\partial_t u(x,t)=-\Lpsi u(x,t), & x\in D,\,t>0,\\
				u(x,t)=0,& x\in D^c,\, t>0,\\
				u(x,0)=f(x),& x\in D,
			\end{cases}
		\end{align}
		has a pointwise solution $u(x,t)\coloneqq \mathds{E}^x[f(A^D(t))]=\mathds{E}^x[f(A(t));t<T_D]$, and $u(x,t)\to u(x,0)$ as $t\to 0$, for all $x\in D$.

