[Definition def:b-geodesics of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] If $b$ is a finite eternal solution, then for $(x,t) \in \mathbb{R}^2$, define the functions $g_{(x,t)}^{b,L},g_{(x,t)}^{b,R}:(-\infty,t] \to \mathbb{R}$ as follows: For $s < t$, let $g_{(x,t)}^{b,L/R}(s)$ be the leftmost/rightmost maximizers of the function
\begin{equation} 
y \mapsto b(y,s)+\mathcal{L}(y,s;x,t)
\end{equation}
over $y \in \mathbb{R}$. For $s = t$, we define $g_{(x,t)}^{b,L/R}(t) = x$.

[Lemma lemma3.3 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Suppose that $K>0$ with the property (equation 1.6 of the paper) be valid. Then there exists $C(K)>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \int_0^{t}\int_\Omega u_\varepsilon^{-\frac3 4}v_\varepsilon|\nabla u_\varepsilon|^2\leq C(K)\bigg\{1+\bigg(\sup\limits_{t>0}\int_\Omega u_\varepsilon^{\frac3 2}(\cdot,t)\bigg)^{\frac{5}{6}}\bigg\}
    \end{equation}
    for all $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and $t>0$.

