    \le \sum_{i=1}^{{N}} \Prob[\big]{\abs{w_i+v_i} > T/2}.
    \end{equation}
    For each $i$, since $w_i$ is uniformly distributed in $[-T/2,T/2]$ and $v_i$ is fixed, we have
    $$
    \Prob[\big]{\abs{w_i+v_i} > T/2}
    = \min\Big(\frac{\abs{v_i}}{T}, 1\Big)
    \le \frac{\abs{v_i}}{T}.
    $$
    Substitute this into (equation eq: infty norm union bound of the paper) to complete the proof.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:a052802e57a17a98306f297c9f718cfd3ccfacb1e5d29841b231fefee17f9786","revision_digest":"sha256:139771eaf2759a504e4642cacf54adb1cc0d57e399541df249522b6456fa142e","source_id":"arxiv:2506.20932","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

