where $(q)_r=q!/(q-r)!$.  Hence
\begin{equation}
 M_{r,u}^*[f_n]=(q)_r[f_n\otimes_ru_n].

\end{equation}
Since $\cD_q$ is the closed span of the ranges of all $M_{r,u}$,
\eqref{primitive:eq:adjoint-product} proves the equivalence of
\textup{(i)} and \textup{(ii)}.

If \eqref{primitive:eq:op-zero} holds and $(u_n)$ is bounded, then
\[
 \norm{f_n\otimes_ru_n}
 \le\norm{L_{f_n,r}}_{\op}\norm{u_n}
