[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] Let \(\nu(s)\) be such that \(|\nu(s)|\leq C\) for all \(s\in\mathbb{R}\) and \(|\nu(s)|\sim K|s|^{\gamma}\) as \(s\to\infty\) for some \(\gamma<0\). Let \(\alpha, \beta\) and
\(m\) be such that \(\alpha+\beta+ (m-1)\gamma >-2\). Then as \(h\to\infty\) we have that
\begin{equation}
\int_{[0,h]^3}(s-u)_+^{\alpha}(s-v)_+^{\beta}\nu(u-v)^{m-1}dsdudv \asymp h^{\alpha+\beta+(m-1)\gamma+2}
\end{equation}

