[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2606.27520, 'Critical curve of loop percolation on the $d$-regular tree'] Let $\alpha>0$ and $\kappa\geq\kappa_c$. 
Let $u,v,w$ be three distinct vertices whose common ancestor is $0$. 
Then 
\begin{equation}
\P\big(\exists\, \ell_1,\ell_2,\ell_3\in \mathcal L_{\alpha,\kappa}\,:\,0 \xleftrightarrow{\ell_1} u, 0 \xleftrightarrow{\ell_2} v, 0 \xleftrightarrow{\ell_3} w\big) \leq \big(16\alpha + 12\alpha^2 + 8\alpha^3\big) \tau_\kappa^{d(u,v) + d(u,w) + d(v,w)}.
\end{equation}

