body:
[Thm interaction_gain of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with  finite distance $\mathscr W_p(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)<\infty$ and finite free energy $\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$, $i=0,1$. Let $ \mathsf{Q}$ be the $\mathscr W_p-$optimal coupling from Theorem (thm:convnex_entropy of the paper). Then for $0\leq t\leq 1$\begin{align}
    \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})\leq (1-t)\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1}) -
        \frac{\beta(1-t)t}{2}\int \sum_{(0,0)\neq (x,y)\in \bar\xi} (x-y)^2\inf_{z\in [x,y]}f(\left\lvertz\right\rvert) \mathsf{Q}^0(d\bar\xi),
    \end{align}
    where $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$,  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$ and $f$ is chosen as in (equation eq:function_f of the paper).

[Lemma 6 (Cutoff-flux bounds) of arXiv:2608.30715, 'Endpoint Energy Atoms Force Local Pressure Concentration in Three-Dimensional Navier--Stok'] Let \(\delta_\tau\) be as in \eqref{eq:delta-def}. For every radius satisfying
\(2R<\operatorname{inj}(\Omega)\), uniformly for \(s<\tau<t<T_*\),
\begin{equation}
 \abs{B_{\mathrm{tr}}(t)}
 +\abs{B_p(t)}
 +\abs{B_\nu(t)}
 \le C_{\Omega,\chi}F_\tau^2
 \left[
 \frac{A(\tau)}{R}
 +\frac{\nu\delta_\tau}{R^2}
 \right].

\end{equation}

