[Thm THeorem:varphi_hatvarphi solution to Schrodinger system of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume that the conditions of Theorem (Theorem:DensityKunita of the paper) are satisfied, and suppose that the Schr\"odinger system (equation Equation:fgSchrodingerSystem of the paper) admits solutions $\mathfrak{f},\mathfrak{g}$ that are non-negative, measurable and bounded functions with compact support. Then the functions $\varphi,\hat\varphi$ given by (equation Equation:phi-definition of the paper), (equation Equation:phihat-definition of the paper) are of class $C^{1,\infty}$ and the pair $(\varphi,\hat\varphi)$ solves the system of PIDEs
\begin{equation}
\begin{dcases}
\frac{\partial \varphi}{\partial t}(t,x)+L\varphi(t,x) =0\;\text{ for }(t,x)\in(0,T)\times\mathbb{R}^n,\\
\frac{\partial \hat\varphi}{\partial t}(t,x)-L^*\hat\varphi(t,x)=0\;\text{ for }(t,x)\in (0,T)\times\mathbb{R}^n,\\
\rho_0(x)=\varphi(0,x)\hat{\varphi}(0,x)\;\text{ for }x\in \mathbb{R}^n,\\
\rho_T(x)=\varphi(T,x)\hat{\varphi}(T,x)\;\text{ for }x\in \mathbb{R}^n.
\end{dcases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

