[Proposition thm:observable-suboptimality-eb-rate of arXiv:2608.25551, 'Beyond Optimal Rates in Stochastic Optimization: Trajectory-Adaptive Stopping Rules'] Fix $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and suppose Assumptions~(assump:strong-convexity of the paper)--(assump:stepsize-bound of the paper) and~(assump:bounded-stochastic-gradients of the paper) hold. Let $R_0 = G^2/\mu^2$, $t_0 = 4$, and $\eta_t = 2/(\mu(t+1))$ for every $t \ge 4$. Then there exist universal constants $C, C_{\mathrm r} < \infty$ such that, almost surely,
\begin{equation}

    \widehat U_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha)
    \le
    C B_{\mathrm{sub}}^{\mathrm{EB}}
    \left[
        \frac{L_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha)}{t}
        +
        \left(
            \frac{L_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha)}{t}
        \right)^2
    \right],
    \qquad
    t \ge 4,
\end{equation}
and, whenever $L_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha) \le t$,
\begin{equation}

    \mathcal R_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha)
    \le
    C_{\mathrm r} B_{\mathrm{sub}}^{\mathrm{EB}}
    \left(
        \frac{L_t^{\mathrm{sub,EB}}(\alpha)}{t}
    \right)^{3/2}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

