[Proposition P:Prelimit-2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the process $\theta_t^\varepsilon$ be the solution of (equation E:theta-R-Q of the paper) and the limiting variance $\sigma_t^2$ is defined in equation (equation E:Limiting-Variance of the paper). Then, for any $t \ge 0,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t \ge 0}\left|\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(\theta_t^\varepsilon)} - \sqrt{\sigma_t^2} \right|  & \le K \sqrt{\sqrt{\eta} +  \sqrt{\varepsilon} + \left( \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} - \frac{1}{\gamma^2} \right)  +  \frac{\eta^2}{{\varepsilon}}+  {\varepsilon + \frac{\eta}{\varepsilon} (\sqrt{\varepsilon}+ \sqrt{\eta})}}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}

