[Lem 40 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Fix any probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F, \P)$ and sub-$\s$-algebra $\mathcal G \subset \mathcal F$. For any $\delta>0$ and  event $A \in \mathcal F$ such that $\mathbb P(A) \geq 1-p_0$, we have 
        \begin{equation}

            \P( \P(A | \mathcal G) \geq 1- \sqrt{p_0}) \geq 1-\sqrt{p_0}
        \end{equation}

