[Lemma 6 (The prime $2$ for even parameters) of arXiv:2609.01594, '2609.01594'] Let $A$ be even.  Then $u_n(A)$ is odd exactly when $n$ is odd.  If $n$ is
even, then
\begin{equation}
 v_2(u_n(A))=v_2(A)+v_2(n)-1.
\end{equation}
Consequently, $v_2(u_n(A))\geq v_2(n)$ whenever $2\mid u_n(A)$.

[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2512.01483, 'Scaling Limits of Line Models in Degenerate Environment'] For $\mathbb{P}$-a.e. realisation of the environment, there holds the convergence in law, in the space $C([0,\infty))$,
\begin{equation}

\left( \frac{1}{T^\delta} \int_0^{Tt} H^{(T)} (X^T_2(s)) \, ds \right)_{ t \geq 0} \underset{T \to \infty}{\Longrightarrow} \left(\Delta(t)\right)_{ t \geq 0},
\end{equation}
where $(\Delta(t))_{t \geq 0}$ is the Kesten-Spitzer process, defined as 
\begin{equation}

\Delta(t) = \Delta^\mathcal{H}(B_2)(t) = \int_{-\infty}^{+\infty} L^{B_2}(t,x) \, d\mathcal{H}(x),  \quad t \geq 0,
\end{equation}
where $(L^{B_2}(t,x))_{x \in \mathbb{R}, \, t \geq 0}$ is the local time process of $B_2$, where $B_2$ is a Brownian motion in $\mathbb{R}$ started from $0$ and with diffusion coefficient $\sqrt{2}$.
In addition, for $\mathbb{P}$-a.e. realisation of the environment, we have the convergence in law, in $D([0,\infty))$, 
\begin{equation}

\left( X^{(T)}(t) \right)_{t \geq 0} \underset{T \to \infty}{\Longrightarrow} \left(B_1(\Delta(t)), B_2(t)) \right)_{t \geq 0},  
\end{equation}
where $(\Delta(t))_{t \geq 0}$ is as in \eqref{eq:def_ks_process_thm}, and $B_1$ is a Brownian motion started from $0$, with diffusion coefficient $\sqrt{2}$, and independent from $B_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:covariance-bounds-het of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the modified $GI/GI/n$\xspace system satisfying Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain-het of the paper), (assump:non-lattice-het of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable-het of the paper), with the load $\rho < 1$. Let $\Gamma_{{s,j}}$ and $\Gamma_{a}$ be the terms defined in (equation eq:gamma-s-def-het of the paper) and (equation eq:gamma-a-def-het of the paper), respectively. Then
    \begin{align}

       \Gamma_{{s,j}} &\leq \min\Big(1-\rho, \frac{\mu_j}{\mu_{\Sigma}}\Big) \Big(R_{{s,j}}^{\max} - \frac{1}{2} \mathbb{E}\left[(\mu_j S_j)^2\right]\Big) \\

       - \Gamma_{a} &\leq (1-\rho) \bigg(\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\left[(\Lambda A)^2\right] - R_{a}^{\min}\bigg) 
    \end{align}

