[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] Suppose that $[\ttX]\vdash\Gamma$ is a sequent of $\sfu\RS$, and let $\epsilon_u$ be a countable enumeration of elements of $u$. Then we can construct an $\epsilon_u$-recursive $\rmbeta$-preproof $\pi$ of $[\ttX]\vdash\Gamma$ such that either
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\pi$ is a $\rmbeta$-proof, or
        \item If $B$ is an infinite branch of $\pi$ such that the union of its associated template orders is well-founded, then we can find a $B$-recursive well-founded model of $\KP + \lnot\bigvee\Gamma$.
    \end{enumerate}

