[Lemma lem:sumovery of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) there exist numbers $b_\ell^{(h)}$ such that, for every $h=0,1,\dots, r+1,$
\begin{align*}
   \Theta_{k}^{(h)}:
=
   \sum_{y=0}^\infty
        \left(\frac{y}{\sigma}\right)^{h}
        \mathbf P(S_k=-y, \tau = k)
=
    \sum_{\ell=0}^{\lfloor \frac{r-h}{2}\rfloor}
        \frac{b_\ell^{(h)}}{k^{\ell+3/2}} + v^{(h)}_k,
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
    |v_k^{(h)}|
\le
    \frac{C\log^{\lfloor \frac{r-h+1}{2} \rfloor} k}{k^{(r-h+4)/2}}.
\end{align*}
Moreover,
$$
    \Theta_k^{(h)}(z)
:=
    \sum_{0\le y\le\sigma|z|/4}
        \left(\frac{y}{\sigma}\right)^{h}
        \mathbf P(S_k=-y,\tau = k)
=
    \Theta_k^{(h)}
+
    O\left(\frac{1}{k^{3/2}(1+|z|)^{r-h+2}}\right).
$$

