[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c$ such that for any $i,m\in \ZZ$, with $T$ denoting an instance of BLPP and $\widetilde{T}$ denoting the BLPP obtained by resampling just $X_{i,m}$ to a fresh sample $\widetilde{X}_{i,m}$, we have, for all $r>0$,
  \begin{equation}

    \PP(|\widetilde T_\0^\n-T_\0^\n| \geq r)\leq Ce^{-cr^2}.
  \end{equation}

