[Theorem eq:multi-derivative of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:multiplicative-Lindeberg}
Let \(X_1,\ldots,X_M\) and \(Y_1,\ldots,Y_M\) be two independent families.  Assume that, for each \(i\), \(X_i,Y_i\) satisfy the hypotheses of (lem:one-coordinate-Lindeberg of the paper) with the same constants and match through order \(m\).  Let \(F:\mathbb R^M\to(0,\infty)\) be \(C^{m+1}\).  Suppose that for each coordinate \(i\), every \(z\in\mathbb R^M\), and \(r=1,\ldots,m+1\),
\begin{equation}
 \left\lvert\partial_i^rF(z)\right\rvert\le C_r a_i^rF(z),
 \qquad 0<a_i\le a_0(K,m,C_1).
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \left\lvert\log\mathbb E F(X)-\log\mathbb E F(Y)\right\rvert
 \le C\sum_{i=1}^M a_i^{m+1}.
\end{equation}

