[Proposition prop: strongest result for discrete and bounded time of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $f \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal B}} $. There exists a sequence of (discrete time) Markov chains $((X_t)_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} })_{n\geq 1}$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} } \left| \mathrm{d}^{(n)}(t) -f(t) \right| \xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{} 0,
    \end{equation}
    where for $n\geq 1$, $\mathrm{d}^{(n)}(\cdot)$ is the distance to stationarity for the chain $(X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0}$.

