[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Assume that Assumption~\ref{assu:frozenLipschitz} is satisfied. Then for any fixed time horizon $T>0$ and $p \geq 2$, the process $(\hat Y^{x,y}_t)_{t \in [0,T]}$ is locally $L^p$-bounded and continuous in $(x,y) \in \R^{d_1+d_2}$ with respect to $L^p$-convergence. More precisely, for any bounded set $U \subseteq \R^{d_2}$ there exists a constant $C_{p,T,U}>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{(x,y) \in \R^{d_1}\times U} \hat \E \Big[ \sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} |\hat Y^{x,y}_t|^p \Big] \leq C_{p,T,U},
    \end{align*}
    and for any $(x,y) \in \R^{d_1+d_2}$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{(x',y')\to (x,y)} \hat \E \Big[ \sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} |\hat Y^{x',y'}_t-\hat Y^{x,y}_t|^p \Big] =0.
    \end{align*}

