    Furthermore, for any $t\geq 0$, the distribution of $\XX^n(t)$ is $\mu(t)$-chaotic; that is, for any $t \geq 0$, any $k\in\nat$ (such that $k\leq n$), and any bounded and continuous function $\ff\!: (\real\times \{+,-\})^k \to \real$,
    \begin{align*}
