    \end{align*}
    Equivalently, $\text{Law}\bigparens{\xx^n_1(t), \xx^n_2(t), \dots, \xx^k_n(t)} \cdinf{n} \mu^{\otimes k}(t)$, or the particles become ``asymptotically independent'' as the population size grows. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

