[Prop 9 (Martingale structure) of arXiv:2604.12797, 'A free boundary problem for the mean-field limit of diffusing particles with nonlinear bou'] For any $\phi \in C^1(\R)$, the limit points of $(Z^{n,\phi})_{n\geq 1}$ are continuous processes. Moreover, let $\psi_{\varepsilon}$ be the probability density function of a reflected
	Brownian motion on the positive half-line at time $\varepsilon>0$, and let $H$ be a bounded continuous process $H$ adapted to the filtration $(\mathcal{\bar{{F}}}_{t}^{n})_{t\geq0}$ from \eqref{eq:Filtration_F_bar}. Then the difference
    \begin{equation}
 \int_0^t H_s \di Z^{n,\phi}_s-\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\int_{0}^{t}H_s\bigl(\tfrac{1}{2}\partial_x\phi(0)-\phi(0)\gamma(s,C_{s}^{n})\bigr)\langle\mu_{s}^{n},\sigma_{A^n}(s,\cdot)^{2}\psi_{\varepsilon}\rangle \ds 
    \end{equation}
is a martingale for $(\mathcal{\bar{{F}}}_{t}^{n})_{t\geq0}$ and it vanishes uniformly on compacts in $L^2(\Omega)$ as $n\rightarrow \infty$.

