[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $\beta\in (0,1/2)$ and $\delta\in (0,1/40)$. There exist a constant $C'$ such that the following estimates hold for all $n$ large enough, $\ell\in [n^\delta,n]$, and $m\in [\![\beta n,(1-\beta)n]\!]$,
  \begin{equation}

    \EE[|\pivot_\delta^\ell(m)|]\leq C'\ell^{2/3}n^{300\delta}, \EE[|\pivot_\delta^\ell(m)|^2]\leq C'\ell^{5/3}n^{500\delta}.
  \end{equation}

