[Corollary cor:flip-probability-ld of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Recall \(b_t^{\gR},b_t^{\gB}\) from
(equation eqn:scaled-camp-sizes of the paper). Fix \(t\ge0\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and
suppose that (equation eqn:linear-camp-condition of the paper) holds for some fixed
constant \(c_0>0\). Then, uniformly over all such configurations,
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
p_t^{\gB}
&=
N^{-I(b_t^{\gB},b_t^{\gR})+o(1)},
\\
q_t^{\gR}
&=
N^{-I(b_t^{\gB},b_t^{\gR})+o(1)},
\\
p_t^{\gR}
&=
N^{-I(b_t^{\gR},b_t^{\gB})+o(1)},
\\
q_t^{\gB}
&=
N^{-I(b_t^{\gR},b_t^{\gB})+o(1)}.

\end{align}
\end{subequations}
The missing self-edge changes the relevant camp size by one and hence its
scaled parameter by \(b/N\), which is absorbed by the uniform \(o(1)\) terms. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $(t_n)$ be a sequence of positive integers and $(w_n)$ be a sequence of positive real numbers such that $w_n = o(t_n)$ as $n\to \infty$. Let $p{\ensuremath{\;:\;}} {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}}  \to [0,1]$ be a weakly decreasing function (but not necessarily continuous) such that $p(x) \xrightarrow[x\to -\infty]{} 1$ and  $p(x) \xrightarrow[x\to +\infty]{} 0$. There exists a sequence of discrete time Markov chains $((X_t^{(n)})_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 1}$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}}  {\ensuremath{\;:\;}} t_n + cw_n \in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} } \left| \mathrm{d}^{(n)}(t_n + c w_n) - p(c) \right| \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 0.
\end{equation}

