[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.29878, 'Discontinuous phase transitions \\ in the one-dimensional \\ pair and triplet creation pro'] Let $v :\RR \to [0,1]$ be Lipschitz continuous, i.e., $|f(x)-f(y)| \le K|x-y|$ for all $x,y$. Suppose that the initial configuration has a density $v$ in the sense of \eqref{densdef}. If $t$ is fixed and $-m_\ep \le m < m_\ep$ then
$$
 P\left( \left| n^{-1} \sum_{y \in [m\delta_\ep, (m+1)\delta_\ep)} 
\xi_t(y) - u^\ep(t,y) \right| > \ep^{0.01} \right) \le  C\ep^{0.41}
$$
So with high probability this bad event will not occur for any $m \in [-m_\ep,m_\ep)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 2 (Sharp-window scattering limit) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:intro-main-random-measure}, if
$\eta$ is a stationary point process of positive intensity, then for
$\lambda_d$-almost every $\xi\in\bR^d$,
\begin{equation}

    \frac{1}{\sqrt{|\omega\cap B_R|}}
      \sum_{x\in\omega\cap B_R}\chi_\xi(x)
    \dto \mathcal{CN}\bigl(0,S_\eta(\xi)\bigr),
\end{equation}
where the left-hand side is defined to be $0$ when $|\omega\cap B_R|=0$,
and consequently
\begin{equation}

    \frac{1}{|\omega\cap B_R|}
      \left|\sum_{x\in\omega\cap B_R}\chi_\xi(x)\right|^2
    \dto S_\eta(\xi)\operatorname{Exp}(1).
\end{equation}
The second left-hand side is also defined to be $0$ when
$|\omega\cap B_R|=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 13 (Rare positive jumps) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] As $p\downarrow0$,
\begin{equation}
 t_p=L+3\log L-\log2+o(1),

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X_{\lambda,p})\sim\frac{1}{L}.

\end{equation}
The conclusion holds for every choice of a global interior maximizer; it does
not require or imply uniqueness.

