[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] There are \(n_0\geq 0, r_0\geq 0\), \(c,C>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), and any \(1\leq i<j\leq n\) with \(j-i\geq r_0 n^{2/3}\),
    \begin{equation*}
        \babs{ \Cov(n^{-1/3}W_i,n^{-1/3}W_j) } \leq C\exp(-c\tfrac{|j-i|}{n^{2/3}}).
    \end{equation*}

