body:
[Lemma 72 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $\ell \in \N$ and consider the event 
\begin{equation}
    B^{\ell}_n := \bigcap_{(u;v) \in E_{\ell n}} \bigcap_{j \in \lbr n\rbr}  B_{u,v}^{j-1,n,\ell} . 
\end{equation} Then there exist constants $c_0,C_0>0$, depending only on $\ell$, such that for all $n\in \N$,
\begin{equation}
    \P(B^{\ell}_n) \geq 1- C_0 \exp(-c_0 n^{1/6}) . 
\end{equation}

