[Lemma LEM:cov of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $g$ be a smooth, compactly supported function. Under the conditions   
\begin{align*}
\textup{dist}(\supp g, \xi_j) \ge \varepsilon^{-\frac 12 +2\eta} 

\end{align*}

\noindent
for every  $1 \le j \le k$,  we have 
\begin{align*}
\sigma_g^2=\mathbb{E}_{\nu^\perp_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k } } \big[ |\langle v,g \rangle|^2 \big]=\jb{g, (-\partial_x^2+1)^{-1} g}\cdot \big(1+O(e^{-c \varepsilon^{-\frac 12+2\eta} }) \big),
\end{align*}

\noindent
uniformly in $\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k \in [- \overline L_\varepsilon, \overline L_\varepsilon] $ and $\overline L_\varepsilon$.

