body:
[Lemma 5 (adding and removing points) of arXiv:2606.08581, '2606.08581'] Let \(A\) be a finite multiset of diameter \(D\).
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] For any \(b\in\mathbb R\), \(I(A\cup\{b\})\ge I(A)\).
\item[(ii)] If \(b\in A\), then \(I(A)-I(A\setminus\{b\})\le D^2\).
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2609.00245, 'Higher-order Gaussian bounds for maximally subelliptic boundary value problems'] \cite[Assumption \ref*{Heat::Assumption::Locality}]{StreetHypoellipticityAndHigherOrderGaussianBounds} holds.
    That is, \(\forall \xi_0\in \Compact\), \(\delta\in(0,\delta_0)\), the \(\LtSpace*[\ManifoldN,\Vol][\C^M]\)
    closure of
    \begin{equation*}
        C_{\xi_0,\delta}:=\left\{ \phi\in \DomainLinfty : \opL^j \phi\big|_{\BV*{\xi_0}{\delta}}=0,\forall j\geq 0 \right\}
    \end{equation*}
    contains \(\LtSpace*[\ManifoldN\setminus \overline{\BV*{\xi_0}{\delta}},\Vol][\C^M]\).
    The same holds with \(\opL\) replaced by \(\opL^{*}\), throughout.

