[Definition def:conjugator of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Choose $C_i \in SL_2(K)$ as in Proposition (prop:branchmodel of the paper), and set $R = C_1C_2^{-1} \in SL_2(K)$. Let $\varpi$ be a uniformizer of $K$, positive for small $u > 0$, and put
\begin{equation*}
	m_R = \min_{j,k}v(R_{jk}) \ \ \ \ \ \widehat R = \varpi^{-m_R}R \ \ \ \ \ \widehat\Delta = \det(\widehat R) = \varpi^{-2m_R}	
\end{equation*}
Then every entry of $\widehat{R}$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_K$, at least one entry is a unit, and $\widehat\Delta > 0$ at every small $u > 0$. We refer to $R$ as the \emph{relative conjugator}, and $\widehat R$ as the \emph{projective relative conjugator}.

[Proposition prop:main of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $Y$ be the process constructed in (equation eq:def_procc of the paper) with $Y_0^m = \mu+m\delta_{x_0}$, where $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F^+$, $x_0 \in\mathbb{R}$ and $m \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{ \infty\}$ and denote by $\mathbb{E}_{Y_0^m}$ the expectation with respect to the law of the process $Y$ started from $Y_0^m$.
  Then it follows for all $T>0$ that
	\begin{equation}
		\sup_m \mathbb{E}_{Y_0^m}\Big[\int_0^T\langle Y_t,1\rangle dt\Big] \leq C(T),
	\end{equation}
where $C(T)$ depends only on $\nu((0,\infty])$ and $\langle \mu,1\rangle$.

