[Thmb* once visited site of arXiv:2509.19809, 'Exact Limsup Growth of Rarely Visited Sites for One-Dimensional Simple Random Walk'] There exists some constant $0<C<\infty$ such that
\begin{eqnarray*}
\limsup_{n\to\infty} \dfrac{g_1(n)}{(\log n)^2}=C~~~~~~a.s.
\end{eqnarray*}
And for $n\in{\mathbb N}$,
\begin{eqnarray*}
{\mathbb E}\, g_1(n)=2.
\end{eqnarray*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 86 (Operator and cubic terms) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] For $\mathscr U_a^\rho=\rho V_a+X_a+Y_a$ one has
\begin{align}
 \sum_{(a;b,c)\in\mathfrak L}
 \|T^{a;b,c}(\mathscr U_{b^\perp}^\rho)\|_{L_T^1H^{s_2-1}}
 &\le T M_T^{\mathrm{op},H}(\Xi)
 \|\mathscr U^\rho\|_{E_T^{2,\sigma}},
 \\
 \sum_{(a;b,c)\in\mathfrak L}
 \|T^{a;b,c}(\mathscr U_{b^\perp}^\rho)\|_{L_T^1B_{2,\infty}^{\sigma-1}}
 &\le\left(T M_{T,\mathrm{diag}}^{\mathrm{op},B}(\Xi)
 +M_{T,\mathrm{cen}}^{\mathrm{op},B}(\Xi)\right)
 \|\mathscr U^\rho\|_{E_T^{2,\sigma}},
 \\
 \sum_{a\in\mathfrak C}\|\Gamma_a^{\chi,\rho}\|_{\mathfrak R_T^{s_2,\sigma}}
 &\lesssim T\sum_{a\in\mathfrak C}\left(
 \|\Gamma_a^{\chi,\rho}\|_{C_T\mathcal C^{-\beta_{\Gamma,a}-\kappa}}
 +\|\Gamma_a^{\chi,\rho}\|_{L_T^\infty B_{2,\infty}^{-\beta_{\Gamma,a}-\kappa}}
 \right).

\end{align}
All three bounds have Lipschitz analogues for differences of the components of
$\Xi$ and of the inputs.

[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2606.12381, 'Markov property and path regularity for the solutions to SPDEs driven by cylindrical-marti'] Assume $M$ has independent increments. For $u \geq 0$, let $\xi$ be a   $G$-valued $\mathcal{F}_{u}$-measurable square integrable random variable. 
Then, for every $\varphi \in B_{b}(G)$, $u \leq s \leq t$, we have
\begin{equation}
\Exp \left[ \varphi(X(t,u;\xi)) \, \vline \, \mathcal{F}^{M,\xi}_{s} \right] =  \left( P_{s,t} \varphi \right)(X(s,u;\xi)).    
\end{equation}
In particular, $(X(t,u; \xi): t \geq u)$ is a Markov process.

