[Lemma lem:second_point_fixed of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $\gamma$ and $\delta$ be as in Proposition~(prop:asymp_escape_crossing_probabilities of the paper). Then, the one-edge crossing probability satisfies, for $|x|=R:$
     \begin{align*}
         \pi_{r,(x,u)}\asymp 
         \begin{cases}
         u^{-1} r^d R^{-d/\gamma} \wedge 1  &\text{if }\delta>1/\gamma, \\
         u^{-1} r^d R^{-d \delta}(1+\log_+(uR^{d\delta})) \wedge 1 &\text{if }\delta=1/\gamma, \\

         u^{-\gamma\delta}r^dR^{-d\delta}&\text{if }\delta<1/\gamma.
         \end{cases}
     \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

