[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\X=\{1,\ldots,s\}$ and suppose that

\begin{equation*}
Q_z(i,j)=\sum_{k\in\N^d}e^{z\cdot k}q_{ij}(k)
\end{equation*}

is finite for all $|\operatorname{Re}z|_1<\eta$ and all $i,j$. Assume that the embedded matrix $Q_0$ is irreducible and aperiodic. Assume also that, for every $\theta\in[-\pi,\pi]^d\setminus\{0\}$, there are no complex numbers $a_i$ with $|a_i|=1$ and no $\omega$ with $|\omega|=1$ such that

\begin{equation*}
e^{\mathrm i\theta\cdot k}a_j=\omega a_i
\end{equation*}

for every triple $(i,j,k)$ with $q_{ij}(k)>0$. If the Markov-additive covariance matrix is symmetric positive definite, then Assumption~\ref{ass:operator-spectral} holds on $\mathcal B=\mathbb C^s$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 3 (Signed
transfer) of arXiv:2608.06591, 'Random Triangles on Concentric Circles'] \protect\hypertarget{lem-signed}{}

Let \(S = \operatorname{sign}(\cos\omega)\). For every bounded
measurable \(\phi\), \begin{equation}\phantomsection{
\mathbb{E}\left[S\,\phi(h)\right]
  = \frac{2}{\pi}\int_0^{\pi/2}
    \phi\left(r_i \sin t\right)\,
    \mathbf{1}\!\left\{r_i \sin t < r_k\right\} dt .
}\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 7 (Cell-to-flower volume bound) of arXiv:2607.20680, 'Exact Scale--Shape Factorization of the Typical Poisson--Voronoi Cell Volume in Arbitrary '] For every admissible candidate cell \(P\),
  \begin{equation}

    0<
    \frac{\vol_d(P)}{\vol_d(\Delta(P))}
    \leq 2^{-d}.
  \end{equation}
Consequently, every nontrivial shape-factor law \(\eta_{d,k}\) is supported on \((0,2^{-d}]\). The constant \(2^{-d}\) is universal and is sharp in the larger class of convex bodies, as shown by centered Euclidean balls.

