[Corollary Cor2 of arXiv:2608.30212, 'A Painlev\'e equation for the H\"ormander-Bernhardsson constant'] Let $n=2k\in \mathbb{N}$ with $k\ge 2$. Assume $\varphi_j=\varphi_j(c)$ and $\psi_j=\psi_j(c)$, $1\le j\le k$ are continuous in $c$ such that
\begin{align}
D_{2k}(z) = \exp\left(-\frac{cz}{1+z^2}\right) + \mathcal{O}(z^{2k+1})
\end{align}
holds. Define $I_k = \{c\in\mathbb{R}:\text{ condition (equation Phi-interlace of the paper) holds}\}$, let $I_{k,0}$ be the connected component  of $I_k$ that contains $0$, and let $H=H_c$ be the corresponding $\pm1$ function on $(0,\pi)$ with $H_c(0+)=(-1)^{k+1}$. If $\sup I_{k,0}<\infty$, then $ C_{2k-2} = \sup I_{k,0}$.

