[Lemma lemma_fineteness_moments_plusBC of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$ be a bounded, open and simply connected domain such that $\partial D$ has Hausdorff dimension strictly smaller than $7/4$. Then, for any $k \geq 1$,
\begin{equation*}
    \int_{D^k} \vert f_{D}^{(+,k)}(x_1,\dots,x_k) \vert^2 \prod_{j=1}^{k}dx_j < \infty
\end{equation*}
where $f_{D}^{(+,k)}$ is as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper).

