[Definition def:first-moment-condition of arXiv:2609.02710, 'Asymptotic Mean Value Laplacian\\ on equiregular sub-Riemannian manifolds'] The first-kind coordinates at $x$ satisfy the \emph{first-moment condition}
with respect to $\mu$ if the limits
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma_i(x):=\lim_{h\downarrow0}\frac1h
  \int_{B_{x,h}}\xi_iJ_x(\delta_h\xi)\,\,d\xi,
  \qquad i=1,\ldots,k,
\end{equation}
exist. We call the $\Gamma_i(x)$ the first-moment coefficients in the
chosen chart.

[Prop theorem:lowerboundLp of arXiv:2504.19942, 'The edge-averaging process on graphs \\ with random initial opinions'] Consider the edge-averaging process on $G=(V,E)$ where $G$ is either the $n$-cycle or the infinite path $\mathbb Z$. For every $p\in[1,\infty)$ and $\delta>0$, there are i.i.d.\ random variables $\{f_0(v)\}_{v \in V}$ in $L^p$, such that if $t^*=\min (t,n^2)>30^4$, then  
\begin{equation}
\|f_t(o)-\mu\|_p\geq 

\begin{cases}
    t_*^{\frac{1-p}{2p}-\delta}&p\in [1,2)\,,\\
    t_*^{-1/4}&p \ge 2\,.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

