[Thm correspondence of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] The map \begin{align}
     \mathsf{gap}:\mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)\to \mathcal P_{s,1}( \mathsf{S}), \mathsf{P}\mapsto 
     \mathsf{sq}_{\#}\mathsf{P}^0
\end{align}
is a bijection and for $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ it holds 
 \begin{align}
\int fd\mathsf{P}=\int \int_0^{\tau_1(\xi)}f(\theta_x\xi)dx\mathsf{P}^0(d\xi),
    \end{align}
    where $f:\Gamma\to \IR$ is bounded and measurable. We call $ \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P})$ the gap distribution of $\mathsf{P}$ resp.\ of the point process $\xi$ with distribution $\mathsf{P}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

