[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every $d\ge1$, the inclusion
$R_{\mathrm{ev}}\hookrightarrow\cO_d$ extends uniquely to a continuous
homomorphism
\begin{equation}
 \iota_d:\widehat R_{\mathrm{ev}}^{\mathrm{BG}}
 \longrightarrow\widehat\cO_d.
\end{equation}
More precisely,
\begin{equation}
 \val_{\Phi_d}((q^2;q^2)_m)
 =\left\lfloor\frac{m}{d^\sharp}\right\rfloor.
\end{equation}

