[Thm Thm_MakNikPal of arXiv:2606.22183, 'Expected loss of quasi-arithmetic means of exchangeable random variables'] Let $I\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ be a nonempty open interval, $\alpha:(I-I)\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be an even error function, and $L:I\to \mathbb{R}$ be a function.
Then the following two assertions are equivalent:
 \begin{enumerate}
   \item[(i)] $L$ is strongly $\alpha$-convex, i.e., (equation help_strongly_alpha_convex_def of the paper) holds for all  $x,y\in I$ and $t\in[0,1]$.
   \item[(ii)] For all $x_0\in I$, there exists a constant $c_{x_0}\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
         \begin{align}
           L(x)\geqslant L(x_0) + c_{x_0}(x-x_0) + \alpha(x-x_0),\qquad x\in I.
         \end{align}
 \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:scalar-control-factorization of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] Let $S_h$ be any declared scalar summary measurable with respect to $\mathscr F_h$, and let
\begin{equation}
\Gamma_{h\to h'}:=G_{h\to h'}-c_{h\to h'}

\end{equation}
be the conditional net gain from continuing rather than stopping.  Relative to always stopping, define the one-step meta-control values
\begin{align}
V_{\rm meta}(\mathscr F_h)
&=\mathbb E[(\Gamma_{h\to h'})_+],\\
V_{\rm meta}(S_h)
&=\mathbb E\!\left[\left(\mathbb E[\Gamma_{h\to h'}\mid S_h]\right)_+\right].
\end{align}
If
\begin{equation}
a(S_h)=\mathbb E[(\Gamma_{h\to h'})_+\mid S_h],
\qquad
b(S_h)=\mathbb E[(-\Gamma_{h\to h'})_+\mid S_h],
\end{equation}
then the exact value of retaining the full legal shallow information rather than only $S_h$ is
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
V_{\rm meta}(\mathscr F_h)-V_{\rm meta}(S_h)
=
\mathbb E[\min\{a(S_h),b(S_h)\}].
}

\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
V_{\rm meta}(\mathscr F_h)=V_{\rm meta}(S_h)
\end{equation}
if and only if, conditional on $S_h$, the legal shallow states do not place positive probability on both $\Gamma_{h\to h'}>0$ and $\Gamma_{h\to h'}<0$ on any set of positive probability.  Equivalently, there exists an optimal \emph{\textsc{Stop}/\textsc{Continue}} meta-action that factorizes through $S_h$; ties at zero are value-neutral. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lmb of arXiv:2510.22701, 'Gaussian fluctuations in Mean Field Stable matchings'] Suppose that the density function $\rho$ satisfies condition (equation pd of the paper) and has a finite $r$-th moment for some $r>0$. Then, with $\kappa_n:=\ceil{\log^7 n}$ we have for $0< p< \min\{d, r/2\}$ that
     \begin{align}
         \operatorname{\mathbb E} \bcls{|\widetilde Y_k-\widehat Y_k|^p} &\leqslant \frac{o(1)}{(n-k)^{p/d}}, \qquad 1\leqslant k\leqslant m_n; \\

         \operatorname{\mathbb E} \bcls{|\widetilde Y_k-\widehat Y_k|^p}  &\leqslant    C z_n^{p},\qquad m_n+1\leqslant k\leqslant n,

     \end{align}
     where $z_n=\omega(n^{2/r})$ and $C$ depends on $p$ and $r$. Analogous upper bounds also hold for $\operatorname{\mathbb E} \bcls{|\widetilde Y^p_k-\widehat Y^p_k|}$. Furthermore, if there exists some $\zeta>0$ such that (equation rspeed of the paper) holds, then
     \begin{align}
          \operatorname{\mathbb E} \bcls{|\widetilde Y_k-\widehat Y_k|^p} &\leqslant \frac{C}{(n-k)^{p(1/d + (1\wedge\zeta/d))}}, \quad 1\leqslant k\leqslant m_n,
     \end{align}
     where $C$ depends on $p$ and $r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

