For any $\varepsilon\in (0,\widehat{r})$, there exist $T>0$ and $C>0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
u^{*}-u\le
Ce^{-2\alpha(t)} r^{-4}\log (re^{\alpha(t)/2})
\quad \text{in $B_{\widehat{r}}\setminus B_{\varepsilon}$}
\end{align*}
for any $r\in\left[\varepsilon,\widehat{r}\right)$ and
$t>\underline{T}$.

