[Lem Central Limit Theorem of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] [billingsley95]
    Let $(X_i)_{i \in {\mathbb N}}$ be a sequence of i.i.d random variables in $\mathbb{R}^d$ with $\Vert X_1\Vert$ being square-integrable and having a regular covariance matrix $C$. Then, we have for the sum $S_n:=\sum_{i=1}^n X_i$
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{S_n-n\,{\mathbb{E}}{X_1}}{\sqrt{n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} Y,
    \end{align*}
    where $L(Y)=\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)$ and $\mathcal{N}(\mu,C)$ denotes a $d$-dimensional normal distribution with mean $\mu$ and covariance matrix $C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem coefficent-MLE of arXiv:2508.13827, 'Surface sums in two-dimensional large-$N$ lattice Yang--Mills: Cancellations and explicit '] Suppose $\ell$ is a simple loop, $e$ is a simple-preserving edge of $\ell$, and $p=p(e)^{-1}$. Then, for $1\leq m\leq n$,\begin{equation}
             c(\ell^n\ominus_e^{n-m} p, K^{e,\ell}_{n,m}) =  c(\ell^n\ominus_e^{n-m+1} p, K^{e,\ell}_{n,m-1})- \sum_{i=1}^{m-1} c(\ell^i, K_{\ell^i}) c(\ell^{n-i}\ominus_e^{n-m} p, K^{e,\ell}_{n-i,m-i}).
         \end{equation}

