[Proposition prop:det4+det2 of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] Let ${\lambda}\in {\mathbb R}^{2n}$. Then we have
 \begin{align*}
 \sum_{\mathcal{A}\subset [\![2n ]\!],\, |\mathcal{A}|=n} \Delta (\mathcal{A})^4 \Delta (\mathcal{A}')^4&=2^{n} \Delta(\lambda)^2
\operatorname{Hf}\left(\frac{{\bf{1}}_{i\neq j}}{(\lambda_i-\lambda_j)^2}\right).
 \end{align*}
