[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2605.17296, 'Zero correlations and averaged fields of orthonormal Gaussian Functions'] Let $Z_{1},Z_{2},Z_{3}$ be i.i.d. standard complex normal random variables.
For $a,b,c,d>0$, 
\begin{equation}
\E\left[ \left\vert a|Z_{1}|^{2}-b|Z_{2}|^{2}\right\vert \right] 
= \frac{a^{2}+b^{2}}{a+b}. 

\end{equation}
\begin{align}
\lefteqn{\E\left[ |a|Z_{1}|^{2}-b|Z_{2}|^{2}|\cdot
|c|Z_{1}|^{2}-d|Z_{3}|^{2}|\right] }  \notag \\
& =bd\left( 2xy-(x+y)+\frac{2y^{2}}{(1+x)^{2}(1+x+y)}+\frac{2x^{2}}{(1+y)^{2}(1+x+y)}+1\right), 

\end{align}
where $x=a/b$ and $y=c/d$.

