[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $T = \E X  >0,$ and assume that $X \sim f \dd \pi_{T},$ where $f: \N \rightarrow (0, \infty) $ is log-concave. Then,
    \begin{displaymath}
        I ( T_{a}(X) | \pi_{aT} ) \le a^{2}T^{2} \frac{1}{1-a}
        +\frac{a^{3}T^{3}}{4} \Big( \frac{1}{1-a} \Big)^{2}.
    \end{displaymath}

