body:
[Lemma lem:global_matrix_meromorphicity of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] The 1-forms

\begin{equation}
\mathcal R\ni (z_k,w_k)\mapsto \boldsymbol{\mathcal{M}}_{i_1,j_1,i_2,j_2}\left(z_1,w_1;z_2,w_2\right) \frac{\,\mathrm{d} z_1 \,\mathrm{d} z_2}{z_2(z_2-z_1)}, 
\end{equation}
for $k=1,2$ are meromorphic with possible poles only at $p_\infty$, $p_0$, $q_\infty$, $q_0$, and $(z_1,w_1)=(z_2,w_2)$.

