[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumption {\rm\ref{A2}} holds. Then, for any $t\in \RR$ and $x\in\RR^n$, there exists $\mu^x_{t} \in \mathscr{P}_1(\RR^m)$ such that for any $s\le t$ and $y\in\RR^m$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{W}_1(\delta_{y}P^x_{s,t}, \mu^x_t)\le  C_1\left(1+|x|+|y|\right)e^{-\beta (t-s)},\quad\sup_{t\in\RR}\int_{\RR^m}|y|\mu^x_{t}(dy)\le  C_1(1+|x|),
\end{align}
where $\beta>0$ is defined in Lemma $\ref{L3.1}$, and $C_1>0$ is independent of $t$, $s$, $x\in \RR^n$ and $y\in \RR^m$. Moreover, there is a constant $C_2>0$ such that for any $x_1,x_2\in\mathbb{R}^n$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{t\in\mathbb{R}}\mathbb{W}_1(\mu^{x_1}_t, \mu^{x_2}_t)\le  C_2|x_1-x_2|.
\end{align}

