[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] Assume $\max_{1\le i \le k} p_i<1$. Then the quadratic variation $\langle M^{(f)} \rangle_\cdot$ satisfies 
    \begin{equation*}
        \frac{1}{n}\langle M^{(f)}\rangle_n \xrightarrow[n \to \infty]{\PP} 
        \sigma_f^2:=\pi(v_f).
    \end{equation*}

