body:
[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] Let $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ be a $\Lambda$-coalescent with death according to $D(dz)$ where $D(\{0\}) = 0$. Similarly, let $(\widehat{X}(t))_{t \geq 0}$ be a $\Lambda_*$-coalescent where $\Lambda_*(dz) = 2\Lambda(dz) + D(dz)$. If $X(0) = \widehat{X}(0)$, then there exists a coupling of $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ and $(\widehat{X}(t))_{t \geq 0}$ and a random time $t^* > 0$ a.s. such that

    \begin{align*}
        X(t)+1 \geq \widehat{X}(t),
    \end{align*}

    \noindent for all $t \leq t^*$.

