[Lemma global_existence of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Under the conditions of Theorem (theo:tied-SGD of the paper), let $C_*$ be the uniform spectral bound in Lemma (lemma:bound-tied-SGD of the paper). For every finite $T>0$ and every pair $C_*^2<\rho_-<\rho_+$, there exists a unique admissible trajectory $\bar\mu\in C([0,T];X_{\rho_-}^0)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\bar\mu(t)=\bar\mu(0)+\int_0^tV(\bar\mu(s))\,ds,
\qquad t\in[0,T],

\end{equation}
where the identity is understood in \(X_{\rho_+}^0\). Moreover,
\begin{equation}
q(\bar\mu(t))\succeq0,
\qquad t\in[0,T],
\end{equation}
and $|\bar\mu_\alpha(t)|\le C_*^{2|\alpha|}$
for every multi-index $\alpha$.

