body:
[Lemma lemXYY of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Let $u, v \in {\mathbb R}$ such that $u + iv \notin [x_{max}, +\infty[$. Then, we have:
\begin{equation}
{\textnormal{Re}}(Y^\pm(u + iv)) =u - \mu_2
\pm \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{\mu_2^2 - 2u  + \sqrt{(\mu_2^2 -2u)^2 + 4v^2}} 
\end{equation}

If $u, v \in {\mathbb R}$ satisfy $u + iv \notin [y_{max}, +\infty[$, then
\begin{equation}
{\textnormal{Re}}(X^\pm(u + iv)) = u - \mu_1 \pm  \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{\mu_1^2 - 2u + \sqrt{(\mu_1^2 - 2u)^2 + 4v^2}}.
\end{equation}
Let $\delta = \min(\mu_1, \mu_2) > 0$. Then, ${\textnormal{Re}}(Y^-(x)) < 0$ for all $x$ such that ${\textnormal{Re}}(x) < x_{max} + \delta, x \notin [x_{max}, +\infty[$. Similarly, ${\textnormal{Re}}(X^-(y)) < 0$ for all $y$ such that ${\textnormal{Re}}(y) < y_{max} + \delta, y \notin [y_{max}, +\infty[$.

