[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] If $P\sim\operatorname{Pois}(\lambda)$ and $G\sim\operatorname{Gamma}(n,1)$, then
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}(P< n)=\mathbb{P}(P\le n-1)=\mathbb{P}(G>\lambda).
\end{align*}

