[Lemma lemma_exit_exp of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] There are constants $c_3>0$ and $C_2 \geq 1$ such that for all $\delta \in (0,1]$ and all $\zeta >0$ satisfying $2\delta \zeta^{1-2\gamma} \leq 1$, for all $n \in \mathbb{N}_0$ and $\mathbb{P} \in \mathscr{M}_{\gamma,\delta}(I_n)$, 
\begin{equation*} \mathbb{P} ( \tau_{a_{n-1}} \wedge \tau_{a_{n+1}}  > m a_n^{2-2\gamma}) \leq e^{-c_3 m} \end{equation*}
for all $m \in \mathbb{N}$, and 
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{E}[\tau_{a_{n-1}} \wedge \tau_{a_{n+1}}] \leq C_2 a_n^{2-2\gamma}.
\end{equation*}

