body:
[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.30089, 'On the Coefficients of Hurwitz-Type Matrix Polynomials'] Let \(A_0,\ldots,A_n\) be the coefficients of the HTM polynomial
\(\mathbf f_n\) defined by \eqref{hup01}, and suppose that
\(\mathbf f_n\) admits the representation \eqref{hupfqp}.
Furthermore, let \(P_{k,m}\) and \(Q_{k,m}\), \(k=1,2\), be as in
Definition~\ref{def2p}. Then the following identities hold.

If \(n=2m\), \(m\geq1\), then
\begin{equation}
A_{n-k}
=
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle
\frac{(-1)^{m+j}}{j!}
\left(P_{1,m}^{*}\right)^{(j)}(0),
&
k=2j,\quad 0\leq j\leq m,
\\[2ex]
\displaystyle
-\frac{(-1)^{m+j}}{j!}
\left(Q_{1,m}^{*}\right)^{(j)}(0),
&
k=2j+1,\quad 0\leq j\leq m-1.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

If \(n=2m+1\), \(m\geq0\), then
\begin{equation}
A_{n-k}
=
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle
\frac{(-1)^{m+j}}{j!}
\left(Q_{2,m}^{*}\right)^{(j)}(0),
&
k=2j,\quad 0\leq j\leq m,
\\[2ex]
\displaystyle
\frac{(-1)^{m+j}}{j!}
\left(P_{2,m}^{*}\right)^{(j)}(0),
&
k=2j+1,\quad 0\leq j\leq m.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

