[Theorem thm:soft_ogp of arXiv:2412.03511, 'Near-optimal shattering in the Ising pure $p$-spin and \\ rarity of solutions returned by '] If $\beta \in (\bar{\beta}_{d}, \beta_c)$, there exists $\varepsilon>0$, $c>0$ and $0\le \underline{q}<\overline{q} \le 1$ depending on $\beta$ and $\xi$ such that for all $\tau \in [0,1]$, 
  \begin{equation}
     \operatorname{\mathbb{E}} \mu_{\beta,\bm{G}}\Big(\Big\{\bm{\sigma} : \exists\, \bm{\sigma}' \in S_{(1-\varepsilon)\beta}(\bm{G}_\tau),\,\,\textup{s.t.}\,\,  \underline{q} \le \langle \bm{\sigma},\bm{\sigma}'\rangle/N  \le \overline{q} \Big\}\Big) \le e^{-cN}\,.
\end{equation}

In the case $\tau = 1$, if $\beta \in (\bar{\beta}_{d}, \beta_c)$ then for any $\bm{\sigma} \in \{-1,+1\}^N$,
\begin{equation}
\operatorname{\mathbb{P}}\Big( \exists\, \bm{\sigma}' \in S_{\beta}(\bm{G}'),\,\,\textup{s.t.}\,\,  \langle \bm{\sigma},\bm{\sigma}'\rangle/N  \ge \underline{q} \Big) \le e^{-cN}\,.
\end{equation} 

Finally in the case of the pure $p$-spin $\xi(x)=x^p$, for $\varepsilon'>0$, if $\beta \in \big((1+\varepsilon')\sqrt{(2\log p)/p},\\ \sqrt{2\log 2} \big)$, there exists $p_0$, $\delta>0$ and $c'>0$ all depending only on $\varepsilon'$ such that for all $p \ge p_0$, the bounds~(equation eq:soft_ogp of the paper) and~(equation eq:tauequal1 of the paper) hold with $\underline{q} = 1 - \delta/p$, $\overline{q} = 1- 1/p^{1+\delta}$ and $\varepsilon = c'\sqrt{(\log p)/ p}$.

