[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Recall notation \eqref{Rn}. For $k=1,2\dots,$ $\alpha>0$, $u>-\alpha$, $ v< u$, $|v|<\alpha$   and $t_1,\dots,t_k \ge 0$,  the following integrals:
\begin{equation}
    L_k = \int_{(0,\infty)^k} \tfrac{ \prod_{i=1}^k x_i^{\alpha+v+2t_i-1} }{ \big(R_k(\vv x)\big)^{u+v} (1+x_k)^{\alpha-v+2t_k} \prod_{i=1}^{k-1} (1+x_i)^{2\alpha+2t_i} } \,\mathrm{d}x_1 \dots \mathrm{d}x_k
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    H_k = \int_{(0,\infty)^k} \tfrac{ y_1^{u-v-1} \left( \prod_{j=2}^k y_j^{\alpha-v+2t_{j-1}-1} \right) \prod_{j=1}^{k} \big(R_j(\vv y)\big)^{2t_{j+1}-2t_j} }{  (1+y_1)^{\alpha+u} \prod_{j=2}^k (1+y_j)^{2\alpha+2t_{j-1}} } \,\mathrm{d}y_1 \dots \mathrm{d}y_k,
\end{equation}
 are finite and equal.

