[Lemma l.convex_Phi of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Let $(L,\alpha)$ be a decomposition of some $q\in \mathcal Q_\infty$, let $\Phi$ be associated with $(L,\alpha)$, and let $\phi$ be the terminal condition of $\Phi$ given as in~(equation e.phi=initial of the paper).
Then, the following holds:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  If $P_1$ is not a Dirac mass, then there exists $z\in\mathbb{R}^{D}$ such that
    \begin{align}
        z^\intercal \nabla^2 \phi(x)z >0,\qquad\forall x\in\mathbb{R}^{D}.
    \end{align}


    \item

    If $\supp P_1$ spans $\mathbb{R}^{D}$, then~(equation e.znabla^2Phi(x)z>0 of the paper) holds for every non-zero $z\in \mathbb{R}^{D}$.

    \item  For every $z\in \mathbb{R}^{D}$ satisfying~(equation e.znabla^2Phi(x)z>0 of the paper), it holds that $z^\intercal \nabla^2 \Phi(t,x)z >0$ for every $(t,x)\in [0,1]\times\mathbb{R}^{D}$.
\end{enumerate}

