[Prop pr:decay_1 of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] If $\alpha_0$ is sufficiently small, then there exist constants $0 < \rho < 1$ and $C > 0$ such that for any $u[0]$ with $V_{\alpha_0}(u[0]) < \infty$, we have 
	\begin{equs}

		\mathbb{E} V_{\alpha_0}\big(u[T\wedge t_0]\big) &\leq \rho V_{2\alpha_0}(u[0]) + C\;, \\

		\sup_{a \leq t_0} V_{2\alpha_0}\big(u[T\wedge a]\big) &\leq 2V_{\alpha_0}(u[0]) + C\;.
	\end{equs}

