[Corollary C_TP_sizes of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Let $W$ be a witness graph of order $\sigma$ and cost $\kappa$, 
and let $T_1,...,T_\omega$ be its maximal tree parts. Then,
\begin{equation}

\sum_{s=1}^{\omega}|V(T_i)| \leqslant \sigma + O(\kappa)\,.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:hardy of arXiv:2411.13430, 'Optimal subelliptic super-Poincar\'e and isoperimetric inequalities on stratified Lie grou'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm1 of the paper), the measure $\mu$ satisfies the Hardy inequality 
    \begin{equation}      
        \int \frac{\left\lvert f \right\rvert^q}{\left\lvert x \right\rvert^q}d\mu \lesssim \int \left\lvert \nabla f \right\rvert^qd\mu + \int \left\lvert f \right\rvert^qd\mu
    \end{equation}
    for each $q \in [1, 2)$, and the Caffarelli-Kohn-Nirenberg inequality
    \begin{equation}
        \int \left\lvert f \right\rvert^qd\mu \lesssim \left(\int \left\lvert f \right\rvert^q\left\lvert x \right\rvert^{q\alpha}d\mu\right)^{1/(\alpha+1)} \left(\int \left\lvert \nabla f \right\rvert^qd\mu + \int \left\lvert f \right\rvert^qd\mu\right)^{\alpha/(\alpha+1)} 
    \end{equation} 
    for each $q \in [1, 2]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lemma reduction conv of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Fix a symmetric, stochastic $n\times n$ matrix $\ensuremath{\mathcal K}$, and let $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ denote its irreducible components. Fix \(m \in (-1,1)^{\mathcal{A}}\). 
Suppose there exist a positive constant \(\varepsilon := \varepsilon(m,\mathcal{K})\) and a positive integer \(u := u(m,\mathcal{K})\) such that
\begin{equation}
    \Phi^0_u(p_1,\dots,p_{2^u})(\t) \ge \varepsilon, \quad \forall \t\in\O,
\end{equation}
for every choice of  \( (p_1, \ldots, p_{2^u})\) such that $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p_i)=m$. 
Then,  there exist constants \(t_0>0\) and \(\varepsilon_0>0\) depending only on $m,\ensuremath{\mathcal K},J$,  such that for all $p\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}(\O)$ with $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p)=m$, the solution \(p_t\) of (equation non-linear rqs of the paper) satisfies 
\begin{equation}
p_t( \tau)\ge \varepsilon_0, \quad \forall\tau\in\Omega\,, \;\forall\,t\ge t_0\,.
\end{equation}

