body:
[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] The map
		\begin{equation}
			q_B:\mathbb F_2(\pLie)\longrightarrow\mathbb N_{G,K},
			\qquad
			q_B(X,\Omega)=(X,B\Omega),
		\end{equation}
		is a surjective Carnot group homomorphism with central kernel $\ker B$. Its differential is the identity on the horizontal layer, so it is a submetry. Equip all linear spaces with the Lebesgue measures induced by their fixed inner products, and let $\mathrm d\sigma_Z$ be the induced Hausdorff measure on the affine fiber $B^{-1}(Z)$. Then
		\begin{equation}
			p_t^0(X,Z)
			=
			\det(BB^*)^{-1/2}
			\int_{B^{-1}(Z)}q_t^{\mathrm{free}}(X,\Omega)\,
			\mathrm d\sigma_Z(\Omega).
		\end{equation}

