[Corollary cor:BLPP-one-point of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] For $k = 1$, the Fredholm determinant
$F_{t,a,n} = \det(I - K_{t,a,n})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
\bigl[D_t - \tfrac{1}{2}D_a^2\bigr]
F_{t,a,n+1} \cdot F_{t,a,n} = 0.
\end{equation}

