[Lemma lem:E of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d > 8$, $L \ge L_3$, and $m(p) L$ be sufficiently small.
For any $j \in \{1, \dots, d\}$, we have
\begin{align}

\abs{ \nabla_j \hat A_\mu ^{(m)}(k) } &\lesssim L^2 (\abs k + m ) e^{mL}
	\qquad (m \ge 0) , \\

\abs{ \nabla_j \hat F_p ^{(m)}(k) } &\lesssim L^2 (\abs k + m )  e^{mL}
	\qquad (m \in [0, m(p)]) .
\end{align}
Also, given any $\varepsilon \in (0,1]$ such that $\varepsilon <d-8$,
if $m \in [0, m(p)]$ and $\tilde{b}(m) \le 3$ then
\begin{align} 
\abs{ \nabla^\gamma \hat E_p ^{(m)} (k) }
\lesssim  \beta L^{2+\varepsilon} (\abs k  + m)^{2 + \varepsilon - \abs \gamma }  e^{mL}
	\qquad (\abs \gamma \le 2).
\end{align}
All constants are independent of $\mu,p,m,L$.

