body:
[Proposition 27 (Projection) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Suppose that $\mathscr{K} \subset \mathscr{L}(N, d)$ is nonempty and satisfies Assumption \ref{ass:projection}. Then, for any $L \in \mathscr{L}(N, d)$ there exists $\hat{L} \in \mathscr{K}$ such that
\begin{equation} 
\dist_{\mathrm{AW}}(L, \hat{L}) = \inf_{M \in \mathscr{K}} \dist_{\mathrm{AW}}(L, M).
\end{equation}
In fact, we have
\begin{equation} 
\argmin_{M \in \mathscr{K}} \dist_{\mathrm{AW}}(L, M) = \left[ \argmin_{M \in \mathscr{K}} \|L - M\|_{\mathrm{F}} \right],
\end{equation}
where $[\cdot]$ denotes the equivalence class in $\dist_{\mathrm{AW}}$. In particular, the solution in $\tilde{\mathscr{L}}(N, d)$ is unique.

