[Theorem CLTcoefficients of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] In addition to the assumptions of Theorem~(CLT of the paper), assume that $G_X$ is proximal and that $\mathds{E} \big[\sup_{0 \le s \le 1} M(X_s)^\epsilon\big]<\infty$ for some $\epsilon>0$. Then 
	the CLT (equation eq:CLT:theorem of the paper) holds for $F(a)=|\langle ya,z \rangle |$ as well, for any $y,z \in \R^d$ with $\|y \|=\|z \|=1$.\\
	In particular, choosing $y=e_i$ and $z=e_j$ as unit vectors, there exist $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $\sigma^2>0$ such that 
			\begin{equation*}
			\frac{\log X_t^{(i,j)} - t \lambda}{\sqrt{t}} \stackrel{d}{\to} \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2), \quad t\to \infty.
		\end{equation*}

