[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2506.18063, 'Reduced critical branching processes in non-favorable random environment \thanks{ This wor'] If Conditions B1 and B2 are\ valid, $k\sim \theta
m=\theta (n-r)$ for some $\theta >0,$ then
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{z\rightarrow \infty }\lim_{n\gg k\sim \theta m\rightarrow \infty }
\mathbf{P}\left( S_{r}>za_{k}|\mathcal{R}(ta_{k},n)\right) =0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

