[Definition of arXiv:2609.00233, 'A survey on mapping class groups of 3-manifolds'] We define
\begin{multline*}
\Diff^+(M,(B_h),(T_i),(M_j)) \coloneqq \\
\{ f \in \Diff^+(M,T) \mid f(B_h)=B_h, f(T_i)=T_i, f(M_j)=M_j \text{ for every $h,i,j$} \}
\end{multline*}

[Definition def:centered-capped-arrays-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] For \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), 
set \(m=m_{\xi,d}\).
Define the stopped centered capped prefix array by
\[
\widehat F^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}_{\xi,d,n}
=
\sum_{\ell=0}^{m-1}
\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell).
\]
For \(L>m\), define the stopped centered capped post-bin partial sum by
\[
\widehat F^{\mathrm{post,cap}}_{\xi,d,n,L}
=
\sum_{\ell=m}^{L-1}
\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell).
\]
The corresponding unstopped arrays \(F^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}_{\xi,d,n}\) and \(F^{\mathrm{post,cap}}_{\xi,d,n,L}\) are obtained by removing the factors \(\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}\).

