[Definition 15 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] Let $\pi:\mathcal{A}\rightarrow M$ be a Lie algebroid with anchor map $\rho$.
    An $\mathcal{A}$-path is a $C^1$ curve $a: I \to \mathcal{A}$ such that:
    \begin{equation*}
    \rho(a(t)) = \frac{d}{dt} \pi(a(t)).
    \end{equation*}

