body:
[Theorem th4.1 of arXiv:2511.07173, '\bf Mean-field backward stochastic Volterra integral equations: well-posedness and related'] \rm

Let (ass3.1 of the paper) be in force and $g$ is Lipschitz continuous with respect to  $(\mu,\nu)$ in 1-Wasserstein distance.
Let $(Y^{N,i}(\cdot),Z^{N,i,j}(\cdot,\cdot))_{1\leqslant j\leqslant N}$, $(\overline{Y}^{i}(\cdot),\overline{Z}^i(\cdot,\cdot))$ be the solutions of   Eq. ((1.3 of the paper)) and  Eq. ((5.2 of the paper)), respectively. Then,  for  $1<p<2$,
\begin{equation*}
		\begin{aligned}
			&\ \mathbb{E}\bigg[\int_0^T|  Y^{N,i}(t)- \overline{Y}^i(t)|^pdt

			+ \int_0^T\(\int_t^T \sum\limits_{j=1}^N|Z^{N,i,j}(t,s)- \delta_{ij}\overline{Z}^i(t,s)|^2ds\)^\frac{p}{2} dt\bigg] \nonumber\\
			   &\leqslant C  \mathbb{E}\int_0^T  {\cal W}_p^p(\mu^N(t), \overline{\mu}(t))dt
              +C  \mathbb{E}\int_0^T\int_t^T{\cal W}_p^p(\nu^N(t,r), \overline{\nu}(t,r))drdt.
		\end{aligned}
	\end{equation*}

