body:
[Lemma lem:limitingresolventboundedness of arXiv:2608.11603, 'Continuous-time directed polymers to the Critical SHF via moments'] {}
	Fix $\alpha = ij,\alpha' = kl \in \mathsf{Pair}[\![n]\!]$ such that $\alpha \neq \alpha'$. Then, for all sufficiently $\lambda \gtrsim e^{\theta_{\star}} + 1$, the limiting operators defined in equation~(equation eqn:defn_limiting_operators of the paper) satisfy the following norm bounds:
	\begin{subequations}
		\begin{align}
		\normop{\mathcal{G}^{\ast}_{\alpha}(\lambda)} 
		& \lesssim \lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}}  \\
		\normop{\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}(\lambda)}
		& \lesssim \lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}}  \\
		\normop{\mathcal{G}_{\alpha\alpha'}(\lambda)}
		& \lesssim 1                \\
		\normop{\diag{\theta_{\star}}{\alpha}(\lambda)}  
		& \lesssim (\log\lambda - \theta_{\star})^{-1}    \, \, .
		\end{align}
	\end{subequations}
	Moreover, with these norm bounds, the sum in equation~(equation eqn:limiting_resolvent of the paper) converges absolutely in norm.

