[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2605.17296, 'Zero correlations and averaged fields of orthonormal Gaussian Functions'] For every $z_0 \in \C$, 
\begin{equation*}
\bigl(X_n(z+z_0)\bigr)_{n\ge 0}
\inlaw 
\bigl(\lambda(z_0,z) X_n(z)\bigr)_{n\ge 0}, 
\end{equation*}
where 
$\lambda(z_0,z) = e^{- i \Im (z_0\bar z)}$.

[Lem lem-gf-pos of arXiv:2411.06301, 'Inverting the operation of conditioning a branching process on extinction'] Let $X = \{X(n)\}_{n\in\mathbbm N_0}$ be a $d$-type branching process which is positive regular and non-singular (Definition~(def-bp-basic of the paper)). There exists $N\in\mathbbm N$ such that for each $k,j  \in \{1,\dots,d\}$, 
\begin{equation}  
p_{k,j}(N) > 0 \quad \text{where} \quad
p_{k,j}(N) := 
\begin{cases}
\mathbbm P_k\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[X_j(N) \geq 1 \: \text{and} \: X_k(N) \geq 1   \aftergroup\egroup\originalright]  ,\quad & k \not= j  \\
\mathbbm P_k\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[X_k(N) \geq 2   \aftergroup\egroup\originalright]  ,\quad & k = j  . 
\end{cases}  
\end{equation}

