body:
[Proposition 4 (Polarized identity and weighted-Poincar\'e deficit) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] In the regular moment-map model,
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \Gamma_{\rm tr}(A,B)
  =
  \Gamma_{\rm quad}(A,B)
  -3\mathsf T(A,B)
  +\mathsf U(A,B)}
  \tag{3.11}
\end{equation}
for every \(A,B\in\mathsf S_n\).  Moreover, the bilinear form
\begin{equation}
  \mathsf D
  :=
  4\mathsf T-\Gamma_{\rm quad}
  \tag{3.12}
\end{equation}
is positive-semidefinite, and
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \Gamma_{\rm tr}
  =
  \frac14\Gamma_{\rm quad}
  +\mathsf U
  -\frac34\mathsf D.}
  \tag{3.13}
\end{equation}

[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2607.19873, 'Local limit theorem for the operator norm of products of random matrices'] Assume that $\Gamma_{\mu}$ is strongly irreducible and that $\mu$ admits a finite exponential moment \eqref{Exponential-moment}. 
Then, there exist constants $\ee, c >0$ such that for any $n \geq 1$, 
\begin{align*}
\bb P \left( \left\| \frac{g_n \cdots g_1}{\| g_n \cdots g_1 \|} - \frac{\pi_{g_n \cdots g_1} }{\| \pi_{g_n \cdots g_1} \|}  \right\| > e^{- \ee n} \right) \leq c e^{-\ee n}. 
\end{align*}

