[Lemma lem:approx_dual of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}_{tem}^+)$, $p>2$, such that (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper) holds and let $a$ be defined as in (equation eq:def_d of the paper). Let $Y^n$ be as above, independent of $X$. Then there exists a time $T_0>0$ depending only on $\langle \mu,1\rangle$ and $a$ such that for all $t \leq T \leq T_0$  we have
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			&\mathbb{E}\Big[(-1)^{J_t^n}\exp\Big(-\langle Y_t^n, X_{T-t}\rangle-a \int_0^t\langle Y_s^n, 1 \rangle ds\Big)\Big] = \mathbb{E}\Big[\exp(-\langle Y_0,X_T\rangle)\Big]\\
			& + \mathbb{E}\Big[ \int_0^t(-1)^{J_{s-}^n} \exp\Big(-\langle Y_{s-}^n, X_{T-s}\rangle-a \int_0^s\langle Y_r^n, 1 \rangle dr\Big) \Big(\langle Y_{s-}^n, h(X_{T-s})\rangle - \langle Y_{s-}^n, h_n(X_{T-s})\rangle \Big) ds\Big].
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}

