body:
[Lemma 63 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $A : \bbr^m \to \bbr^{(m \times d) \times d}$ be the linear operator given by
\begin{align*}
A_{ij,k}(v) =
\begin{cases}
v_i, & \text{if $j=k$,}
\\ 0, & \text{otherwise,}
\end{cases}
\quad \text{for all $v \in \bbr^m$,}
\end{align*}
for all $i=1,\ldots,m$ and $j,k = 1,\ldots,d$. Then we have
\begin{align*}
v \otimes w = A(v) \cdot w \quad \text{for all $v \in \bbr^m$ and $w \in \bbr^d$.}
\end{align*}

