[Theorem thm:product of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $(D,\delta,\Pi)$ satisfy Assumptions~(ass:chain of the paper)--(ass:ortho of the paper). Let $F\in\Dom(D)$ and $u\in\Dom(\delta)$. Assume the pointwise product $Fu:\Omega\to\mathcal{H}$ (given by $(Fu)(\omega):=F(\omega)u(\omega)$) satisfies:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\arabic*)]
\item $Fu\in L^2(\Omega;\mathcal{H})$,
\item $Fu\in\Dom(\delta)$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
\begin{equation}
\delta(Fu) = F\delta(u) - \inner{DF}{u}_\mathcal{H} \qquad \text{in } L^2(\Omega).
\end{equation}

[Prop 11 of arXiv:2609.02173, 'Bounding Selmer Groups of Superelliptic Jacobians via Class Groups'] For every finite place \(v\) of \(K\), one has
	\begin{enumerate}
