[Lemma lem:recursive_def_rk of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] For any $k\ge 0,$ the following holds,
    \begin{align}
    &r_k(R)\underset{R\to \infty} \longrightarrow \infty. \\[0.8ex]
    &\pi_{^{r_{k+1}(R),R}}^{_{(2)}}= \pi_{r_{k+1}(R)} \pi_{^{r_{k}(R),R}}^{_{(2)}}\;\text{ for all large $R$}.\\[1.2ex]
    &r_k(R)\lesssim r_{k}(2R).
\end{align}

