[Lemma lem:concentration of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:replacement of the paper), for any $z \in \mathbb{C}^+$ , there exists $C, c > 0$ so that
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathbb{P} \left( \left|s_{\tilde X_n'}(z) - \mathbb{E} [s_{\tilde X_n'}(z)] \right| \geq C \frac{t}{\sqrt{n}} \right) \leq C e^{-c t^2}  
    \end{equation}
    for any $t > 0$. 
    The same bound holds for $s_{\tilde Y_n'}$.

[Lemma one-step_Z_to_T of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ for some $\alpha, K > 0$. Then there exists $C, c > 0$ depending on $(K, \alpha, d)$ such that for any $L \in \mathbb N^+$ and any $x \in \mathbb{T}^d_L$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \frac{c}{|o - x|^{\alpha + d}} \le Q_L(o, x) \le \frac{C}{|o - x|^{\alpha + d}}.
    \end{align}

