[Lem of arXiv:2609.03848, 'The mean-field limit of the Schr\"{o}dinger-Lohe model\\ and emergent dynamics'] \label{L-B.1}
Let $t\mapsto X(t,\cdot)$ be a continuous and bounded, time-dependent vector field on $(\mathbf{S}\mathfrak{H})^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$ that is Lipschitz continuous on $\mathfrak{H}^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$ uniformly in $t\in \mathbb R$, and let
$\mathcal{S}(t,t_0)$ be the flow generated by the vector field $X$ on $(\mathbf{S}\mathfrak{H})^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$. For each initial datum $F^{0}\in\mathcal{P}((\mathbf{S}\mathfrak{H})^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N)$, we set
\begin{equation}\label{CharFla}
F(t,\cdot):=\mathcal{S}(t,0)\#F^{0}\,.
\end{equation}
Then $F$ is a weak solution of the Liouville equation on $(\mathbf{S}\mathfrak{H})^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$:
\begin{equation} \label{Liouville}
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle \partial_tF+\operatorname{div}(FX)=0, \quad t > 0, \\
\displaystyle F{\big |}_{t=0}=F^{0}.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

