body:
[Corollary 26 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] For every $T>0$, there are $r>0$, $L<\infty$, and $\varepsilon_*>0$ such
that
\begin{align*}
 \mathcal U_r=\{(w,\iota(\eta)):\norm{(w,\eta)}_{E_b}<r\}
\end{align*}
is $d_L$ small for $P_T$, where
\begin{align*}
 d_L\bigl((w,[\rho]),(\widetilde w,[\widetilde\rho])\bigr)
 =1\wedge L\left(\norm{w-\widetilde w}_{H^b}+d_{\PP}([\rho],[\widetilde\rho])\right).
\end{align*}
Thus, for every $z,z'\in\mathcal U_r$,
\begin{align}
 W_{d_L}\bigl(P_T(z,\cdot),P_T(z',\cdot)\bigr)\le1-\varepsilon_*.
\end{align}

