[Thm area min of arXiv:2512.12796, 'Symmetrization and the Planar Skorokhod Embedding Problem'] Let $\mu\in\mathfrak{M}$. Then for every $s\in(0,1)$
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{E}_{s}(U^{G}_{\mu})\leq\mathcal{E}_{s}(U)
\end{equation}
for any simply connected domain $U$ in $\mathscr{B}(\mu)$. In other
words 
\begin{equation}
\inf_{U:s.c.d\in\mathscr{B}(\mu)}\mathcal{E}_{s}(U)=\mathcal{E}_{s}(U^{G}_{\mu}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:Xconvergencetwosided of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] There exist random variables $\hat{X}_\infty$ and $\hat{X}^+_\infty$ depending on $\hat\eta$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \hat{X}^+_\infty&=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \hat{X}^+_n:=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}^W_0(W[1,\infty)\cap\hat{\eta}[1,n]=\varnothing\mid \hat\eta),\\
        \hat{X}_\infty&=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \hat{X}_n:=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}(\log n)^{1/3}\mathbb{P}^W_0(W[1,\infty)\cap\hat{\eta}[0,n]=\varnothing\mid\hat\eta)
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
almost surely and in $L^p$ for every $p<3$.

