body:
[Lemma L: squeeze lemma of arXiv:2511.11036, 'Analysis of a class of Recursive Distributional Equations Including the Resistance of the '] Assume that $\mathcal{F}$ and $Q$ satisfy assumptions (equation A: elliptic of the paper) and (equation A: lipschitz of the paper) and fix $F_{\text{in}} \in CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$.  Suppose that $\{F^{(N),+}_{\text{in}}\}$ and $\{F^{(N),-}_{\text{in}}\}$ are two sequences of continuous functions in $CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$ such that
		\begin{gather}
			F^{(N-1),-}_{\text{in}} \leq F^{(N),-}_{\text{in}} \leq F_{\text{in}} \leq F^{(N),+}_{\text{in}} \leq F^{(N-1),+}_{\text{in}} \quad \text{pointwise for each} \, \, N,  \\
			\lim_{N \to +\infty} F^{(N),+}_{\text{in}} = \lim_{N \to +\infty} F^{(N),-}_{\text{in}} = F_{\text{in}} \quad \text{vaguely.} 
		\end{gather}
	Let $\{F^{(N),+}\}$ and $\{F^{(N),-}\}$ be the (continuous) viscosity solutions of (equation E: initial value problem appendix of the paper) with respective initial data $\{F^{(N),+}_{\text{in}}\}$ and $\{F^{(N),-}_{\text{in}}\}$.  If the limit of the two sequences coincides, that is, if 
		\begin{align*}
			F := \lim_{N \to +\infty} F^{(N),+} = \lim_{N \to +\infty} F^{(N),-} \quad \text{pointwise in} \, \, \mathbb{R} \times (0,+\infty),
		\end{align*}
	then the maximal subsolution and minimal supersolution of (equation E: initial value problem appendix of the paper) with initial datum $F_{\text{in}}$ are equal in $\mathbb{R} \times (0,+\infty)$ and, in particular, they both equal the limit $F$.

