[Lemma lem:independent_xi of arXiv:2511.17101, 'Central limit theorem for the range of critical branching random walk'] For any $i\in \mathbb Z, k_1\ge 0$. The random variable 
$\xi_i^{k_1}$  is independent of
\begin{align}

\sigma\setof{(\xi_j^{k_2}\1_{\{\mathrm{dist}(u_i,u_j)=m\}}, \mathrm{dist}(u_i,u_j))}{j>i,k_2\ge 0,m\ge k_1+k_2} .
\end{align}

