body:
[Theorem thm:chen of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $x$ be a bounded-variation path and $s\le u\le t$. Then
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,t}=\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,u}\otimes\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{u,t}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the signature is a monoid homomorphism from chronological concatenation of paths to tensor multiplication.

