[Lemma 42 of arXiv:2609.01826, 'An extension theory for fully fractional Schr\"odinger equations with memory'] Let $b>0$ and $0<\Re \mu<1$. Then
\begin{equation}
\int_0^\infty y^{\mu-1} e^{\pm i by} dy = \frac{\G(\mu)}{b^\mu} e^{\pm i\frac{\mu \pi}{2}}.
\end{equation}

