[Lem edge-measured-partialE of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] Let $K_0\subseteq (\partial G)^2$ (resp.~$K_1\subseteq (\partial G)^2$) be the set of $(f,g)\in(\partial G)^2$ such that there is a sequence of same-level edges (resp. inter-level edges) $x_ny_n$ in which $\iota(x_n)\to f$ and $\iota(y_n)\to g$ as $n \to \infty$. Then, $K_0$ and $K_1$ are compact subsets of $(\partial G)^2$ and 
		\begin{equation}

			\partial E = \partial G \cup \pi \left(\edge{0}{} (K_0\times [0,1])\right) \cup \pi\left(\edge{1}{}(K_1\times [0,1])\right),
		\end{equation}
		where $\pi:\mathrm{Lip}_1\to \mathrm{Lip}_1^0$ is the projection $f\mapsto f-f(\mathbf{o})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

