[Proposition prop:pde-u-v of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Let $u=\frac{1}{2}(y_1+y_2)$ and $v=\frac{1}{2}(y_2-y_1)$. Then for $j=1,2$, $F^{(j)}(y_1,y_2,x_1,x_2,x_3)$ satisfies the following pair of second-order PDEs:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\left(\frac{\kappa}{4}(\partial_{uu}+\partial_{vv})+\frac{1+\frac{\kappa-6}{2}}{v}\partial_v+\sum_{i=1}^3\left(\frac{4(x_i-u)\partial_{x_i}}{(x_i-u)^2-v^2}-\frac{2h}{(x_i-u+v)^2}-\frac{2h}{(x_i-u-v)^2}\right)\right)F=0,\\
\left(\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{uv}-\frac{1-\frac{\kappa-6}{2}}{v}\partial_u+\sum_{i=1}^3\left(\frac{4v\partial_{x_i}}{(x_i-u)^2-v^2}+\frac{2h}{(x_i-u+v)^2}-\frac{2h}{(x_i-u-v)^2}\right)\right)F=0.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

