[Lemma 3 (Complete exclusion region) of arXiv:2607.20680, 'Exact Scale--Shape Factorization of the Typical Poisson--Voronoi Cell Volume in Arbitrary '] Fix $\bfx\in\mathcal A_{d,k}$ and put
  \[
    P=P(\bfx).
  \]
A nonzero additional nucleus $y$ changes $P$ on a set with nonempty interior if and only if
  \begin{equation*}
    y\in\operatorname{int}\Delta(P).
  \end{equation*}
Consequently,
  \begin{equation}

    \mathbb P
    \{
      \PP\cap\operatorname{int}\Delta(P)=\varnothing
    \}
    =
    \exp[-\lambda Q(\bfx)] .
  \end{equation}

