body:
[Proposition 10 (Uniform local kinetic estimates) of arXiv:2608.08177, 'Uniform-in-Time Smoluchowski--Kramers Approximation\\ in Total Variation for Fractional SD'] Let \Cref{ass:smooth,ass:dissipative} hold.  Fix
$\gamma\in(1/2,H)$ and $p\ge2$.  There exist $\mu_0\in(0,1]$ and $C<\infty$
such that
\begin{align}
 \sup_{0<\mu\le\mu_0}\sup_{t\ge0}
 \norm{Z_t^\mu}_{L^p}&\le C,
 \\
 \sup_{0<\mu\le\mu_0}\sup_{t\ge0}
 \norm{U_t^\mu}_{L^p}&\le C\mu^{\gamma-1},
 \\
 \sup_{0<\mu\le\mu_0}\sup_{k\in\mathbb N_0}
 \norm{[Z^\mu]_{\gamma;[k,k+1]}}_{L^p}&\le C.

\end{align}
The same conclusions hold for random initial data having sufficiently high
moments, uniformly in $\mu$.

