[Lemma atechone of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] For non-commutative variables $a,r$, define 
\begin{align*}
\Delta\left(a,r\right)
  &:=2\mathfrak{s}[(z-a)r]-r^2,
\end{align*}
where $\mathfrak{s}$ denotes the symmetrization operator. Then, for all $q\geq 1$,
\begin{align*}
g\left(a+r\right)
  &=g\left(a+r\right)\left(\Delta\left(a,r\right) g (a)\right)^{q}+\sum_{j=0}^{q-1}g\left(a\right)\left(\Delta\left(a,r\right)g\left(a\right)\right)^j,
\end{align*}

