[Proposition prop:master-common-diagonal of arXiv:2608.11084, 'Sharp Frobenius-Norm Concentration for Sample Moment Tensors'] Let \(X_1,\ldots,X_N\) be i.i.d. copies of a centered sub-Gaussian random
vector \(X\in\mathbb R^d\) with covariance matrix \(\Sigma\) and
sub-Gaussian constant \(K\). Let \(p\ge2\) be an integer. Then, for every
\(q\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\|
\bigg(
\sum_{i=1}^N
\big\|
X_i^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\big\|_{\mathsf F}^2
\bigg)^{1/2}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\|_{L_q}
\lesssim_p
K^p
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(
\sqrt N\,\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma)^{p/2}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if \(X\) is Gaussian, then
\begin{equation}
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\|
\bigg(
\sum_{i=1}^N
\big\|
X_i^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\big\|_{\mathsf F}^2
\bigg)^{1/2}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\|_{L_q}
\asymp_p
\sqrt N\,\mathrm{Tr}(\Sigma)^{p/2}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

