[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Let $0<\beta<1$ and $C,C'>0$ with $C'\geq\beta C$.
Under~\cref{ass:general-spectral-link}, for every $M\in\R^{m\times n}$,
\begin{equation}
  \widetilde\Phi_{h,C'}(M)
  -\beta\widetilde\Phi_{h,C}(M)
  -(1-\beta)\inpr{M,\nabla\widetilde\Phi_{h,C'}(M)}
  \leq0.
  \notag
\end{equation}
Consequently, $V_s\leq0$ whenever $C_{s+1}\geq\beta C_s$.

