[Lemma eq:redina of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] For any $Q_1,Q_2,Q_3,R_1,R_2\in{\mathbb C}^{2n\times 2n}$ it holds
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{split}

				\big|(Q_1G(w_1)Q_2G(w_2)Q_3)_{\bm x\bm y}\big|&\lesssim \sqrt{N} (Q_1|G(w_1)|Q_1^*)_{\bm x\bm x}^{1/2} (Q_3|G(w_2)|Q_3^*)_{\bm x\bm x}^{1/2}\langle |G(w_1)|Q_2|G(w_2)|Q_2^*\rangle^{1/2} \\
				\langle |G(w_1)|R_1G(w_2)R_2|G(w_1)|R_2^* G(w_2)^*R_1^*\rangle&\lesssim N\langle |G(w_1)|R_1|G(w_2)|R_1^*\rangle\langle |G(w_1)|R_2^*|G(w_2)|R_2\rangle,
			\end{split}
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

