[Lemma 37 (Stirling's approximation) of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $t > 0$. We have as $x \to \infty$
  \begin{equation*}
    \frac{\Gamma(x - t)}{\Gamma(x)} = \frac{1}{x^{t}} \ee^{\frac{-t}{2x} + o(1/x)}\,.
  \end{equation*}

