$F_K(A,q)\in\Z[A^{\pm1},q^{\pm1}]$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \HH_1(K;A,q)-1=\{1;A\}\{-1;A\}F_K(A,q).
\end{equation}

[Corollary 42 of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] Assume the setting of Lemma \ref{lemma:initialtimephisol}. Then there exists a unique mild and variational solution on the entire interval $[0,\tau]$. Moreover, \begin{equation}
\norm{\phi}_{\mathcal W_r(\tau)} \leq \begin{cases}
\norm{\phi}_{\mathcal W_r(\tau_1)} & \tau < t_1 \\
(1+\const t^{-\alpha_1/2}_1)\norm{\phi}_{\mathcal W_r(t_1)} & \tau \geq t_1.
\end{cases} \qedhere
\end{equation}

