[Proposition prop:cheegerhyp of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let ${\ensuremath{\mathcal G}}  =(V,{\ensuremath{\mathcal E}} ,w)$ be a weighted hypergraph as above. Then, for all $k=2,\ldots,N$,
    \begin{equation}
      \mu_k \le \frac{2 \big( r({\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} )-1\big)^2}{cr({\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} )-1} \, \varphi_k ({\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} )  \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $r({\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} )$ and $cr({\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} )$ are called, respectively, the {\em rank} and {\em co-rank} of ${\ensuremath{\mathcal G}} $ and correspond to the maximum and the minimum of the cardinalities of the edges $e \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal E}} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

