body:
[Lem 21 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] The stochastic process
\begin{align*}
  M_t^B:=\int_0^t \int_{\R\setminus \{0\}} \overline{H}(s;y)\tilde{N}(ds,dy)
\end{align*}
is well-defined. Moreover, for any fixed $T>0$, $(M_t^B)_{0\le t\le T}$ is an $L^2$-martingale.

