[Theorem thm:stationary-toppling of arXiv:2604.13968, 'Divisible sandpiles via random walks in random scenery'] Let $(G,\rho,\sigma)$ be a stationary random rooted network with $\mathbb{E}[|\sigma(\rho)|/\deg(\rho)] < \infty$. Under parallel toppling, for each $k \geq 0$:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[\em (a)] The random rooted network $(G,\rho,\sigma_k,u_k)$ is stationary.
			\item[\em (b)] The degree-weighted mass is conserved: $\mathbb{E}[\sigma_k(\rho)/\deg(\rho)] = \mathbb{E}[\sigma(\rho)/\deg(\rho)]$.
		\end{itemize}

