[Lemma lem:eta-local-comparison of arXiv:2606.29557, 'Propagation of chaos for Belavkin equations beyond pure states'] For every \(T>0\), there exists \(C_{\eta,T}<\infty\), independent of
\(N\) and \(j\), such that
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  &\mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\eta}}
  \left[
    \sup_{0\le t\le T}
    \left\|
      \overline\gamma_t^{N,j}
      -
      \gamma_t^{N,\eta,j}
    \right\|_1^2
  \right]\le
  C_{\eta,T}
  \int_0^T
  \mathbb E_{\mathbb Q^{N,\eta}}
  \left[
    \left\|
      \rho_s^{N:(j),\eta}
      -
      \overline\gamma_s^{N,j}
    \right\|_1^2
  \right]\mathrm d s.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}

