body:
[Corollary Quantitative Stability of $I_\gamma^*$ of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $(M^n , [\hat{h}])$ be the conformal infinity of an asymptotically hyperbolic manifold $(X^{n+1},g^+ )$ such that $\Lambda_{\gamma} (M,[\hat{h}]) < \Lambda_{\gamma} (\mathbb{S}^n ,[h_{0}])$. Then, there exist constants $C>0$ and $\theta \geq 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
    I_\gamma^* [U,\bar{g}^*] - \Lambda_\gamma (M,[\hat{h}]) \geq C d(U, \mathcal{M}^*)^{2+\theta},
\end{align*}
for all $U \in W^{1,2}(X,y^a)$ with nonzero trace.

[Lemma Lem:H of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For each $z\in\mathbb{Z}^d$ and $m\in\mathbb{N}$, the following holds:
		\begin{align}
			\|\mathbf{1}_{\mathscr{C}_\infty}-\theta(\mathfrak{p})\|_{\underline{H}^{-1}\left(\square_m(z)\right)}\leqslant 
			\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
				\mathcal{O}_s(C m),  & d=2,  \\ 
				\mathcal{O}_s(C), & d\geqslant 3,
			\end{array}\right. 
		\end{align}
		where $C$ and $s$ are finite positive constants depending on $d,\mathfrak{p}$.

