[Theorem THM33 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $M\in \text{MF}(X)$ and $m^*:=m|_{E_M}$.   Then, the subprocess $X^M$ is a nearly $m^*$-symmetric right process on $E_M$, which is properly associated with the Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E}^M,{\mathscr F}^M)$ {on $L^2(E_M, m^*)$} given by
\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned}
		&{\mathscr F}^M={\mathscr F}^{E_M}\cap L^2(E_M, \rho_M+\lambda_M), \\
		&{\mathscr E}^M(f,g)={\mathscr E}(f,g)+\nu_M(\tilde{f}\otimes \tilde{g}),\quad f,g\in {\mathscr F}^M,
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where ${\mathscr F}^{E_M}$ is defined as in (equation eq:31 of the paper) with $G=E_M$.
 Furthermore,  $X^M$ is $m^*$-tight,  and $({\mathscr E}^M,{\mathscr F}^M)$ is quasi-regular on $L^2(E_M,m^*)$.

