[Lemma 21 (the map is a contraction) of arXiv:2609.01093, 'Ideal MHD below the classical well-posedness threshold'] With $T_*$ chosen by \eqref{eq:Tstar}, the map $\mathcal M$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \|\mathcal M\Ufield-\mathcal M\Vfield\|_{\mathcal Y}
 \le C_\delta T^\varepsilon R(1+R)
       \|\Ufield-\Vfield\|_{\mathcal Y}
 \le\tfrac12\|\Ufield-\Vfield\|_{\mathcal Y}
\end{equation}
for all $\Ufield,\Vfield\in\mathcal U_{R,\delta}$ and every $T\le T_*$.

[Definition 4 of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] The \textbf{$AB$-transition exit distribution} on \(\bar{A} \cap (\partial A + 1)\) and the \textbf{$BA$-transition exit distribution} on \(\bar{B} \cap (\partial B + 1)\) are defined as follows:  
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        &\eta^-_A(\d x) = \frac{1}{v^-_A}\rho(x)\mathcal{L}q(x), \quad x \in \bar{A} \cap (\partial A + 1),\\
        &\eta^-_B(\d x) = \frac{1}{v^-_B}\rho(x)\mathcal{L}q(x), \quad x \in \bar{B} \cap (\partial B + 1),
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where \(v^-_A\) and \(v^-_B\) are normalizing constants such that \(\eta^-_A\) and \(\eta^-_B\) define probability measures on \(\bar{A} \cap (\partial A + 1)\) and \(\bar{B} \cap (\partial B + 1)\), respectively.

[Defn def:ifs of arXiv:2412.09535, 'Local limit theorem for joint subgraph counts'] Given downwards closed $\mathcal{H}$, an integer $n$, and some $\eta > 0$, a collection of statistics $\mathcal{F} = (F_H)_{H \in \mathcal{H}}$, where $F_H \in \mathcal{R}_{\mathcal{H},n}$ for all $H \in \mathcal{H}$, is an \vocab{$(\mathcal{H}, n, \eta)$-integral factor system} (abbreviated \vocab{$(\mathcal{H}, n, \eta)$-IFS} or \vocab{IFS} if the parameters are unimportant) if for all $H \in \mathcal{H}$, in $\mathcal{R}_n$ we can write
\[F_H = \sum_{\mathrm{NIV}~\mkern-5mu H' \preceq H} a_{H'} X^*_{H'} = \sum_{\mathrm{NIV}~\mkern-5mu H' \preceq H} b_{H'} \gamma^*_{H'} = \sum_{\mathrm{NIV}~\mkern-5mu H' \preceq H} c_{H'} \gamma_{H'},\]
where
\begin{cond}
\item  all $a_{H'}$ are integers and $a_H = 1$;
\item  $\abs{b_{H'}} \leq \eta n^{(v(H) - v(H'))/2}$ for all $H'$ and $b_H = (p(1-p))^{e(H)/2}$;
\item  $\abs{c_{H'}} \leq \eta n^{(v(H) - v(H'))/2}$ for all $H'$ and $c_H = (p(1-p))^{e(H)/2}$.
\end{cond}

