[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] The function $\psi$ defined in \eqref{eqn-regular-potential}  is of $C^2$ class and 
\begin{equation}
\psi^\prime(s)= s(s^2-1) \mbox{ and } \psi^{\prime\prime}(s)= 3s^2-1, \;  s \in \mathbb{R}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\Psi^\prime$ maps $L^6(\domO)$ into $L^2(\domO)$, and 
     \begin{equation}
       \vert \psi^\prime(\phi)\vert_{L^2} \leq \Vert  \phi \Vert_{L^6}^3 + \vert \phi \vert_{L^2}, \;\; \phi \in L^6(\domO),
