[Cor dense-conv of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] In the supercritical regime for an admissible sequence $(k,0), (k,\alpha)$ and $4\alpha >-d+k-1$, the number of $k$-dimensional simplices, given through $\mathcal{V}_{k}^{(0)}$, asymptotically determines $\mathcal{V}_{k}^{(\alpha)}$,
\begin{equation}
\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k}^{(\alpha)} = \frac {\mu_{k}^{(\alpha)}} {\mu_{k}^{(0)}} \tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k}^{(0)}+ D_t^{(\alpha)},
\end{equation} 
where $\mu_k^{(0)}$ is as in ((Eq: muk0 of the paper)) and $ D_t^{(\alpha)} $ satisfies ((eq:order-Dt of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:TAL of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] Let $\mu\in\mathcal{P}(H^{-s}(\Lambda_{L} ))$ be a Gaussian measure $\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)$ with covariance operator $\Sigma$ which is a strictly positive, self-adjoint, compact operator in $L^2(\Lambda_{L})$ that admits a smooth diagonalizing basis $\{e_k\}\subset H^s(\Lambda_{L} )$. Then, for any $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(H^{-s}(\Lambda_{L}))$, we have the inequality
\begin{equation}
        W^2_{\Sigma^{-1}}(\nu,\mu)\le 2\mathcal{H}(\nu|\mu).
\end{equation}

