[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2609.02225, '\textbf{The direct moving plane method for weak solutions of the fractional $p$-Laplacian}'] Let $n\ge2$, $0<s<1$ and $1<p\le2$. Let $f:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ be locally Lipschitz continuous with $f(0)\ge0$. Let $u\in W^{s,p}_0(B_1)\cap L^\infty(B_1)$ be a nontrivial nonnegative weak solution of
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
(-\Delta)^s_pu=f(u) &\text{in }B_1,\\
u=0 &\text{in }B_1^c.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Then $u$ is radially symmetric with respect to the origin and radially nonincreasing in $B_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm survival of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Suppose that $h\neq 0$ is given by
	\begin{equation*}
		h(x) = \int_0^\infty(1-\ee^{-\lambda x})\nu^1(d\lambda) + b_1\mathbbm{1}_{x>0} , \quad x\in \mathbb{R}_+,
	\end{equation*}
	 with $b_1\geq 0$ and let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 =f\in \mathcal{C}_c^+(\mathbb{R})$ and $f\neq 0$. Then 
	 \begin{equation*}
	 	\mathbb{P}(\langle X_t,1\rangle >0, \quad \forall t > 0) >0. 
	 \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop holderproper of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] We work under the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:convergence of the paper). Then, the following convergence in law in the space $\mathbb{D}([0,T], \mathbb{R})$ holds true
\begin{align*} 
\left(\langle \mu^{K}_{t}, \varpi \rangle\right)_{t \in [0,T]} \xrightarrow[K \longrightarrow + \infty]{}  \left(\langle \mu^{*}_{t}, \varpi \rangle\right)_{t \in [0,T]}. 
\end{align*}
As a consequence, using the results of Section~(subsec:tension of the paper) and Theorem~(theo:roel of the paper) again, we obtain that the process $\left((\mu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]}\right)_{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}}$ converges in law in $\mathbb{D}([0,T], (\mathcal{M}_{\varpi+\omega}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}),\mathrm{v}) \times [0,R_{\max}])$ towards $(\mu^{*}_{t},R^{*}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]}$.

[Prop Resolvent-Formula of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] For every  $u\in\mathscr{B}_b(X)$ we have
\begin{equation}
	\check{R}_\alpha u(x) = \mathbb{E}_x\left[\int_0^\infty e^{-\alpha {\bf A}_t}u(\mathbb{X}_t)\,d{\bf A}_t \right],\quad \alpha>0.
\end{equation}
Assume in addition that $\mu$ is $G$-bounded and charges no semi-polar sets. Then 
\begin{equation}
	\check{R}_\alpha = (1 + \alpha G^\mu)^{-1} G^\mu,\quad \alpha\geq0.	

\end{equation}

