body:
[Prop p:DOV-geodesic-holder of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] {dov}}]
    For every $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}$, we have the scaling relation
    \begin{align}
        \left\{\Pi_{(s,x),(t,y)}(s + (t-s)r)\right\}_{r\in[0,1]}
        \overset{d}{=} \left\{(t-s)^{2/3}\Pi_{(0,0),(1,0)}(r) + x + (y-x)r\right\}_{r\in[0,1]},
    \end{align}
    where the equality in distribution is as $C([0,1])$-valued random variables.
    For a proof of the above statement, see the discussion below [dov].

    Moreover, given $S\geqslant 1$ and $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}$ with slope $\left|\frac{y-x}{t-s}\right| \leqslant S$ and $t-s \leqslant 1$,
    there is a random constant $\mathfrak{C}_{(p:DOV-geodesic-holder of the paper)} > 0$ with the following two properties.
    First, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}(\mathfrak{C}_{(p:DOV-geodesic-holder of the paper)} > m) \leqslant 
        Ce^{-c m^{3}}
        \qquad\text{for all $m\geqslant 0$},
    \end{align*}
    where $C,c>0$ are universal constants.
    Second, for all $r,r'\in [s,t]$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \left|\Pi_{(s,x),(t,y)}(r)-\Pi_{(s,x),(t,y)}(r')\right|
        \leqslant \mathfrak{C}_{(p:DOV-geodesic-holder of the paper)}\, |r-r'|^{2/3}\log^{1/3}\left(2\vee \frac{1}{|r-r'|}\right)
        + S|r-r'|.
    \end{align}
    We emphasize that $\mathfrak{C}_{(p:DOV-geodesic-holder of the paper)}$ depends on the point $(s,x;t,y)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 27 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $u\in C((0,T)\times\mathbb{R})$ and $(t,x)\in(0,T)\times \mathbb{R}$. We denote by $\mathcal{P}^{2,+} u(t,x)$ (the ``parabolic superjet" of $u$ at $(t,x)$) the set of triples $(p,q,X)\in\mathbb{R}^3$ satisfying
	\begin{align*}
		u(s,y)\leq u(t,x)+p(s-t)+ q(y-x)+\frac{1}{2} X(y-x)^2+o(|s-t|+|y-x|^2).
	\end{align*}
	Similarly, we define $\mathcal{P}^{2,-} u(t,x)$ (the ``parabolic subjet" of $u$ at $(t,x)$) by $\mathcal{P}^{2,-} u(t,x):=-\mathcal{P}^{2,+}(- u)(t,x)$.

