[Definition def:conservative of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] [Conservative set of reactions] 
Assume that $\mathcal R $ is a set of chemical reactions. Then we say that $\mathcal R $ is conservative if
\begin{equation}
\mathcal M_+ \cap \mathbb R_+^M \neq \emptyset.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 10 (Single-scale estimate) of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] There exists $C = C(d) < \infty$ such that for every bounded Lipschitz domain $U \subset \Rd$, every $\eps \in (0,1)$, every integer $k \ge 0$ with $\eps 3^k \le \operatorname{diam}(U)$, and every $h \colon \eps\Zd \to \R$ with $h = 0$ on $\eps\Zd \setminus U$,
		\begin{equation}

			\|h\|_{L^2(U^\eps)}^2
			\le
			C \operatorname{diam}(U)^2
			\eps^{2d}
			\sum_{x \in \eps\Zd}
			\sum_{\substack{z \in \eps\Zd \\ \eps 3^k \le \|z\|_\infty < \eps 3^{k+1}}}
			J(z)\bigl(h(x{+}z) - h(x)\bigr)^2\,.
		\end{equation}

