body:
[Proposition of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $\delta>0$. For each $n$, let $ {\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} ^{(n)} \in{\ensuremath{\textup{Conj}}} ^*({\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n)$. Assume that $f_1({\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} ^{(n)})\geq \delta n$ for $n$ large enough. Let $a\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $.
Let $(t_n)$ be a sequence of positive real numbers such that $t_n = \frac{\ln n + a + o(1)}{\ln(n/f_1({\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} ^{(n)}))}$. Let $\theta >0$.   
As $n\to \infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
   \frac{1}{2} \sum_{\lambda \in \widehat{{\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n}^{**}} \left( d_\lambda \left| \chi^\lambda({\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} ^{(n)}) \right|^{t_n}\right)^{\theta} \to \sum_{r\geq 1} e^{-ar\theta} \sum_{\mu \vdash r} \left(\frac{d_\mu}{r!}\right)^\theta.
\end{equation}
In particular, as $n\to \infty$
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1}{2}\sum_{\lambda \in \widehat{{\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n}^{**}} d_\lambda^2 \left| \chi^\lambda({\ensuremath{\mathcal C}} ^{(n)}) \right|^{2t_n} \to e^{e^{-2a}}-1.
\end{equation}

