for any $u>0$. So in an interval $I \subset [0,T]$ of length $\leq n^{-1}$, we have $\mathbb{P}(||X(t)-X(s)||>1+u)\leq e^{-\frac{u^2}{4|t-s|}}$ for all $t,s \in I$. In particular, it follows for $u>0$ that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}(||X(t)-X(s)||>u)\leq C e^{-u^2/4},
\end{equation}
for some $C>0$. ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:6537a791d5448569ea39becef16367d6cc1af674ea6b2ddf93719fb0f3ae02a5","revision_digest":"sha256:2a842966fd051911b4146b1cfc2f0a4af9aec4dc8188bcd79d66a089a8cb616c","source_id":"arxiv:2411.01633","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

{"artifact_digest":"sha256:acd6a1e0ad5371599cb9a8e4eb5691d346eed5d4b96ca0195e277f27ef440f91","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/ac/acd6a1e0ad5371599cb9a8e4eb5691d346eed5d4b96ca0195e277f27ef440f91.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:24c7ca3e32e7d86b000f92bdfa5a900f0d4475a8d498a774032117fe794cf773","bundle_entry_key":"2609-01851-theorem-11-multipartite","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_145","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_145.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-01851-theorem-11-multipartite","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: $(\impliedby)$ Consider edge $xy \notin E(H)$ for infection. We will show that if conditions 1-3 hold, then there exists a copy $H'$ of $H$ in $K_n$ with $xy \in E(H')$ such that all other edges of $H'$ also belong to $E(H)$.

    Since $H$ is a complete $r$-partite graph, vertices $x$ and $y$ must belong to the same partite set, say $I$, and $|I|=2$. Then $x$ and $y$ are each adjacent to all other vertices in $H$. Additionally, there exists a partite set $J$ with $|J|=1$, say that $J = \{z\}$. The edges $xz$ and $yz$ must belong to $H$ and are already infected.

