body:
[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2511.09726, 'The non-covered set in Dvoretzky covering is a set of multiplicity'] Let $(f_n(\omega,t))_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of random functions. Suppose that there exists $\alpha \in (0,1)$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \underset{n,m\rightarrow \infty}{\lim}\mathbb E \left[\|f_n(\omega,\cdot) -f_m(\omega, \cdot)\|_{1}^\alpha\right] = 0. 
    \end{equation}
    Then there exists a subsequence  $\{f_{n_k}\}_{k\geq 0}$ that converges in $L^1(\mathbb T)$ almost surely.

