body:
[Corollary 11 (Constructive endpoint-resolution bounds) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] Let $d=\lfloor(m-1)/2\rfloor$, let $\xi_{d+1}$ be the largest zero on $[0,1]$ of the shifted Legendre polynomial of degree $d+1$, and put
\begin{equation}
A_{m,L}=\min\left\{\frac1{m+1},\frac{L}{m(m+1)}\right\},\quad
D_{m,N}=\prod_{j=1}^m\frac{N-j}{N+j}.

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
A_{m,L}D_{m,N}&\le\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N},\\
\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}
&\le\min\left\{B_{m,N},
L\left(1-\xi_{d+1}+\frac1{N+1}\right),1\right\}.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
If $L$ is fixed and $m^2/N\to\tau\in(0,\infty)$, then
\begin{equation}
e^{-\tau}\le\liminf\frac{m^2\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}}L
\le\limsup\frac{m^2\Delta^{\uparrow,L}_{m,N}}L
\le j_{0,1}^2+\tau,

\end{equation}
where $j_{0,1}\simeq2.4048$ is the first positive zero of $J_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 6 (Variational representation) of arXiv:2608.22816, 'A Cap-Move Reformulation of Ling's Proof of Samuels' Conjecture'] For $0\le \mu_1\le \cdots \le \mu_n$ and $\delta>0$, it holds that
	\begin{align*}
		\min_{b\ge 0} \min_{\substack{z_i\in [0,\mu_i], i\in [n] \\ z_1+\cdots+z_n\le b}} \sum_{i=1}^n \log\pth{1-\frac{z_i}{\delta+b}} = \min_{1\le i\le n} \sum_{j=i}^n \log\pth{1-\frac{\mu_j}{\delta + \sum_{k=i}^n \mu_k}}. 
	\end{align*}

