[Proposition prop:Global law for A of arXiv:2411.10311, 'Planar Novikov-Shubin invariant for adjacency matrices of structured directed dense random'] Let $A $ be the adjacency matrix of the directed stochastic block model as defined above. Then 
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{n\1K} \sum_{w \in \spec(A) }\delta_{\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}w} \to \sigma( z)\mathrm{d}^2 z  + \varrho\1 \delta_0
\end{equation} 
weakly in probability, where $\varrho = 1- \int_{\mathbb{C}} \sigma(z) \mathrm{d}^2 z$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.26662, 'Boundary–Moment Universality and Curvature Corrections in Random Geometric Graphs on Riema'] There are $C<\infty$ and $r_0>0$ such that, for
$n\ge3$ and $0<r<r_0$,
\begin{equation}
\operatorname{Var} C_n(r)
\le C\left(
n^3r^{2d}
+n^4r^{3d}
+n^5r^{4d+4}
\right).

\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
\operatorname{Var}\widehat{\mathcal G}_{3,n}(r)
\le C\left(
\frac1{n^3r^{2d+4}}
+\frac1{n^2r^{d+4}}
+\frac1n
\right).

\end{equation}
Let $r_n\downarrow0$ and assume
\begin{equation}
n^3r_n^{2d+4}\rightarrow\infty,
\qquad
n^2r_n^{d+4}\rightarrow\infty.

\end{equation}
Then
\[
\widehat{\mathcal G}_{3,n}(r_n)
\xrightarrow{\Pp}\mathcal G_3(f;g).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 5 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\alpha$ be a probability measure on $(\X,\calX)$. A process $(J_n,S_n)_{n\geq0}$ with values in $\X\times\N^d$ is a discrete multi-time Markov renewal chain with initial law $\alpha$ and semi-Markov kernel $q$ if $J_0$ has law $\alpha$, $S_0=\zerod$, and

\begin{equation*}
\Pp\left(J_{n+1}\in A,\ S_{n+1}-S_n=k\mid J_0,S_0,\ldots,J_n,S_n\right)=q_k(J_n,A)
\end{equation*}

for all $A\in\calX$ and $k\in\N^d$.

