[Theorem of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] For every continuous time scaling triplet $((t_n), (w_n),p)$, there exists a sequence of continuous time Markov chains $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+})_{n\geq 1}$ such that for every $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $, we have 
\begin{equation*}
\mathrm{d}^{(n)}\left( t_n + c w_n\right) \xrightarrow[n\to+\infty]{} p(c).
\end{equation*}

