[Lemma 3 (Bounded extreme eigenvalues after $K$) of arXiv:2607.12667, 'Phase Transition of Eigenvalues of Covariances from the Spiked Mixture Model in High-dimen'] For $\mathbf{S}_{d,n} = \Z+\Pb_1\Pb_2^\mathsf{T}$, defined in \eqref{eq:covariance_int} and assuming that $d\geq 2K$, we have: 
\begin{align*}
    &\lambda_{i}(\Z) \leq \lambda_i(\Sb_{d,n}) \leq \lambda_{i-K}(\Z), &\forall i > K.
\end{align*}

[Mainthm 1 of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] Let  $(X_i,p_i)$  be a sequence of pointed complete $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifolds with $\ric (X_i) \geq - (n-1)$,  $G_i \leq \iso (X_i)$ a sequence of closed groups of isometries, and assume
\begin{equation}
(X_i,G_i, p_i) \xrightarrow{eGH} (X,G,p) .      
\end{equation}
Then $\mathfrak{g}$, the Lie algebra of $G$, admits an ideal $\mathfrak{h} \trianglelefteq \mathfrak{g}$ with $\mathfrak{g}/\mathfrak{h}$ nilpotent and such that
\begin{equation}
    \dim ( \mathfrak{h}) \leq \limsup _{i \to \infty } \dim (G_i)  .   
\end{equation}
   Moreover, if $\vol (B_1(p_i))\geq v$ for some $v > 0 $, then $\mathfrak{h}$ can be taken so that equality in \eqref{eq:h-ineq} holds. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Sigma-oo-equiv-left-adjointable of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $i\colon G\to G'$ be an injective homomorphism of compact Lie groups. Then $i^*\colon{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_{G'}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ admits a left adjoint $i_!$, and the Beck--Chevalley map $i_!\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty\to\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty\textbf{\textup{L}}i_!$ of functors ${{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{G,*}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_{G'}$ is an equivalence.
    \begin{proof}
        Proposition~(prop:i!-left-Quillen-equiv-sp of the paper) shows that we have a homotopical Quillen adjunction $i_!\colon\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G'}$-OrthSp}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 i^*$, proving the existence of the left adjoint $i_!$ of $i^*=\textbf{\textup{L}}i^*\colon{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_{G'}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$. Since also $i_!\colon\textbf{\textup{$\bm G$-Top}}_*\to\cat{$\bm{G'}$-Top}$ and the suspension spectrum functors are left Quillen (see Lemmas~(lemma:res-pted-Quillen of the paper) and~(lemma:Sigma-oo-left-Quillen of the paper), respectively), it then suffices to observe for the Beck--Chevalley condition that the \emph{underived} Beck--Chevalley map $i_!\Sigma^\infty\to\Sigma^\infty i_!$ is an isomorphism.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

