body:
[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.29361, 'Convergence of the subcritical $\gamma$-LQG metric to the critical $2$-LQG metric as $\gam'] Fix a bounded open set $U \subseteq \CC$ and $\alpha , A \in (0,\infty)$. Suppose that we have chosen the functions $b,M$ such that $b(\xi) \sqrt{M(\xi)} > 2A$. Then, there exist constants $c_0,c_1 \in (0,\infty)$ depending only on $U,\alpha,$ and $A$ such that for all $t\geq 1$, it holds with probability at least 
    \begin{equation*}
        1-c_0 t^{1-\left(\frac{b(\xi) \sqrt{M(\xi)}}{A}-2\right)\alpha} - c_0 e^{-c_1 (\log t)^2}
    \end{equation*}
that the following is true. For all $z \in (e^{-t-100} \ZZ^2) \cap U$ such that $h_{e^{-t}}(z) - h_1(z) \leq 2t - \alpha \log t$, we have that
\begin{equation*}
    M_{e^{-t}}(z) \leq 4\exp\left(\frac{2t - (h_{e^{-t}}(z) - h_1(z))}{A}\right).
\end{equation*}

