[Proposition prop:simple of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let $G=(V,\mathcal{E})$ be a finite graph as in Convention (conv;simple of the paper), with $|V|=N$. Fix an integer $1\leq m\leq N$. Consider a collection $B_1,...,B_m$ of nonempty disjoint subsets of $V$, and assume that
\begin{equation}
\varphi(B_1)\le \varphi(B_2)\le \cdots \le \varphi(B_m)\,. 
\end{equation}
Then, for all $k=1,...,m$,
\begin{equation}
 \mu_k \leq 2 \, \frac{\sum_{i=k}^m \mathrm{vol}(B_i) \,\varphi(B_i)}{\sum_{i=k}^m \mathrm{vol}(B_i)} \,  . 
\end{equation}

