body:
[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] There exists a distribution $\Wick{|\nabla X_1|^2}\in\CC_{-\delta}^{2-d-\kappa}(\IR^d)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\Wick{|\nabla X_1|^2}=\lim_{\eps\to0}\big(|\nabla X_{1,\eps}|^2-c_\eps^1\big)
\end{equation}
in probability in the space $\CC_{-\delta}^{2-d-\kappa}(\IR^d)$ for any $\kappa,\delta>0$ with $c_\eps^1=\IE\big[|\nabla X_{1,\eps}|^2\big]$ a diverging constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

