[Corollary co:kappa of arXiv:2607.05345, 'The local product condition implies cutoff'] If (equation eq:ass-det-init of the paper) holds, then
		\begin{eqnarray*}
			\gamma_\star & \ge & \kappa,
		\end{eqnarray*}
		where $\kappa$ is the Bakry-\'Emery curvature. In particular, when $\kappa>0$, we have
		\begin{eqnarray}

			\forall \varepsilon\in(0,1/2),\quad \mathrm{w}_{\textsc{mix}}(\varepsilon) & \le & \frac{3}{2\kappa}\log\frac{1}{\varepsilon}.
		\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

