[Lemma EI2 of arXiv:2607.05418, 'On the Group Randomness of 0-1 Real Sequences from Binary Linear Codes'] Assume $s \in \Omega_p$ and $\tilde{s} \in \widetilde{\Omega}_p$ are derived from exactly the same instant of $p$ (not necessarily distinct) codewords from $\mathcal{C}$. Then the eigenvalues of $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}_{\tilde{s}}$ and $\mathcal{G}_s$ satisfy
    $$\lambda_{i+1} \leq \tilde{\lambda}_i \leq \lambda_{i-1}$$
    for $1 \leq i \leq p$, where for convention, $\lambda_0=+\infty$ and $\lambda_{p+1}=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 39 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $d=2$ and fix $x\in\X$. Assume that $\overline H_x(\zerod)=1$ and that

\begin{equation*}
\overline H_x(u+v)=\overline H_x(u)\overline H_x(v),
\qquad u,v\in\N^2.
\end{equation*}

Then

\begin{equation*}
\overline H_x(u_1,u_2)=a_1^{u_1}a_2^{u_2},
\qquad a_i=\overline H_x(e_i).
\end{equation*}

If $0<a_1<1$ and $0<a_2<1$, this function cannot be the rectangular no-renewal survival of a probability distribution on $\N^2$.

