[Lemma lem:partitionFunction of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] Let $\Lambda \subset (-\frac{L}{2},\frac{L}{2}]^{2}$. There exist a constant $C(\lambda,m,|\Lambda| ) \geq 1$ independent of $L$ and $N$ such that 
\begin{equation}
1 \leq \mathbb{E}^{\mu_{m,L}^{\otimes N}}\left[\exp \bigg (-\frac{\lambda}{N} \int_{\Lambda} : \|Z_{\epsilon}(x)\|^{4}_{\mathbb{R}^{N}}:_{m}dx \bigg )\right] \leq C(\lambda,m,|\Lambda|), 
\end{equation}
uniformly in $\epsilon<m^{2}$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$. Furthermore, for $|\Lambda|=1$ and $\lambda \geq e$, it holds
\begin{equation}
\log C(\lambda,m,|\Lambda|) \lesssim \lambda \big (  |\log m| \vee(\log \lambda)^{2} \big ).
\end{equation}

