[Thm Red of arXiv:2605.10452, 'A secretary for Messrs. Luce and Mallows'] {\bf(CDK)}
Let $\{V_j\}_{j=1}^n$ be independent exponential random variables with $V_j\sim\text{Exp}(\theta_j),\ j\in[n]$.
Then
\begin{equation}
P\left(\text{Red}(V_1V_2\cdots V_n)=\sigma\right)=P_n^{\mathcal{L}_\text{inv};\{\theta_j\}_{j=1}^n}(\sigma),
\end{equation}
where $\text{Red}(V_1V_2\cdots V_n)$ is the reduced permutation in $S_n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:gaussianTVrate of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let
\begin{equation*}
 Y_{n+1}=MY_n+G\xi_{n+1}
\end{equation*}
be a Gaussian autoregressive process on $\mathbb R^N$, with transition kernel $Q$, where $M\in\mathbb R^{N\times N}$ satisfies $\rho(M)<1$, $G\in\mathbb R^{N\times N'}$, the $\xi_n$ are i.i.d.\ standard Gaussian vectors in $\mathbb R^{N'}$, and the covariance $\Sigma_{n_0}$ of the $n_0$-step transition law is nonsingular for some $n_0\ge1$; this holds in particular when $GG^\top\succ0$, with $n_0=1$. Then the chain has a unique invariant law $\pi$, which is a centered Gaussian. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{n\to\infty}\lVert \delta_zQ^n-\pi\rVert_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}\le\rho(M)
 \qquad\text{for every initial state }z,
\end{equation}
and the limit exists and equals $\rho(M)$ for a suitable $z$. Finally, there are initial states $z,\widetilde z$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{n\to\infty}
 \norm{\delta_zQ^n-\delta_{\widetilde z}Q^n}_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}=\rho(M).
\end{equation}

