[Proposition prop:2nd-indistin of arXiv:2608.22765, 'Learning to Control Coupled-Dynamics Environments with Joint Markov Decision Processes'] Assume Condition~(cond:weaker of the paper). Start from any $q_0\in\mathbb R^{\mathcal S\times\mathcal A}$ and $M_0\in\mathbb R^{(\mathcal S\times\mathcal A)^2}$. At each iteration, choose any greedy selector
\begin{equation}
\sigma_k(s)\in\arg\max_{c\in\mathcal A}q_k(s,c).
\end{equation}
Update the mean by ordinary value iteration,
\begin{equation}
q_{k+1}(s,a)=r(s,a)+\gamma\sum_{s'\in\mathcal S}P_S(s'\mid s,a)\max_{c\in\mathcal A}q_k(s',c),
\end{equation}
and update the second moment by
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
M_{k+1}(s,a,\tilde s,\tilde a)=\mathbb E\Bigl[&
R^a\tilde R^{\tilde a}+\gamma R^a q_k\bigl(\tilde S'^{\tilde a},\sigma_k(\tilde S'^{\tilde a})\bigr)+\gamma\tilde R^{\tilde a}q_k\bigl(S'^a,\sigma_k(S'^a)\bigr)\\
&+\gamma^2M_k\bigl(S'^a,\sigma_k(S'^a),\tilde S'^{\tilde a},\sigma_k(\tilde S'^{\tilde a})\bigr)\,\Bigm|\,S=s,\tilde S=\tilde s\Bigr].
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The expectation again uses the coupling from (equation eq:2ndmoment of the paper). Then $q_k\to Q^*$ and $M_k\to M^*$ as $k\to\infty$, where $M^*$ is the common fixed point in Condition~(cond:weaker of the paper).

