[Lem l.delta of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] Under the preceding setup, for every $t\in(0,\infty)$, 
\begin{align}

	\int_{\Sigma(t)} \mathrm{d}\vec{u}\ \prod_{i=1}^{m} \mathcal{T}_{i,\varepsilon}(u_i)
	\xlongrightarrow{\varepsilon}
	\int_{\Sigma(t)} \mathrm{d}\vec{u}\ \prod_{i\notin I} \mathcal{T}_{i}(u_i)	
	\text{ strongly,}
\end{align}
where the $\Sigma(t)$ on the left-hand side is $\{\sum_{i\in[\![m]\!]}u_i=t\}$, while the $\Sigma(t)$ on the right-hand side is $\{\sum_{i\in[\![m]\!]\setminus I}u_i=t\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma L:K5 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the term $\mathsf{K}_5(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ be defined in equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W2W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\mathsf{K}_5(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta) & \le K e^{-(2p)\alpha (t-r_1 \vee r_2)} e^{-(2p)\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r_1 \vee r_2 - r_1 \wedge r_2)}. 
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}

