[Prop thm:3-6-0-CP of arXiv:2412.00708, 'Stochastic PDE approach to fluctuating interfaces'] For every $t>0$ and $G\in L^2({\mathbb{R}}) \cap L^1({\mathbb{R}})$, we have
\begin{align*} 
\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow 0} \| e^{-tK\mathcal{A}} G(z) 
- \langle G, e\rangle_{L^2({\mathbb{R}})} e(z)\|_{L^2(\varepsilon^{-1}{\mathbb{T}})} =0,
\end{align*}
with the first $G$ interpreted as $G|_{\varepsilon^{-1}{\mathbb{T}}}$,
where $K=\varepsilon^{-2}$ and
\begin{align*}
e(z) := U_0'(-z) /\|U_0'\|_{L^2({\mathbb{R}})}, \quad z\in {\mathbb{R}}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

