{"artifact_digest":"sha256:d64cc7567c72af4d5940a1bac1d5169a6ec06eb36f3d5a76e531701e27838ee7","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/d6/d64cc7567c72af4d5940a1bac1d5169a6ec06eb36f3d5a76e531701e27838ee7.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:eb18fa18d774709c2015f01d87ee0ca275c2d09f2bbc70a839e4b6cb4cceb5d3","bundle_entry_key":"2605-08345-theorem-8-companion-process-finite-numbe","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_028","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_028.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-08345-proposition-8-companion-process-finite-numbe","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let \( T \) be the waiting time before the next jump of \( \Comp \). For \( t \ge 0 \), we have 
\begin{equation}
\Prob(T > t \vert \CompL(0) = \CompSmL_0) = \exp \left( - r \int_0^t  1 \wedge (\lipnorm \CompSmL_0 e^{-\underline{d}_1 s}) \mathrm{d}s \right).
\end{equation}
For \( s \in [0,t] \) and \( \CompSmL_0 > 0 \) we have 
\[ 1 \ge \lipnorm \CompSmL_0 e^{- \underline{d}_1 s} \Longleftrightarrow s \ge \dfrac{1}{\underline{d}_1} \ln \left( \lipnorm \CompSmL_0 \right). \]
We define the time where both terms of the minimum are equal
