body:
[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.02785, 'Characterization of Stanley-Reisner varieties by their automorphism group'] For $i\in[n]$ the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]
\item $i$ is a cone vertex of $\Delta$;
\item $\emptyset\in\mathcal{A}_i(\Delta)$;
\item $-\mathbf{e}_i\in\mathcal{R}(\Delta)$.
\end{enumerate}
In that case
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\arabic*)}]
\item $\mathcal{A}_i(\Delta)=\{S\in\Delta: i\notin S\}$;
\item $\Delta=\mathcal{A}_i(\Delta)\cup\{S\cup\{i\}:S\in\mathcal{A}_i(\Delta)\}$, so $\mathcal{R}(\Delta)$ determines $\Delta$;
\item $\Delta$ is fully exposed.
\end{enumerate}

