[Proposition 27 (Finite-support Wick-chaos product formula) of arXiv:2607.16724, 'Algebraic Transfer for Operator-Valued Gaussian Chaoses: Oriented Schatten Profiles and Si'] For $P\in\mathfrak M_{m,n}$, let $q(P)=m+n-2|P|$.  Then
\begin{equation}

 I_n(L)I_m(K)
 =
 \sum_{P\in\mathfrak M_{m,n}}
 I_{q(P)}\bigl(\operatorname{Sym}_{q(P)}(L\circ_PK)\bigr).
\end{equation}
If $q(P)=0$, the corresponding term is the deterministic operator
$L\circ_PK$.  The coefficient order in every contraction is
$L_{\mathbf j}K_{\mathbf i}$.

