body:
[Lemma lem:countable-dense-regular-families of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] There exists a countable collection $\mathscr D$ of finite regular based loop families with the following property. For every finite regular based loop family $L=(\ell_1,\ldots,\ell_r)$ and every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $L'=(\ell'_1,\ldots,\ell'_r)\in\mathscr D$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $L'$ has the same marked ambient ribbon type as $L$;
\item $\max_i d_1(\ell'_i,\ell_i)<\varepsilon;$
\item the marked ambient equivalence can be realized by an ambient isotopy fixing $o$ and $\partial\Sigma$ pointwise and supported in an open set of area smaller than $\varepsilon$.
\end{enumerate}
Hence, corresponding complementary components have areas differing by less than $\varepsilon$.

