body:
[Defin of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $\psi$ be an $\mathbb{X}$-shuffling rule.
	We say that $\psi$ is \textit{$\mathfrak{S}$-equivariant}
	\footnote{
		The motivation for this name is the equivalence (equation eq:conseq-perm-invariance-psi of the paper), by analogy with the notion of \textit{equivariance} of some mapping with respect to some group action, which means commutation of that mapping with the group action.
	}
	if for every $(T,{\boldsymbol{x}},\mathtt{u})\in\trees^{\bullet}[\mathbb{X}]$ and every ${\boldsymbol{\sigma}}\in\mathfrak{S}_T$ we have:
	\begin{align*}
	\psi(T,{\boldsymbol{x}},\mathtt{u})=\psi\bigl({\boldsymbol{\sigma}}\cdotT,\,{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}_*\,{\boldsymbol{x}},\,{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}\cdot\mathtt{u}\bigr).
	\end{align*}

[Theorem value generalized Dynkin game of arXiv:2607.18531, 'Doubly reflected BSDEs driven by Inhomogeneous simple Lévy processes: Applications to gene'] Let $(Y,Z,V,K^{+},K^{-})$ be the unique solution of the DRBSDE (equation basic equation of the paper) associated with the driver $f$, terminal condition $\xi$, lower obstacle $L$, and upper obstacle $U$. Then, for every $\theta\in\mathcal{T}_{0,T}$,
	\begin{equation}
		Y_{\theta}
		=
		\underline{\mathcal{V}}_{\theta}
		=
		\overline{\mathcal{V}}_{\theta},
		\qquad \text{a.s.}

	\end{equation}
	Consequently, the generalized Dynkin game (equation payoff generalized Dynkin game of the paper)--(equation upper value generalized Dynkin game of the paper) admits a value under the nonlinear expectation $\mathcal{E}^{f}$, and this value is characterized by the first component of the solution to the associated DRBSDE. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem th:non-critical of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Let $\lambda< 1$ with $\lambda \neq 7/8$. Then for every $t>0$ and every 
	$0\neq\phi\in\ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b^+(\mathbb{R})$,
	\begin{equation}
		{\mathbb V}{\textsc{ar}}(\ensuremath{\mathcal Y}_{\lambda,N}(t,\phi))
		\xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{}
		\begin{dcases}
			0 &\text{if}\ \lambda<7/8\; \text{,}\;\;\\
			\infty &\text{if}\ \lambda>7/8\; \text{,}\;\;
		\end{dcases}
	\end{equation}
	where the variance is taken with respect to the environment law $\mathbb{P}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor 't Hooft master loop equation surface sum of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a non-null loop $\ell$ and a specific edge  $\mathbf{e}$ of $\ell$. Let $\upbeta_0(d)$ be as in the statement of Theorem~(thm: surface sum representation in 't hooft limit of the paper). Then for all $|\upbeta|\leq\upbeta_0(d)$,
\begin{align*}
	\phi(\ell) =&\sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
	\phi(\ell_1)\phi(\ell_2) - \sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
	\phi(\ell_1)\phi(\ell_2)\\
	&+ \upbeta\sum_{\ell'\in \mathbb{D}_-(\mathbf{e},\ell)}\phi(\ell') - \upbeta\sum_{\ell'\in \mathbb{D}_+(\mathbf{e},\ell)}\phi(\ell').
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma L:lmm_tu1 of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Let $0<s<t$, and $a,b \in \mathbb{R}$ satisfy the property that $\min \{a , b\} \geq -2$ and $a
    + b > -3$. Furthermore, suppose that $t - s \ll s$. Then,
  \begin{align}
    \int_{s}^{t} \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } \theta_2 \int_{s}^{\theta_2} \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } \theta_1  \int_0^s \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } r\;  (\theta_1 - r)^{a}  (\theta_2 - r)^{b}
    \lesssim
    \begin{dcases}
      (t-s)^{(a + b + 3)\wedge 2}, & a + b \neq -1, \\
      (t-s)^2 (1 + |\log (t-s)|),  & a + b = -1.
    \end{dcases}
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

