[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] For all $\gamma \in [0,1]$ and all $X,Y\in \mathcal{L}_{c,g}(E)$ we have
\begin{align*}
X\le_{\gamma,g} Y \qquad \Longleftrightarrow \qquad \E[f(X)] \le \E[f(Y)] \quad \text{ for all } f \in \mathcal{F}_{\gamma,g}\cup\{g\},
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{F}_{\gamma,g}:=\{(1-\gamma) f + \gamma g: f(x)-f(y)\le c(x,y) \,\, \text{ for all } x,y\in E\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 2 of arXiv:2606.09121, 'Truncated Signature Information for Mixed Fractional Brownian Paths'] For $\epsilon>0$, set
\begin{equation}
    \delta_m(\epsilon;\Theta,\mcH)
    =\inf_{\substack{\theta,\theta'\in\Theta\\
                      \|\theta-\theta'\|\ge\epsilon}}
      \|\Phi_{m,\mcH}(\theta)-\Phi_{m,\mcH}(\theta')\|.
\end{equation}

[Lemma def:weak_axioms2 of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] Taking images under conformal maps is a bijection, with inverse the restriction to $U=\BD$, from the couplings $(\Gamma,D)$, $\Gamma$ a non-nested $\CLE_4$ in $\BD$ and $D$ a metric on $\Gamma$, satisfying the following conditions onto the weak geodesic $\CLE_4$ metric couplings of~(def:weak_axioms of the paper):
