[Proposition 11 (Joint half-line compactness for reaction families) of arXiv:2608.30211, '2608.30211'] Let $\mathfrak F$ be compactly positive.  Then
\begin{equation}
 (f,\varrho)\longmapsto\phi^f_\varrho
 \quad\text{is continuous from }\mathfrak F\times[0,1]
 \text{ into }C_b([0,\infty)),
\end{equation}
and $(f,\varrho)\mapsto\mu^f_\varrho$ is continuous.  On the compact
parameter set this gives
\begin{equation}
 \widehat\mu:=\min_{f\in\mathfrak F}\min_{\varrho\in[0,1]}
 \mu^f_\varrho>0.
\end{equation}
The profile tails can be chosen uniformly in $(f,\varrho)$.

