[Lemma lemma2.8 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] For all $p\geq2$ and each $T>0$, there exists $C(p,T)>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \int_\Omega u_\varepsilon^p(\cdot,t)\leq C(p,T)~~\mbox{for all}~~ t\in(0,T)\cap(0,T_{\max,\varepsilon}),
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}
    \int_0^{t}\int_\Omega u_\varepsilon^{p-1}v_\varepsilon|\nabla u_\varepsilon|^2\leq C(p,T)~~\mbox{for all}~~ t\in(0,T)\cap(0,T_{\max,\varepsilon}).
    \end{equation}

