[Definition of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] We call mild solution of (equation PDE_problem_linear of the paper) to any function $v: {\Omega_T}\to [0,1]$ satisfying $M(v,t) := v_t -  {(Sv)_t} = 0$ a.s. with
    \begin{equation}
         {(S v)_t} (\cdot):= \int_0^t \left[ P_{t-s}(\cdot,0)v_s(0)h_s(0) - P_{t-s}(\cdot,1)v_s(1)h_s(1) - \int_0^1 P_{t-s}(\cdot,x)\nabla(v_s(x)f_s(x)) dx \right]ds ,
    \end{equation} where $P_t(u,v) = \sum_{w \in  {\psi}^{-1}(v)} \Phi_t(u,w)$ is the density kernel generated by the Laplacian $\Delta$ on $[0,1]$ with reflecting Neumann boundary conditions and is related to the heat kernel
    \begin{equation}
        \Phi_t(u,w) = \frac{1}{(4\pi t)^{1/2}} e^{-\frac{(u-w)^2}{4t}},
    \end{equation} by the reflection map $\psi:\mathbb{R} \to [0,1]$ defined as 
    \begin{equation}
        \psi(u+k) = \begin{cases}
            u, \quad u \in [0,1], k \textrm{ even,}\\
            1-u, \quad u \in [0,1], k \textrm{ odd,}
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation} extended to $\mathbb{R}$ by symmetry as $\psi(v) = \psi(-v)$, for $v \in \mathbb{R}$.

[Prop eqn:sol.sde1 of arXiv:2411.02033, 'Two stochastic versions of the Arps curve decline'] The solution of Equation~((eqn:sde1 of the paper)) is:
\begin{equation}
\forall t \geqslant 0 , \quad Q_t = q_0 (1+bd_0t)^{-1/b} + \sigma (1+bd_0t)^{-1/b} \int_0^t (1+bd_0u)^{1/b}\,\mathrm{d}B_u .
\end{equation}

[Lemma notDn of arXiv:2606.30475, 'Ancestries in random $d$-DAGs'] As $n\to\infty$, we have for $M>0$ fixed
 \begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\Big(\floor{Mn^{\frac{d-1}{d}}} \notin D_n \Big) \to M^d \int_0^1 e^{-\frac{M^d}{d-1}\big((1-\beta)^{1-d}-1\big)} \,\mathrm{d} \beta.
 \end{equation}

