[Definition 5 of arXiv:2606.20169, 'THEORY OF UNCERTAIN PROBABILITY:\\ CAN WE DERIVE THE PROBABILITY DENSITY FUNCTION OF UNCER'] Given a measurable space $\left(\Pi,\mathbb{F}\right)$, the set function $\mathbb{P}$ on $\mathbb{F}$ is a measure with

\begin{longlist}
\item $\mathbb{P}\left(\mathfrak{A}\right)\geq\mathbb{P}\left(\emptyset\right)=0$ for all $\mathfrak{A}\in\mathbb{F}$;
\item 
$\mathbb{P}$ is $\sigma$-additive;
\item 
$\mathbb{P}=\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{X}}\left(\mathcal{P}_{V_{\gamma}}\left(v_{\gamma}\right)\right)$. 
\end{longlist}

It will be proved that $\mathbb{P}\left(\Pi\right)=1$, and  is referred to as a measure of uncertain probability.

[Definition def:DU of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] A Volterra kernel $K$ satisfies the \emph{Decreusefond--\"Ust\"unel conditions} [DU] if:
(1)~$\int_0^T\int_0^t K(t,s)^2\,ds\,dt < \infty$;
(2)~there exists $H\in(0,1)$ such that $|K(t,s)|\leq C|t-s|^{H-1/2}$ for $s<t$;
(3)~$\partial_t K(t,s)$ exists and satisfies integrability conditions ensuring $\Dom(\delta^X)$ is dense.

[Lem exch_repr of arXiv:2606.15339, 'Uniform integrability of the distance to the nearest leaf in random trees'] Conditional on $\mathcal G_n$:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item $\tilde d^{(U)}$ is uniform on $\Sigma_{M(\mathcal{T}_n)}$;
\item $\mathbf{P}(\mathcal E_n\mid\mathcal G_n)=1/n$;
\item $(d^{\mathrm{dfs}}_1,\dots,d^{\mathrm{dfs}}_n)\stackrel{d}{=} \left((\tilde d^{(U)}_1,\dots,\tilde d^{(U)}_n)\,\bigm|\,\mathcal E_n\right)$.
\end{enumerate}

[Definition d:QR of arXiv:2508.21658, 'Infinite-dimensional stochastic differential equations for Coulomb random point fields'] A Dirichlet form $ (\E , \mathscr{D} ) $ on $ \Lnu $ is quasi-regular if: \\ 
\As{Q1} there exists an $ \E $-nest $ \{ \fFF_{k} , k \ge 1 \} $ consisting of compact sets; 

\noindent 
\As{Q2} 
there exists an $\E _1 $-dense subset of $\mathscr{D}$
whose elements admit $\E$-quasi-continuous $\nu $-versions;
\\\As{Q3} 
there exists $ \{ f_k , k \ge 1 \} \subset \mathscr{D} $ having $ \E $-quasi-continuous $ \nu $-versions $ \{ \tilde{f}_k , k \ge 1 \} \subset \mathscr{D} $ and an $ \E $-polar set $ \mathfrak{N} \subset \sS $ such that 
$ \{ \tilde{f}_k , k \ge 1 \} \subset \mathscr{D} $ separates the points on $ \sS \backslash \mathfrak{N} $.

[Lemma lem:ehr-born of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] For all $\theta\in\mathbb{R}$ and $k\in\{0,\dots,n\}$,

\begin{equation}
\bigl|\langle m=k-\tfrac n2\rvert\,e^{-i\theta J_x}\,\lvert m=+\tfrac n2\rangle\bigr|^{2}
=\binom nk\cos^{2k}\!\tfrac\theta2\,\sin^{2(n-k)}\!\tfrac\theta2 .

\end{equation}

