\end{align}
for every $t\in(0,T]$ and every $a\in U$, where $\widetilde u_t$ is defined as in (equation damped_def_ctrl_2 of the paper) with $h=J_1a$. In particular, estimate (equation stima_norma_L2_utilde_1 of the paper) is satisfied with $\beta=\frac\varepsilon\alpha$ and $\varepsilon<\frac\alpha2$ if $\alpha\in\left(0,\frac12\right]$ and with $\beta=\frac\varepsilon{1-\alpha}$ and $\varepsilon<\frac{1-\alpha}2$ if $\alpha\in\left[\frac12,1\right)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

