[Theorem teo_1 of arXiv:2606.27549, 'On Analytically Tractable Multidimensional Diffusions via Doob $h$-Transforms, with Resett'] Let $h({\bf x})\in C^{2}(\mathcal{D})$ be a strictly positive function, and such that 

\begin{equation}
\widehat{\cal L}^* h({\bf x})\equiv
\sum_{i=1}^n \widehat{b}_i({\bf x})\partial_{x_i}h({\bf x})
+{1\over 2}\sum_{i,j=1}^n  \widehat{a}_{ij}({\bf x})
\partial_{x_i,x_j}h({\bf x})=0, \qquad \boldsymbol{x} \in \mathcal{D.}

\end{equation}

Moreover, let us assume that the function
\begin{equation} 
    \Omega({\bf x}):=\frac{\nabla h({\bf x})\cdot  A({\bf x})}{h({\bf x})}, 
    \qquad {\bf x}\in \mathcal{D},
\end{equation}
possesses the property of global Lipschitz continuity. Hence, the time-homogeneous diffusion process ${\bf X}_t$, with infinitesimal moments 

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{ll}
	b_i({\bf x})=\widehat{b}_i({\bf x})
    +\displaystyle{1\over h({\bf x})}\sum_{j=1}^n \widehat{a}_{ij}({\bf x})
	\ \partial_{x_j}h({\bf x}) & (i=1,\ldots,n), 
    \\
	a_{ij}({\bf x})=  \widehat{a}_{ij}({\bf x})  & (i,j=1,\ldots,n),
\end{array}

\end{equation}

has the transition p.d.f.\ $f({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)$ given in ((2.1 of the paper)), 
for $\bf{x},\,\bf{y}\in  {\cal D}$ and $t>\tau\geq  0$, 
which satisfies the initial delta condition 

\begin{equation}
\lim_{t\downarrow\tau}f({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)=
\lim_{\tau\uparrow t}f({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)=\prod_{i=1}^n
\delta(x_i-y_i),

\end{equation}
and the Kolmogorov and Fokker--Planck equations  

\begin{equation}
{\partial_\tau}{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)+{\cal L} {f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)=0,

\qquad  
{\partial_t}{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)={\cal L}^* {f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau),


\end{equation}

where ${\cal L}$ is the infinitesimal generator  associated to $\bf{X}_t$ and ${\cal L}^*$ its adjoint operator.

