[Lemma lem:bernton41mod of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] Let $(x,y) \in \calX \times \calY$.
    Then, for any $\delta < I(x, y)$ (given in (equation eq:rate-function-candidate-theorem of the paper)), there exists $r > 0$ such that 

    \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta\big(B_{\calX \times \calY}((x,y), r)\big) \leq -\delta, 
    \end{equation}

    where $B_{\calX \times \calY}((x,y), r)$ denotes an open ball of radius $r$ around $(x, y)$ in $\calX \times \calY$.

