body:
[The 21 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let \( \phi\in\text{\rm SCL}(\T^n) \) and $H:\T^n\times\R^n\to\R$ be a Tonelli Hamiltonian. Then we have
\begin{align*}
	\reg(\phi,H) = \reg(\phi), \qquad
	\cut(\phi,H) = \cut(\phi).
\end{align*}
In other words,
\begin{align*}
	\reg(\phi,H)=\big\{x\in\T^n:\partial_P \phi(x)\neq\varnothing\big\},\qquad \cut(\phi,H)=\big\{x\in\T^n:\partial_P \phi(x)=\varnothing\big\}.
\end{align*}

