[Definition def:filling-state of arXiv:2602.21315, 'The Instability of all Backoff Protocols\thanks{For the purpose of Open Access, the author'] Fix $\lambda \in (0,1)$ and a send sequence $\overline{p}$ with $p_0=1$. Let $j$ be a positive integer.  We say a high-level state $\Psi$ is \emph{$j$-filling} if bin~$j$ is exposed and the following properties hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item $\textup{type}^\Psi = \textup{filling}$.
\item $j^\Psi = j$.
\item For all $k \in [j-1]$, $z_k^\Psi = \mu_k^{\overline{\gamma}}$.

\item  $\mathcal{S}^\Psi = \{\Upsilon_{j, \ge \widetilde{W}[j]} \setminus \Upsilon_{j, \ge j^2}\}
\cup \{\{k\}\colon k \in \Upsilon_{j, \ge j^\chi}\}$.


\end{itemize}

[Thm 5.1 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Under the above assumptions (A:A1 of the paper)-(A:A2 of the paper), the function $u(\cdot,\cdot)$ defined by (equation u of the paper) is continuous on $[0,T]\times {\mathbb R}^n$, and it is a viscosity solution of PDE (equation PDE' of the paper). Moreover, there exist two constants $q>0$ and $C>0$ depending only on $(p,\theta,T,K_1)$ such that
\begin{align}
\forall (t,x)\in [0,T]\times{\mathbb R}^n, \ \ |u(t,x)|\leq C(1+|x|^q).
\end{align}

