[Definition Def: p-th variation of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] For any $x \in C([0, 1])$ and $p \ge 1$, we denote 
    \begin{equation}    
    	[x]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}^n}(t) := \sum_{j \in I_n} \big \vert x(t^n_{j + 1} \wedge t) - x(t^n_j \wedge t)\big\vert^p, \qquad \forall \, t \in [0, 1],
    \end{equation}
    the \textit{$p$-th variation of $x$ along the $n$-th dyadic partition $\mathbb{T}^n$} for each $n \ge 0$. If the limit of $[x]_{\mathbb{T}^n}^{(p)}(t)$ as $n \to \infty$ exists and is continuous, then we say that \textit{$x$ admits finite $p$-th variation along the dyadic partition sequence $\mathbb{T}$}, and write its limit as
    \begin{equation}	
        [x]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}(t) := \lim_{n \to \infty} [x]_{\mathbb{T}^n}^{(p)}(t), \qquad \forall \, t \in [0, 1].
    \end{equation}
    In such case, the convergence is uniform in $t$ and the limit $t \mapsto [x]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}(t)$ is non-decreasing [perkowski2019]. We denote by $V^{p}_{\mathbb{T}}$ the space of such functions $x$ admitting finite $p$-th variation along $\mathbb{T}$.

[Thm entropicCommutator of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Fix an integer $n\ge1$. Assume $0\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$, $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$, and $v:{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}\to{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}$ is globally Lipschitz; if $\mathsf{s}=0$, assume in addition (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper).  Then there exist a threshold $\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}=\beta_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mu,v,n)>0$ and, for every $\beta>0$, constants $\varepsilon_{\beta,n}>0$ and $C_{\mathrm{em}}(\beta,\mu,v,n)<\infty$, made explicit in (rem:entropicCommutatorConstants of the paper), such that, for every $\sigma\in\{\pm 1\}$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}{\mathbb{E}}_{X_N\sim{\mathbb{Q}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)}\Big[e^{\sigma\varepsilon_{\beta,n} N\mathsf{A}_n(v,X_N,\mu)}\Big]\le C_{\mathrm{em}}(\beta,\mu,v,n).
\end{align}
Consequently, for every $f_N\in\mathcal{P}(({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})^N)$,
\begin{align}
\Big|{\mathbb{E}}_{X_N\sim f_N}\Big[N\mathsf{A}_n(v,X_N,\mu)\Big]\Big|\le C_{\beta,n,v}N\mathsf{E}_N(f_N,\mu)+C_{\beta,\mu,v,n},
\end{align}
where $\mathsf{E}_N$ is the modulated free energy (equation eq:ENdef of the paper) and
\begin{align}
C_{\beta,n,v}\coloneqq\frac{\beta}{\varepsilon_{\beta,n}}
\qquad\text{and}\qquad
C_{\beta,\mu,v,n}\coloneqq\frac{1}{\varepsilon_{\beta,n}}
\pa*{\log C_{\mathrm{pf}}(\beta,\mu)+\log C_{\mathrm{em}}(\beta,\mu,v,n)}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2511.11189, 'Sharp asymptotics for the maximal distance from the boundary to the nucleus of a typical P'] Let \(c\in\VO\) be a vertex of \(\CO\) determined by the points 0 and \(\m X_1,...,\m X_d\) of \(\Phi\), and let \(\Urm_0,...,\Urm_d \in\Sp_{\R^d}\), where \(\Sp_{\R^d}\) denotes the \((d-1)\)-dimensional unit sphere, be the unit vectors
		\begin{equation*}
			\Urm_0 = \frac{c}{\|c\|} \; , \; \Urm_i = \frac{\m X_i-c}{\|\m X_i-c\|}.
		\end{equation*}
		Then the vertex \(c\) is pointy if and only if
		\begin{equation*}
			0 \in \Conv\left(P_{\Urm_0^\perp}(\Urm_1),...,P_{\Urm_0^\perp}(\Urm_d)\right)
		\end{equation*}
		where by \(\Proj_{\m u^\perp}\) we denote the orthogonal projection onto \(\m u^\perp\), the \((d-1)\)-dimensional linear subspace orthogonal to \(u\in\Sp_{\R^d}\), see Figure \ref{fig_proj_refl}, and where \(\Conv\) denotes the relative interior of the convex hull of the specified points. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

