body:
[Lem special_classification of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Taut foliations on $S^1\times D^2$ and $\mathbb{T}^2\times I$ transverse to the boundary are classified as follows:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If $\mathcal{F}$ is a taut $C^0$-foliation on $S^1 \times D^2$ transverse to the boundary, then $\mathcal{F}$ is isotopic to the standard foliation by disks.

        \item If $\mathcal{F}$ is a taut $C^0$-foliation on $\mathbb{T}^2 \times I$ transverse to the boundary, then $\mathcal{F}$ is isotopic to a product of a foliation on $\mathbb{T}^2$ with $I$.
    \end{enumerate}

