Here, $ \Ct  > 0 $ is a constant.

[Prop 321-avoiding-permutons of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] The map $\Psi$ is a continuous surjective map from $\mathcal D$ to the set $\mathcal P_{\Av(321)}$ of $321$-avoiding permutons.
    Moreover, considering a $321$-avoiding permuton $\mu$ and its decomposition $\mu=\mu_{{\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=.4]
  \draw (0,0) -- (0.5,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
  \draw[thick,dotted] (0,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
\end{tikzpicture}}}+\mu_{{\, \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=.4]
  \draw (0,0) -- (0,0.5) -- (0.5,0.5);
  \draw[thick,dotted] (0,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
\end{tikzpicture}}}+\mu_{\diagup}$ as above, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \Psi^{-1}(\mu) = \big\{\proj(\mu_{{\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=.4]
  \draw (0,0) -- (0.5,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
  \draw[thick,dotted] (0,0) -- (0.5,0.5);
\end{tikzpicture}}} + \nu) : 0 \le \nu \le \mu_{\diagup} \big\} \,,
    \end{equation}
    where we recall that $\proj(\pi)$ is the pair of measures given by the projections of $\pi$ on the horizontal and vertical axes respectively.

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2607.11773, '2607.11773'] Suppose that {\bf(H1)}-{\bf(H4)}, \eqref{thetaassum2}, \eqref{dissip1} and \eqref{dissip2} hold.
   Then for every 
   $\tau \in \mathbb{R}$, $\delta > 0$ and $D = \{ D(t): t \in \mathbb{R} \} \in \mathcal{D}$,
   there exist constants $T = T(\tau, \delta, D) \ge 3\rho$ and $ m_1 = m_1(\tau, \delta) \ge 1$
   such that for all $t \ge T$ and $m \ge m_1$,
   the solution $u$ of \eqref{lmvlds-2} satisfies
   \begin{align*}
      \mathbb{E}
         \Big[ \sup_{s \in [\tau-\rho, \tau]}
                   \sum_{|i| \ge m}
                      |u_i(s; \tau-t, \varphi)|^2
         \Big]
      + \mathbb{E}
           \Big[ \int_{\tau-\rho}^{\tau}
                    \sum_{|i| \ge m} |u_i(s; \tau-t, \varphi)|^p ds
           \Big]
      < \delta,
   \end{align*}
   where $\varphi \in L^\theta(\Omega, \mathcal{F}_{\tau-t};D_{\rho})$ with law $\mathcal{L}_{\varphi} \in D(\tau-t)$.

