[Lemma 9 (Gamma ratios) of arXiv:2608.30304, '2608.30304'] Let $y>0$ and $0\le\sigma\le1$. Then
\begin{equation}
\Gamma(y+\sigma)\le y^\sigma\,\Gamma(y),
\qquad\text{and}\qquad
\Gamma(y-\sigma)\le\frac{y}{y-\sigma}\,y^{-\sigma}\Gamma(y)\ \ (y>\sigma).
\end{equation}
Consequently, if $y\ge y_0>\tfrac12$ and $-\tfrac12\le\tau\le1$, then
\begin{equation}
\frac{\Gamma(y+\tau)}{\Gamma(y)}\le\frac{y_0}{y_0-\tfrac12}\;y^{\tau}.
\end{equation}

