[Theorem T:Hm-gamma of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Suppose $N = Hd$ and $I$ is a compact interval in ${\mathbb R}^N$.
Then, a.s., $X(I)$ has finite Hausdorff measure with respect to the gauge function
\begin{align}
\phi(r) = r^d f(r) \log\log\log(1/r).
\end{align}
In particular, $X(I)$ has Lebesgue measure zero a.s. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:factorization_H_theta of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] The height $H\colon \mathbb{Z}^{n+\rho}\to\mathbb{R}_{>0}$ factors through
	\begin{equation*}
	\lVert \cdot \rVert\colon \mathbb{Z}^{n+\rho} \to \mathbb{Z}^{\mathcal{D}}_{\ge 0},\ \vec x \mapsto (\lVert x_d \rVert_\infty)_{d\in \mathcal{D}}
	\end{equation*}
	and the coprimality condition $\theta$, detecting (eq:coprimality-toric of the paper), factors through
	\begin{equation*}
		g\colon \mathbb{Z}^{n+\rho} \to \mathbb{Z}^{\mathcal{D}}_{>0},\ \vec x \mapsto (\gcd(\vec x_d))_{d\in \mathcal{D}}.
	\end{equation*}

[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.24675, 'Towards Liouville Quantum Gravity on fractals'] Let $|\gamma|<\sqrt{d_H/C_0}$. Then,
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_K\int_K\frac{1}{d(x,y)^{\gamma^2C}}d\mu(y)\,d\mu(x)<\infty.
	\end{equation*}

[Thm P loc dim of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Almost surely under $\hat{P}_{\bm{\rho}}$, for every $t \in (0,\infty)$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{r\downarrow0}
    \frac{\log\Pi_t(B(x,r))}{\log r}
    =
    d_{\mathrm{cp}},
    \qquad
    \Pi_t\text{-}\mathrm{a.e.}\ x.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thmInveHyperDeter of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $ x_0 \in S\setminus\partial S$ satisfy $\frac{\partial  \sigma(T/2,x_0)}{\partial\nu}<0$, and  $S$ satisfy the outer  paraboloid condition with

\begin{equation}
K <\frac{-\frac{ \partial
\sigma}{\partial\nu}(T/2,x_0)}{4(|\sigma|_{L^\infty(B_\rho(T/2,x_0))}+1)}.
\end{equation}

If $z \in   L_{{\mathbb{F}}}^2 (\Omega; C([0,T];H_{\rm loc}^1(G)))\cap L_{{\mathbb{F}}}^2 (\Omega; C^{1}([0,T];L^2_{\rm loc}(G))) $ is a solution to the equation     (system1 of the paper) satisfying that

\begin{equation}
z=\frac{\partial z}{\partial\nu} = 0 \quad\mbox{ on } (0,T)\times
S,\;\;{\mathbb{P}}\mbox{-}\hbox{\rm a.s.} ,
\end{equation}

then for the neighborhood ${\cal V}$ given in  (def1 of the paper) and some $\varepsilon\in (0,T/2)$,
it holds that

\begin{equation}
z = 0 \quad\mbox{ in } ({\cal V}\cap {\cal D}_{\rho}^+)\times
(\varepsilon,T-\varepsilon),\;\;{\mathbb{P}}\mbox{-}\hbox{\rm a.s.}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:lemma2 of arXiv:2411.12076, 'Explicit solutions of the SI and Bass models on sparse Erd\H{o}s-R\'enyi and regular netwo'] Consider the Bass/{\rm SI} model~{\rm ((eqs:Bass-SI-models-ME of the paper),(eqs:ER-network of the paper))} on $\lim_{M\to \infty} {\cal G}(M,\frac{\lambda}{M})$. Then
	\begin{equation}

		\overline{[S^\infty]}(t)=\sum_{d=0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}_{\rm deg}(d) \,

		\overline{[S^\infty_{B_{d}}]}(t),
	\end{equation}
	where $\mathbb{P}_{\rm deg}(d)$ is given by~(equation eq:pois of the paper).

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.01346, '2609.01346'] For all sufficiently small $\delta$ and $0<s<s_1(\delta)$,
\begin{equation}
 0<x_\delta(s)\leq x_\delta(s_\delta^+)\longrightarrow0,
 \qquad 0<r_\delta(s)\leq C(n,k).
\end{equation}

