body:
[Proposition 43 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W)$ and $\varphi \in L(W,\bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then we have
\begin{align}
(\varphi(Y),\varphi(Y)') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],\bar{W})
\end{align}
and the estimates
\begin{align}
\| \varphi(Y), \varphi(Y)' \|_{X,2\alpha} &\leq | \varphi | \, \| Y,Y' \|_{X,2\alpha},
\\  | \varphi(Y), \varphi(Y)' |_{X,2\alpha} &\leq | \varphi | \, | Y,Y' |_{X,2\alpha},
\\  \interleave \varphi(Y), \varphi(Y)' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} &\leq | \varphi | \, \interleave Y,Y' \interleave_{X,2\alpha}.
\end{align}

