body:
[Lemma lem:JordanLowerBound of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] Consider the Jordan ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_J$. 
    There exists positive constants $c$ and $\delta$ such that for all $n\ge1$, any  vertex $v\in [n]$, and any $S\in[1, \delta n/v]$, 

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P} \left( \widehat{\sigma}_{J}(v) \geq S v \right) \geq \frac{c}{S}.
    \end{equation}

