[Theorem 7 (Energy theorem for the \(b\)-adic cube cascade) of arXiv:2606.08703, '2606.08703'] Let \(b\ge2\), \(d\ge1\), and let \(W\) satisfy \eqref{eq:badic-KP}.  Let
\(\mu\) be the associated canonical \(b\)-adic Mandelbrot cascade on
\([0,1]^d\).  Then, almost surely on \(\{\mu\ne0\}\),
\begin{equation}
        \dimE(\mu)=\dimtwo(\mu)=D_E(W).
\end{equation}

