[Lemma le:beta-power-ratio-monotone of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $\beta\in[0,1)$. The function
\bas{
f:(0,\infty)\to(0,\infty),\qquad f(x)=\frac{1-\beta^x}{x}
}
is decreasing. In particular, for every $n\in{\mathbb N}$,
\bas{
\frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n}\ge \frac1n.
}

