[Lemma lem:beta-q of arXiv:2605.01444, 'From second moments to pairwise negative correlation: \\applications to minimal and unifor'] Define $q(\lambda)\coloneq 1-\theta(\lambda)$ for $\lambda>1$. Then for $\lambda>1$,
	\begin{equation}
	\beta(\lambda)=q(\lambda)-\frac{\lambda q(\lambda)^2}{2}\,.
	\end{equation}

[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F}=\{f\in B(\X):\Vert f\Vert_\infty\le1\}$. Then the following three statements are equivalent: 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item [(\runum{1})] There exists unique invariant probability measure $\mu$ for $\Phi$ such that $\forall\,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\X)$, 
        \begin{equation*}
            \lim\limits_{t\to\infty}\|P_t^*\nu-\mu\|_{TV}=0.
        \end{equation*}
			\item[(\runum{2})] $\Phi$ is uniformly eventually continuous with respect to $\mathfrak{F}$ on $\X$, and there exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_P} at $z$.
            \item[(\runum{3})] There exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ is uniformly eventually continuous with respect to $\mathfrak{F}$ at $z$ and satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_P} at $z$.
		\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Fejer of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $f:[0,1]\rightarrow \lbrack 0,1]$ be continuous, strictly
increasing, with a unique interior fixed point $p\in (0,1)$ and
single-crossing pattern 
\begin{equation}
f(x)>x\ \ (x<p),\qquad f(x)<x\ \ (x>p).  
\end{equation}
Then:

\begin{enumerate}
\item For every $x\in \lbrack 0,1]$ 
\begin{equation}
|f(x)-p|\leq |x-p|,  
\end{equation}

with strict inequality if $x\neq p$;

\item If $x,y$ lie on the same side of $p$ (both $\leq p$ or both $\geq p$),
then 
\begin{equation*}
|f(x)-f(y)|\leq |x-y|.
\end{equation*}
\end{enumerate}

