[Prop 39 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $\beta\geq 0$. Then, for every $x,y,z,t\in \mathbb Z^d$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\phi_{\beta}[x\connect{}y,z,t]\leq \langle \sigma_x\sigma_y\rangle_{\beta}\langle \sigma_z\sigma_t\rangle_{\beta}+\langle \sigma_x\sigma_z\rangle_{\beta}\langle \sigma_y\sigma_t\rangle_{\beta}+\langle \sigma_x\sigma_t\rangle_{\beta}\langle \sigma_y\sigma_z\rangle_{\beta}.
\end{equation}

