[Definition def:raw-prefix-postbin-arrays-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Let \(d\in\mathfrak D_\xi\), and set \(m=m_{\xi,d}\).  Define 
\[F^{\mathrm{pre}}_{\xi,d}
=
\sum_{\ell=0}^{m-1}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\ J\subset I}}
c_J(\xi,d,\ell)M_I(U_J-1).\]
For \(L>m\), define 
\[F^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,d,L}
=
\sum_{\ell=m}^{L-1}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\ J\subset I}}
c_J(\xi,d,\ell)M_I(U_J-1).\]
Whenever the limit exists, set \(F^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,d}=\lim_{L\to\infty}F^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,d,L}\).

