body:
[Theorem 6 (Sharp anisotropic Hermite root rate) of arXiv:2607.07712, 'Parameter-Space Heat Flow, Gaussian Density Ratios, and Sharp Hermite Truncation Rates'] Assume \(S=S^T\), \(I+S>0\), and
\[
0<\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}<1.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\limsup_{m\to\infty}
a_m(u,S)^{1/m}
=
\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}.

\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
\limsup_{m\to\infty}
\|\Pi_mK_{u,S}\|_{L^2(\gamma_d)}^{1/m}
=
\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}.

\end{equation}

Let
\[
R_M^{\mathrm{sp}}(u,S)
:=
K_{u,S}-\Pi_{\le M}K_{u,S}
=
\sum_{m=M+1}^\infty \Pi_mK_{u,S}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\limsup_{M\to\infty}
\|R_M^{\mathrm{sp}}(u,S)\|_{L^2(\gamma_d)}^{1/M}
=
\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}.

\end{equation}
In particular, for every
\[
\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}<\rho<1,
\]
there exists \(C=C(u,S,\rho)>0\) such that
\begin{equation}
\|R_M^{\mathrm{sp}}(u,S)\|_{L^2(\gamma_d)}
\le
C\rho^M,
\qquad M\ge0.

\end{equation}
The rate \(\|S\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{1/2}\) is optimal in the root-test sense.

