[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.03961, 'On the exponential sum over squarefree integers'] Let $H,K\ge1$, let $(b,r)=1$, and suppose that $\alpha=b/r+\beta$ with
$|\beta|\le r^{-2}$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \sum_{1\le h\le H}\min\left(K,\frac1{2\|\alpha h\|}\right)
  \ll\left(\frac{HK}r+H+K+r\right)\log 2r.
\end{equation}

[Lem lem-green-finite of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] For each $x,y\in \mathcal V\mathcal G$, we have
\begin{equation}  
G_{\mathcal A}(x,y)   < \infty .
\end{equation} 
Furthermore, for each fixed $y\in\mathcal V\mathcal G$, the function $x\mapsto G_{\mathcal A}(x,y)$ is discrete harmonic on $\mathcal V\mathcal G\setminus (\mathcal A \cup \{y\})$ and if $y\notin \mathcal A$, then
\begin{equation} 
 \sum_{x \sim y} \mathfrak c(y,x) \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( G_{\mathcal A}(x,y)  - G_{\mathcal A}(y,y) \aftergroup\egroup\originalright)   =  - \pi(y) .
\end{equation}

